<div id="S3.Thmthm10" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmthm10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 3.10</span></span><span id="S3.Thmthm10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmthm10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmthm10.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S3.Thmthm10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\mathcal{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>T</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\mathcal{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.Thmthm10.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{{\mathcal{P}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>T</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{{\mathcal{P}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> be flow categories over <math id="S3.Thmthm10.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.Thmthm10.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{P}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{P}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> respectively. A <span id="S3.Thmthm10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">flow bimodule</span> <math id="S3.Thmthm10.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="S3.Thmthm10.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\mathcal{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>T</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\mathcal{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.Thmthm10.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{{\mathcal{P}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>T</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{{\mathcal{P}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> consists of the following data.</p>
<ol id="S3.I5" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S3.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S3.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A compact <math id="S3.I5.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{A}}_{pp^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔸</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{A}}_{pp^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>-space <math id="S3.I5.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{pp^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{pp^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> (which could be empty) for all <math id="S3.I5.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\in{\mathcal{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in{\mathcal{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.I5.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\prime}\in{\mathcal{P}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\prime}\in{\mathcal{P}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S3.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="S3.I5.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;q</annotation></semantics></math>, a homeomorphism of stratified spaces</p>
