<p id="S3.I6.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.I6.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\mathcal{P}}_{pq_{1}}\times M_{q_{1}p^{\prime}}\rightarrow M_{pp^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\mathcal{P}}_{pq_{1}}\times M_{q_{1}p^{\prime}}\rightarrow M_{pp^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> is induced by the composition of the homeomorphism <math id="S3.I6.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\mathcal{P}}_{pq_{1}}\times M_{q_{1}p^{\prime}}\rightarrow\partial^{pq_{1}p^{\prime}}M_{pp^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\mathcal{P}}_{pq_{1}}\times M_{q_{1}p^{\prime}}\rightarrow\partial^{pq_{1}p^{\prime}}M_{pp^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the inclusion <math id="S3.I6.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{pq_{1}p^{\prime}}M_{pp^{\prime}}\hookrightarrow M_{pp^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↪</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{pq_{1}p^{\prime}}M_{pp^{\prime}}\hookrightarrow M_{pp^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> and so forth.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I6.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S3.I6.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I6.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Similarly, for <math id="S3.I6.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\in{\mathcal{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in{\mathcal{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.I6.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{2}^{\prime}&lt;q_{1}^{\prime}&lt;p^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>&lt;</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{2}^{\prime}&lt;q_{1}^{\prime}&lt;p^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S3.I6.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{P}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{P}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have a commutative diagram</p>
