<li id="S3.I6.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(4)</span> 
<div id="S3.I6.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I6.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="S3.I6.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;q</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S3.I6.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.I6.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{\prime}&lt;p^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{\prime}&lt;p^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S3.I6.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{P}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{P}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have a commutative diagram</p>
