<p id="S3.I6.i5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">such that for <math id="S3.I6.i5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{1},a_{2}\in\Pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1},a_{2}\in\Pi</annotation></semantics></math> the equation <math id="S3.I6.i5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi^{M}_{a_{1}\cdot a_{2}}=\phi^{M}_{a_{1}}\circ\phi^{M}_{a_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>M</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi^{M}_{a_{1}\cdot a_{2}}=\phi^{M}_{a_{1}}\circ\phi^{M}_{a_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> holds, and such that <math id="S3.I6.i5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi^{M}_{id}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi^{M}_{id}</annotation></semantics></math> is the identity map. Moreover, we require that the actions</p>
<table id="S3.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\mathcal{P}}_{pq_{1}}\times M_{q_{1}p^{\prime}}\rightarrow M_{pp^{\prime}},M_{pq_{1}^{\prime}}\times T^{{\mathcal{P}}^{\prime}}_{q_{1}^{\prime}p^{\prime}}\to M_{pp^{\prime}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\mathcal{P}}_{pq_{1}}\times M_{q_{1}p^{\prime}}\rightarrow M_{pp^{\prime}},M_{pq_{1}^{\prime}}\times T^{{\mathcal{P}}^{\prime}}_{q_{1}^{\prime}p^{\prime}}\to M_{pp^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.I6.i5.p1.3" class="ltx_p">are <math id="S3.I6.i5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The following statement is the analog of Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmthm8" title="Lemma 3.8. ‣ 3.2. Topological flow categories and bimodules ‣ 3. Abstract constructions of chain complexes and maps over the integers ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.8</span></a> for flow bimodules. The associativity conditions from Definition <a href="#S3.Thmthm10" title="Definition 3.10. ‣ 3.2.1. Flow bimodules ‣ 3.2. Topological flow categories and bimodules ‣ 3. Abstract constructions of chain complexes and maps over the integers ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.10</span></a> guarantees that the maps between the stratified spaces are well-defined.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmthm11" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmthm11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3.11</span></span><span id="S3.Thmthm11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmthm11.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmthm11.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmthm11.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose <math id="S3.Thmthm11.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{pp^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{pp^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> is nonempty. Given an element <math id="S3.Thmthm11.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\alpha=pq_{1}\cdots q_{k}q^{\prime}_{k^{\prime}}\cdots q^{\prime}_{1}p^{\prime}\in{\mathbb{A}}_{pp^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝔸</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=pq_{1}\cdots q_{k}q^{\prime}_{k^{\prime}}\cdots q^{\prime}_{1}p^{\prime}\in{\mathbb{A}}_{pp^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have a stratified homeomorphism</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vbox{\lx@xy@svg{\hbox{\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\kern 69.03488pt\hbox{\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\hbox{\vtop{\halign{\entry@#!@&amp;&amp;\entry@@#!@\cr&amp;\cr&amp;\crcr}}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern-69.03488pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.55554pt\hbox{$\textstyle{T^{\mathcal{P}}_{pq_{1}}\times\cdots\times M_{q_{k}q^{\prime}_{k^{\prime}}}\times\cdots\times T^{{\mathcal{P}}^{\prime}}_{q^{\prime}_{1}p^{\prime}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 93.03488pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise-23.99998pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\kern 93.03488pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.55554pt\hbox{$\textstyle{\partial^{\alpha}M_{pp^{\prime}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 112.6594pt\raise-26.48006pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\kern-67.69815pt\raise-33.86896pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.55554pt\hbox{$\textstyle{{\mathbb{A}}^{\mathcal{P}}_{pq_{1}}\times\cdots\times{\mathbb{A}}_{q_{k},q^{\prime}_{k^{\prime}}}\times\cdots\times{\mathbb{A}}^{{\mathcal{P}}^{\prime}}_{q^{\prime}_{1},p^{\prime}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}$}