<mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow></span></span></foreignObject> </g> </g> </svg> </mtext><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vbox{\lx@xy@svg{\hbox{\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\kern 69.03488pt\hbox{\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\hbox{\vtop{\halign{\entry@#!@&amp;&amp;\entry@@#!@\cr&amp;\cr&amp;\crcr}}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern-69.03488pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.55554pt\hbox{$\textstyle{T^{\mathcal{P}}_{pq_{1}}\times\cdots\times M_{q_{k}q^{\prime}_{k^{\prime}}}\times\cdots\times T^{{\mathcal{P}}^{\prime}}_{q^{\prime}_{1}p^{\prime}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 93.03488pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise-23.99998pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\kern 93.03488pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.55554pt\hbox{$\textstyle{\partial^{\alpha}M_{pp^{\prime}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 112.6594pt\raise-26.48006pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\kern-67.69815pt\raise-33.86896pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.55554pt\hbox{$\textstyle{{\mathbb{A}}^{\mathcal{P}}_{pq_{1}}\times\cdots\times{\mathbb{A}}_{q_{k},q^{\prime}_{k^{\prime}}}\times\cdots\times{\mathbb{A}}^{{\mathcal{P}}^{\prime}}_{q^{\prime}_{1},p^{\prime}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 75.56444pt\raise-27.71896pt\hbox{{}\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise-1.75pt\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\cong}$}}}\kern 3.0pt}}}}}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 94.68071pt\raise-33.86896pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\kern 94.68071pt\raise-33.86896pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.55554pt\hbox{$\textstyle{\partial^{\alpha}{\mathbb{A}}_{pp^{\prime}}}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces}}}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">As spelled out in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Abo22</a>, Section 8]</cite>, one can define “higher” homotopies between flow bimodules parametrized cubes <math id="S3.SS2.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="S3.SS2.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in{\mathbb{Z}}_{&gt;0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in{\mathbb{Z}}_{&gt;0}</annotation></semantics></math> and construct a cubically enriched category of flow bimodules. Such notions are useful for proving invariance of Floer homology/homotopy groups, but establishing such invariance is beyond the scope of this paper.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.3. </span>Outer-collaring</h3>

<div id="S3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In Floer theory one often needs to inductively construct structures (such as perturbations) on infinitely many moduli spaces. Each moduli space is an orbifold with corners in a suitable sense. One wishes to construct the structures such that near the boundary or corner they are of the product type. This requires various compatible collar structures near the boundary and corners. The existence of a compatible system of collar structures is difficult to construct directly. Instead, following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx18" title="" class="ltx_ref">FOOO20</a>, Chapter 17]</cite>, we take a short-cut by constructing the collars “outside.”</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We will first consider the outer-collaring construction for individual stratified spaces, flow categories, and bimodules. They are operated in the topological category. This discussion is not immediately used in this section. Later we will also discuss outer-collaring of stratified objects in the smooth category.</p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS3.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">3.3.1. </span>Outer-collaring of stratified spaces</h4>

<div id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first discuss the outer-collaring of a single moduli space which may appear in either a flow category or a bimodule. We consider the first case (flow category) and the second case is completely similar. Abbreviate <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{A}}_{pq}^{\mathcal{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝔸</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{A}}_{pq}^{\mathcal{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔸</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{A}}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies conditions of Setup <a href="#S3.Thmthm5" title="Setup 3.5. ‣ 3.2. Topological flow categories and bimodules ‣ 3. Abstract constructions of chain complexes and maps over the integers ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a> and <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p,q\in{\mathcal{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p,q\in{\mathcal{P}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> be an <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔸</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{A}}</annotation></semantics></math>-space whose strata are indexed by words <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\alpha=pr_{1}\cdots r_{l}q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=pr_{1}\cdots r_{l}q</annotation></semantics></math>. Choose <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and we will define a new <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔸</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{A}}</annotation></semantics></math>-space denoted by <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\boxplus r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">⊞</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\boxplus r}</annotation></semantics></math>. As a set,</p>
<table id="S3.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="X^{\boxplus r}=\left(\bigsqcup_{\alpha\in{\mathbb{A}}}\partial^{\alpha}X\times[-r,0]^{{\mathbb{F}}_{\alpha}}\right)/\sim," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">⊞</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">⨆</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝔸</mi></mrow></munder><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">/</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∼</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\boxplus r}=\left(\bigsqcup_{\alpha\in{\mathbb{A}}}\partial^{\alpha}X\times[-r,0]^{{\mathbb{F}}_{\alpha}}\right)/\sim,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{F}}_{\alpha}\subset{\mathbb{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><mi>𝔸</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{F}}_{\alpha}\subset{\mathbb{A}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the set of adjacent faces and where the equivalence relation <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∼</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim</annotation></semantics></math> is generated by the following relation: if <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\leq\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\leq\beta</annotation></semantics></math> (which implies the inclusion of the sets of adjacent faces <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{F}}_{\beta}\subset{\mathbb{F}}_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{F}}_{\beta}\subset{\mathbb{F}}_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>), we identify</p>
<table id="S3.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,(t_{i})_{i\in{\mathbb{F}}_{\beta}})\in\partial^{\beta}X\times[-r,0]^{{\mathbb{F}}_{\beta}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>β</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>β</mi></msup><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>β</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,(t_{i})_{i\in{\mathbb{F}}_{\beta}})\in\partial^{\beta}X\times[-r,0]^{{\mathbb{F}}_{\beta}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">with</p>
<table id="S3.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(y,(s_{j})_{j\in{\mathbb{F}}_{\alpha}})\in\partial^{\alpha}X\times[-r,0]^{{\mathbb{F}}_{\alpha}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(y,(s_{j})_{j\in{\mathbb{F}}_{\alpha}})\in\partial^{\alpha}X\times[-r,0]^{{\mathbb{F}}_{\alpha}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">if <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=y\in\partial^{\alpha}X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><mi>X</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=y\in\partial^{\alpha}X</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{j}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{j}=0</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\notin{\mathbb{F}}_{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>β</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\notin{\mathbb{F}}_{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{j}=s_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{j}=s_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in{\mathbb{F}}_{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>β</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in{\mathbb{F}}_{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>. We call <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\boxplus r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">⊞</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\boxplus r}</annotation></semantics></math> the <span id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">outer collaring</span> of <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> of width <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> (see Figure <a href="#S3.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ 3.3.1. Outer-collaring of stratified spaces ‣ 3.3. Outer-collaring ‣ 3. Abstract constructions of chain complexes and maps over the integers ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.F1" class="ltx_figure ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S3.F1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="175.24" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 190.36 175.24" width="190.36"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,175.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(79.57,0) translate(0,79.57)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 34.46 36.06)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.87em;--ltx-fo-height:0.58em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:8.19pt;" height="6.62" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.62)" width="9.83"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.F1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.700em">X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -11.69 82.17)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.06em;--ltx-fo-height:0.78em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:8.19pt;" height="8.88" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.88)" width="23.38"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.F1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{\beta_{2}}X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo mathsize="0.700em">∂</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">β</mi><mn mathsize="0.700em">2</mn></msub></msup><mi mathsize="0.700em">X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{\beta_{2}}X</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 82.8 -6.41)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.06em;--ltx-fo-height:0.78em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:8.19pt;" height="8.88" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.88)" width="23.38"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.F1.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{\beta_{1}}X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo mathsize="0.700em">∂</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">β</mi><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn></msub></msup><mi mathsize="0.700em">X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{\beta_{1}}X</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 78.74 L 0 0 L 78.74 0"></path><g stroke-width="1.2pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -78.74 78.74 L -78.74 -78.74 L 78.74 -78.74"></path></g><g stroke-dasharray="0.4pt,2.0pt" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -78.74 0 L 0 0 L 0 -78.74"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -72.58 -42.43)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:5.86em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.21em;font-size:8.19pt;" height="10.97" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.55)" width="66.43"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.F1.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{\alpha}X\times[-r,0]^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mo mathsize="0.700em">∂</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">α</mi></msup><mi mathsize="0.700em">X</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em">−</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">r</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">0</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">]</mo></mrow><mn mathsize="0.700em">2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{\alpha}X\times[-r,0]^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 6.89 -42.6)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:5.73em;--ltx-fo-height:0.78em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.21em;font-size:8.19pt;" height="11.31" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.88)" width="64.96"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.F1.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{\beta_{1}}X\times[-r,0]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mo mathsize="0.700em">∂</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">β</mi><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn></msub></msup><mi mathsize="0.700em">X</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em">−</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">r</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">0</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{\beta_{1}}X\times[-r,0]</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -71.85 36.14)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:5.73em;--ltx-fo-height:0.78em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.21em;font-size:8.19pt;" height="11.31" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.88)" width="64.96"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.F1.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{\beta_{2}}X\times[-r,0]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mo mathsize="0.700em">∂</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">β</mi><mn mathsize="0.700em">2</mn></msub></msup><mi mathsize="0.700em">X</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em">−</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">r</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">0</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{\beta_{2}}X\times[-r,0]</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 1. </span>The local picture of an outer collaring of a prestratified space for <math id="S3.F1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&lt;\beta_{1},\beta_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&lt;\beta_{1},\beta_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">One has a natural identification <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=X^{\boxplus 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">⊞</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=X^{\boxplus 0}</annotation></semantics></math> and the natural inclusion <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\boxplus r}\hookrightarrow X^{\boxplus r^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">⊞</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">↪</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">⊞</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\boxplus r}\hookrightarrow X^{\boxplus r^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\leq r^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\leq r^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\boxplus r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">⊞</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\boxplus r}</annotation></semantics></math> has a structure of an <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔸</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{A}}</annotation></semantics></math>-space as follows. For each <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\in{\mathbb{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝔸</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\in{\mathbb{A}}</annotation></semantics></math>, define the boundary stratum</p>
<table id="S3.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\partial^{\beta}X^{\boxplus r}=\bigcup_{\alpha\leq\beta}\Big(\partial^{\alpha}X\times\{(t_{j})_{j\in{\mathbb{F}}_{\alpha}}\ |\ t_{j}=-r\ \forall j\in{\mathbb{F}}_{\beta}\}\Big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>β</mi></msup><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">⊞</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">⋃</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><msup><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.667em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.667em" rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{\beta}X^{\boxplus r}=\bigcup_{\alpha\leq\beta}\Big(\partial^{\alpha}X\times\{(t_{j})_{j\in{\mathbb{F}}_{\alpha}}\ |\ t_{j}=-r\ \forall j\in{\mathbb{F}}_{\beta}\}\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Then the corresponding stratum for <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\in{\mathbb{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝔸</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\in{\mathbb{A}}</annotation></semantics></math> is given by</p>
<table id="S3.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{\beta}^{\boxplus r}=\partial^{\beta}X^{\boxplus r}\setminus\bigcup_{\alpha&lt;\beta}\partial^{\alpha}X^{\boxplus r}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">⊞</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>β</mi></msup><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">⊞</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">∖</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">⋃</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">⊞</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{\beta}^{\boxplus r}=\partial^{\beta}X^{\boxplus r}\setminus\bigcup_{\alpha&lt;\beta}\partial^{\alpha}X^{\boxplus r}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">It is easy to see that the induced map <math id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\boxplus r}\to{\mathbb{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">⊞</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>𝔸</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\boxplus r}\to{\mathbb{A}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a stratification.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The following lemma shows that the outer-collaring construction respects products.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmthm12" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmthm12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3.12</span></span><span id="S3.Thmthm12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmthm12.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S3.I7" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S3.I7.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S3.I7.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I7.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I7.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any </span><math id="S3.I7.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in{\mathbb{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝔸</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in{\mathbb{A}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I7.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, we have </span><math id="S3.I7.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\partial^{\alpha}X)^{{\boxplus r}}=\partial^{\alpha}X^{\boxplus r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">⊞</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">⊞</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\partial^{\alpha}X)^{{\boxplus r}}=\partial^{\alpha}X^{\boxplus r}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I7.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> as </span><math id="S3.I7.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{\alpha}{\mathbb{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><mi>𝔸</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{\alpha}{\mathbb{A}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I7.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-spaces.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I7.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S3.I7.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I7.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I7.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If </span><math id="S3.I7.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I7.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> are </span><math id="S3.I7.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{A}}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔸</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{A}}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I7.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-spaces for </span><math id="S3.I7.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,2</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I7.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, then </span><math id="S3.I7.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1}^{\boxplus r}\times X_{2}^{\boxplus r}=(X_{1}\times X_{2})^{{\boxplus r}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo rspace="0em">⊞</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo rspace="0em">⊞</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">⊞</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1}^{\boxplus r}\times X_{2}^{\boxplus r}=(X_{1}\times X_{2})^{{\boxplus r}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I7.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> as </span><math id="S3.I7.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{A}}_{1}\times{\mathbb{A}}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔸</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>𝔸</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{A}}_{1}\times{\mathbb{A}}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I7.i2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-spaces.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.SSS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.SSS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">These statements are true by inspecting the definition.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmthm13" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmthm13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3.13</span></span><span id="S3.Thmthm13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmthm13.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmthm13.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmthm13.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Given a stratified map</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lx@xy@svg{\hbox{\raise 2.55554pt\hbox{\kern 9.77777pt\hbox{\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\hbox{\vtop{\halign{\entry@#!@&amp;&amp;\entry@@#!@\cr&amp;\cr&amp;\crcr}}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern-9.77777pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.55554pt\hbox{$\textstyle{X_{1}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 16.43573pt\raise 6.1111pt\hbox{{}\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise-1.75pt\hbox{$\scriptstyle{f}$}}}\kern 3.0pt}}}}}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 33.77777pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise-24.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\kern 33.77777pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.55554pt\hbox{$\textstyle{X_{2}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 43.55554pt\raise-24.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\kern-8.99307pt\raise-31.27777pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.55554pt\hbox{$\textstyle{{\mathbb{A}}_{1}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{\hbox{