</div></li>
<li id="S3.I16.ix3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(C)</span> 
<div id="S3.I16.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I16.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each <math id="S3.I16.ix3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p,p^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p,p^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and all <math id="S3.I16.ix3.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\alpha=pr_{1}\cdots r_{l}r_{l}^{\prime}\cdots r_{1}^{\prime}p^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=pr_{1}\cdots r_{l}r_{l}^{\prime}\cdots r_{1}^{\prime}p^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, define</p>
<table id="S3.Ex75" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex75.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="C_{\alpha}^{M}=C^{\mathcal{P}}_{pr_{1}}\times\cdots\times C^{M}_{r_{l}r_{l}^{\prime}}\times\cdots\times C^{{\mathcal{P}}^{\prime}}_{r_{1}^{\prime}p^{\prime}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>α</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>M</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>C</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.055em">⋯</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>C</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>M</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.055em">⋯</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>C</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\alpha}^{M}=C^{\mathcal{P}}_{pr_{1}}\times\cdots\times C^{M}_{r_{l}r_{l}^{\prime}}\times\cdots\times C^{{\mathcal{P}}^{\prime}}_{r_{1}^{\prime}p^{\prime}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.I16.ix3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">As in Definition <a href="#S3.Thmthm24" title="Definition 3.24. ‣ 3.4.4. Derived orbifold lifts of flow categories and bimodules ‣ 3.4. Derived orbifold charts with stratifications ‣ 3. Abstract constructions of chain complexes and maps over the integers ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.24</span></a>, for each pair <math id="S3.I16.ix3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\leq\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\leq\beta</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S3.I16.ix3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{A}}_{pp^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔸</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{A}}_{pp^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>, there is a well-defined chart embedding</p>
<table id="S3.Ex76" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\iota}}_{\beta\alpha}^{M}:C_{\alpha}^{M}\hookrightarrow C_{\beta}^{M}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜾</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>α</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">↪</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>β</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\iota}}_{\beta\alpha}^{M}:C_{\alpha}^{M}\hookrightarrow C_{\beta}^{M}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.I16.ix3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">It is required that the derived orbifold presentations <math id="S3.I16.ix3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{C_{\alpha}^{M}\}_{\alpha\in{\mathbb{A}}_{pp^{\prime}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>α</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝔸</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{C_{\alpha}^{M}\}_{\alpha\in{\mathbb{A}}_{pp^{\prime}}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the collection of chart embeddings <math id="S3.I16.ix3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{{\bm{\iota}}_{\beta\alpha}\}_{\alpha\leq\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝜾</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{{\bm{\iota}}_{\beta\alpha}\}_{\alpha\leq\beta}</annotation></semantics></math> constitute a system of derived orbifold presentations of <math id="S3.I16.ix3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{pp^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{pp^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I16.ix4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(D)</span> 
<div id="S3.I16.ix4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I16.ix4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The strict <math id="S3.I16.ix4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariance condition: for any <math id="S3.I16.ix4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in\Pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in\Pi</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.I16.ix4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{pp^{\prime}}\neq\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>≠</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{pp^{\prime}}\neq\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>, there is an isomorphism between derived orbifold charts <math id="S3.I16.ix4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\phi}^{M}_{a}:C^{M}_{pp^{\prime}}\to C^{M}_{a\cdot p\ a\cdot p^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>a</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.410em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\phi}^{M}_{a}:C^{M}_{pp^{\prime}}\to C^{M}_{a\cdot p\ a\cdot p^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying <math id="S3.I16.ix4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\phi}^{M}_{a_{1}\cdot a_{2}}=\tilde{\phi}^{M}_{a_{1}}\circ\tilde{\phi}^{M}_{a_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>M</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\phi}^{M}_{a_{1}\cdot a_{2}}=\tilde{\phi}^{M}_{a_{1}}\circ\tilde{\phi}^{M}_{a_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.I16.ix4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\phi}^{M}_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>a</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\phi}^{M}_{a}</annotation></semantics></math> restricts to the map <math id="S3.I16.ix4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi^{M}_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi^{M}_{a}</annotation></semantics></math> from Definition <a href="#S3.Thmthm10" title="Definition 3.10. ‣ 3.2.1. Flow bimodules ‣ 3.2. Topological flow categories and bimodules ‣ 3. Abstract constructions of chain complexes and maps over the integers ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.10</span></a> along the zero locus <math id="S3.I16.ix4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathcal{S}}^{M}_{pp^{\prime}})^{-1}(0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathcal{S}}^{M}_{pp^{\prime}})^{-1}(0)</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, <math id="S3.I16.ix4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\phi}^{M}_{id}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\phi}^{M}_{id}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S3.I16.ix4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=id\in\Pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=id\in\Pi</annotation></semantics></math> is the identity map. Moreover, the left and right actions of the charts from <math id="S3.I16.ix4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\mathcal{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>T</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\mathcal{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.I16.ix4.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\mathcal{P}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>T</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\mathcal{P}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> on the charts of <math id="S3.I16.ix4.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> should be <math id="S3.I16.ix4.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.5. </span>Additional structures</h3>

<div id="S3.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In order to construct a coherent system of FOP perturbations, we need more structures on the derived orbifold lifts. They are the <span id="S3.SS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">collar structure</span>, <span id="S3.SS5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">scaffolding</span>, and <span id="S3.SS5.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">straightening</span>.</p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS5.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">3.5.1. </span>Collar structure</h4>

<div id="S3.Thmthm26" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmthm26.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 3.26</span></span><span id="S3.Thmthm26.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmthm26.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S3.I17" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S3.I17.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S3.I17.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I17.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A <span id="S3.I17.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">collar structure</span> on an <math id="S3.I17.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔸</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{A}}</annotation></semantics></math>-stratified derived orbifold chart <math id="S3.I17.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathcal{U}},{\mathcal{E}},{\mathcal{S}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathcal{U}},{\mathcal{E}},{\mathcal{S}})</annotation></semantics></math> is a collection of open chart embeddings</p>
<table id="S3.Ex77" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vbox{\lx@xy@svg{\hbox{\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\kern 36.10985pt\hbox{\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\hbox{\vtop{\halign{\entry@#!@&amp;&amp;\entry@@#!@\cr&amp;&amp;\cr&amp;&amp;\crcr}}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern-36.10985pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{{\mathcal{E}}|_{\partial^{\alpha}{\mathcal{U}}}\times[0,\epsilon)^{{\mathbb{F}}_{\alpha}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise-24.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 48.95694pt\raise 7.36111pt\hbox{{}\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise-2.86111pt\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\widehat{\theta}_{\alpha}^{\rm collar}}$}}}\kern 3.0pt}}}}}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 90.45706pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\kern 60.10985pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{}$}}}}}}}{\hbox{\kern 90.45706pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{{\mathcal{E}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 96.85985pt\raise-25.57895pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\kern-32.70213pt\raise-32.91226pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{\partial^{\alpha}{\mathcal{U}}\times[0,\epsilon)^{{\mathbb{F}}_{\alpha}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 47.95277pt\raise-39.65727pt\hbox{{}\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise-2.74501pt\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\theta_{\alpha}^{\rm collar}}$}}}\kern 3.0pt}}}}}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 90.10985pt\raise-32.91226pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\kern 60.10985pt\raise-32.91226pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{}$}}}}}}}{\hbox{\kern 90.10985pt\raise-32.91226pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{{\mathcal{U}}}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces}}}}}\ \ \forall\alpha\in{\mathbb{A}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext> <svg style="vertical-align:-64.2068392345977px" height="84.58" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="49.97 64.21 193.33 84.58" width="193.33"> <g transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 49.96519720833117 84.57798771101426) translate(49.97,0)"> <g transform="translate(-49.97,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"> <foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:6.62em;--ltx-fo-height:0.84em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="15.1" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.64)" width="91.63"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><msub><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="fal