<p id="S3.I17.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">for all <math id="S3.I17.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&lt;\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&lt;\beta</annotation></semantics></math> which satisfy conditions in item (1) above. We require the following condition is satisfied. For each triple <math id="S3.I17.i2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&lt;\beta&lt;\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&lt;\beta&lt;\gamma</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="S3.Ex82" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\iota}_{\gamma\beta}\Big(\widehat{\theta}_{\beta\alpha}^{\rm collar}(v_{\beta},t_{\beta\alpha})\Big)=\widehat{\theta}_{\gamma\alpha}^{\rm collar}\Big(\widehat{\iota}_{\gamma\beta}(v_{\beta}),t_{\beta\alpha},0_{\gamma\beta}\Big)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ι</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mi>collar</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mi>collar</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ι</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\iota}_{\gamma\beta}\Big(\widehat{\theta}_{\beta\alpha}^{\rm collar}(v_{\beta},t_{\beta\alpha})\Big)=\widehat{\theta}_{\gamma\alpha}^{\rm collar}\Big(\widehat{\iota}_{\gamma\beta}(v_{\beta}),t_{\beta\alpha},0_{\gamma\beta}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.I17.i2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">for all <math id="S3.I17.i2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{\beta}\in{\mathcal{E}}_{\beta}|_{\partial^{\alpha}{\mathcal{U}}_{\beta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>β</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{\beta}\in{\mathcal{E}}_{\beta}|_{\partial^{\alpha}{\mathcal{U}}_{\beta}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.I17.i2.p1.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="t_{\beta\alpha}\in[0,\epsilon)^{{\mathbb{F}}_{\alpha}\setminus{\mathbb{F}}_{\beta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>β</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\beta\alpha}\in[0,\epsilon)^{{\mathbb{F}}_{\alpha}\setminus{\mathbb{F}}_{\beta}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Here <math id="S3.I17.i2.p1.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="0_{\gamma\beta}=(0,\ldots,0)\in[0,\epsilon)^{{\mathbb{F}}_{\beta}\setminus{\mathbb{F}}_{\gamma}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0_{\gamma\beta}=(0,\ldots,0)\in[0,\epsilon)^{{\mathbb{F}}_{\beta}\setminus{\mathbb{F}}_{\gamma}}</annotation></semantics></math> and hence <math id="S3.I17.i2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(t_{\beta\alpha},0_{\gamma\beta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(t_{\beta\alpha},0_{\gamma\beta})</annotation></semantics></math> is regarded as a point of <math id="S3.I17.i2.p1.m13" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[0,\epsilon)^{{\mathbb{F}}_{\alpha}\setminus{\mathbb{F}}_{\gamma}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,\epsilon)^{{\mathbb{F}}_{\alpha}\setminus{\mathbb{F}}_{\gamma}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I17.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S3.I17.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I17.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A collar structure on a derived orbifold lift of a flow category (using the same notations as in Definition <a href="#S3.Thmthm24" title="Definition 3.24. ‣ 3.4.4. Derived orbifold lifts of flow categories and bimodules ‣ 3.4. Derived orbifold charts with stratifications ‣ 3. Abstract constructions of chain complexes and maps over the integers ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.24</span></a>), is a collection of collar structures on the chart <math id="S3.I17.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> such that the following is satisfied.</p>
<ol id="S3.I17.i3.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S3.I17.i3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(a)</span> 
<div id="S3.I17.i3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I17.i3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each <math id="S3.I17.i3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\alpha=pr_{1}\cdots r_{l}q\in{\mathbb{A}}_{pq}^{\mathcal{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝔸</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=pr_{1}\cdots r_{l}q\in{\mathbb{A}}_{pq}^{\mathcal{P}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the collar structures on <math id="S3.I17.i3.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{pr_{1}},\ldots,C_{r_{l}q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{pr_{1}},\ldots,C_{r_{l}q}</annotation></semantics></math> define a product collar structure on the product chart <math id="S3.I17.i3.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then the collection of collar structures on <math id="S3.I17.i3.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> is a collar structure on the derived orbifold presentation of <math id="S3.I17.i3.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> as defined in above item (2).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I17.i3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(b)</span> 
<div id="S3.I17.i3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I17.i3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The collar structure is strictly <math id="S3.I17.i3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I17.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(4)</span> 
<div id="S3.I17.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I17.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Suppose <math id="S3.I17.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathfrak{D}}_{{\mathcal{P}}{\mathcal{P}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔇</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathfrak{D}}_{{\mathcal{P}}{\mathcal{P}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a derived orbifold lift of a flow bimodule <math id="S3.I17.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="S3.I17.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\mathcal{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>T</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\mathcal{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.I17.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{{\mathcal{P}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>T</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{{\mathcal{P}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> which extends <math id="S3.I17.i4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathfrak{D}}^{\mathcal{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔇</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathfrak{D}}^{\mathcal{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.I17.i4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathfrak{D}}^{{\mathcal{P}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔇</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathfrak{D}}^{{\mathcal{P}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Suppose <math id="S3.I17.i4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathfrak{D}}^{\mathcal{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔇</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathfrak{D}}^{\mathcal{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.I17.i4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathfrak{D}}^{{\mathcal{P}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔇</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathfrak{D}}^{{\mathcal{P}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> are equipped with collar structures. Then a collar structure on <math id="S3.I17.i4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathfrak{D}}_{{\mathcal{P}}{\mathcal{P}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔇</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathfrak{D}}_{{\mathcal{P}}{\mathcal{P}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> which extends the collar structure on <math id="S3.I17.i4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathfrak{D}}^{\mathcal{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔇</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathfrak{D}}^{\mathcal{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.I17.i4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathfrak{D}}^{{\mathcal{P}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔇</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathfrak{D}}^{{\mathcal{P}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a collection of collar structures on all the derived orbifold charts <math id="S3.I17.i4.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathcal{U}}_{pp^{\prime}}^{M},{\mathcal{E}}_{pp^{\prime}}^{M},{\mathcal{S}}_{pp^{\prime}}^{M},\psi_{pp^{\prime}}^{M})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathcal{U}}_{pp^{\prime}}^{M},{\mathcal{E}}_{pp^{\prime}}^{M},{\mathcal{S}}_{pp^{\prime}}^{M},\psi_{pp^{\prime}}^{M})</annotation></semantics></math> of the form</p>
