<p id="S3.I19.ix4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Here the “<math id="S3.I19.ix4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=</annotation></semantics></math>” arrow is induced from the identity <math id="S3.I19.ix4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}_{\gamma\alpha}={\mathcal{F}}_{\gamma\beta}|_{{\mathcal{U}}_{\alpha}}\oplus{\mathcal{F}}_{\beta\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}_{\gamma\alpha}={\mathcal{F}}_{\gamma\beta}|_{{\mathcal{U}}_{\alpha}}\oplus{\mathcal{F}}_{\beta\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS5.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS5.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Now consider a derived orbifold lift of a flow category.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmthm29" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmthm29.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 3.29</span></span><span id="S3.Thmthm29.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmthm29.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmthm29.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A <span id="S3.Thmthm29.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">scaffolding</span> of a derived orbifold lift of a flow category <math id="S3.Thmthm29.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\mathcal{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>T</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\mathcal{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> consists of a collection of scaffoldings for the induced system of derived orbifold chart presentations of <math id="S3.Thmthm29.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="S3.Ex89" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex89.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Big(\big({\mathcal{F}}_{\beta\alpha},{\bm{\theta}}_{\beta\alpha}\big)_{\alpha\leq\beta}\Big)_{p&lt;q}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Big(\big({\mathcal{F}}_{\beta\alpha},{\bm{\theta}}_{\beta\alpha}\big)_{\alpha\leq\beta}\Big)_{p&lt;q}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmthm29.p1.2" class="ltx_p">satisfying</p>
<ol id="S3.I20" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S3.I20.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S3.I20.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I20.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Suppose <math id="S3.I20.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="pr_{1}\cdots r_{l}q=\alpha\leq\beta=ps_{1}\cdots s_{m}q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">pr_{1}\cdots r_{l}q=\alpha\leq\beta=ps_{1}\cdots s_{m}q</annotation></semantics></math>. Denote <math id="S3.I20.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\alpha_{0}=pr_{1}\cdots s_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{0}=pr_{1}\cdots s_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.I20.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ldots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ldots</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.I20.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\alpha_{m}=s_{m}\cdots r_{l}q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{m}=s_{m}\cdots r_{l}q</annotation></semantics></math>. Then as subbundles of <math id="S3.I20.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{E}}_{\beta}|_{{\mathcal{U}}_{\alpha}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{E}}_{\beta}|_{{\mathcal{U}}_{\alpha}}</annotation></semantics></math>, in view of the identification <math id="S3.I20.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathcal{U}}_{\alpha}={\mathcal{U}}_{\alpha_{0}}\times\cdots\times{\mathcal{U}}_{\alpha_{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.055em">⋯</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{U}}_{\alpha}={\mathcal{U}}_{\alpha_{0}}\times\cdots\times{\mathcal{U}}_{\alpha_{m}}</annotation></semantics></math>, one has</p>
<table id="S3.Ex90" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex90.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}_{\beta\alpha}={\mathcal{F}}_{ps_{1},\alpha_{0}}\boxplus\cdots\boxplus{\mathcal{F}}_{s_{m}q,\alpha_{m}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo>⊞</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>⊞</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}_{\beta\alpha}={\mathcal{F}}_{ps_{1},\alpha_{0}}\boxplus\cdots\boxplus{\mathcal{F}}_{s_{m}q,\alpha_{m}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I20.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S3.I20.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I20.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">With respect to the last identity, one has (as germs of maps)</p>
<table id="S3.Ex91" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex91.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\bm{\theta}}_{\beta\alpha}={\bm{\theta}}_{ps_{1},\alpha_{0}}\times\cdots\times{\bm{\theta}}_{s_{m}q,\alpha_{m}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝜽</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.055em">⋯</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\theta}}_{\beta\alpha}={\bm{\theta}}_{ps_{1},\alpha_{0}}\times\cdots\times{\bm{\theta}}_{s_{m}q,\alpha_{m}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmthm30" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmthm30.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 3.30</span></span><span id="S3.Thmthm30.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmthm30.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmthm30.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given two flow categories <math id="S3.Thmthm30.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\mathcal{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>T</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\mathcal{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.Thmthm30.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{{\mathcal{P}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>T</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{{\mathcal{P}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> endowed with derived orbifold lifts <math id="S3.Thmthm30.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathfrak{D}}^{\mathcal{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔇</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathfrak{D}}^{\mathcal{P}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.Thmthm30.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathfrak{D}}^{{\mathcal{P}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔇</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathfrak{D}}^{{\mathcal{P}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> respectively, let <math id="S3.Thmthm30.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> be a flow bimodule from <math id="S3.Thmthm30.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\mathcal{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>T</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\mathcal{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.Thmthm30.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{{\mathcal{P}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>T</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{{\mathcal{P}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> endowed with a compatible derived orbifold lift <math id="S3.Thmthm30.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathfrak{D}}^{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔇</mi><mi>M</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathfrak{D}}^{M}</annotation></semantics></math>. Suppose <math id="S3.Thmthm30.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathfrak{D}}^{\mathcal{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔇</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathfrak{D}}^{\mathcal{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.Thmthm30.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathfrak{D}}^{{\mathcal{P}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔇</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathfrak{D}}^{{\mathcal{P}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> come with scaffoldings</p>
<table id="S3.Ex92" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex92.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\big(\big\{{\mathcal{F}}^{\mathcal{P}}_{\beta\alpha},{\bm{\theta}}^{\mathcal{P}}_{\beta\alpha}\big\}_{\alpha\leq\beta}\big)_{p&lt;q},\text{ }\big(\big\{{\mathcal{F}}^{{\mathcal{P}}^{\prime}}_{\beta^{\prime}\alpha^{\prime}},{\bm{\theta}}^{{\mathcal{P}}^{\prime}}_{\beta^{\prime}\alpha^{\prime}}\big\}_{\alpha^{\prime}\leq\beta^{\prime}}\big)_{p^{\prime}&lt;q^{\prime}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mtext> </mtext><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big(\big\{{\mathcal{F}}^{\mathcal{P}}_{\beta\alpha},{\bm{\theta}}^{\mathcal{P}}_{\beta\alpha}\big\}_{\alpha\leq\beta}\big)_{p&lt;q},\text{ }\big(\big\{{\mathcal{F}}^{{\mathcal{P}}^{\prime}}_{\beta^{\prime}\alpha^{\prime}},{\bm{\theta}}^{{\mathcal{P}}^{\prime}}_{\beta^{\prime}\alpha^{\prime}}\big\}_{\alpha^{\prime}\leq\beta^{\prime}}\big)_{p^{\prime}&lt;q^{\prime}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmthm30.p1.2" class="ltx_p">A <span id="S3.Thmthm30.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">scaffolding</span> of such a derived orbifold lift <span id="S3.Thmthm30.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">compatible with</span> the given scaffoldings is given by a collection of scaffoldings for the induced system of derived orbifold chart presentations</p>
<table id="S3.Ex93" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex93.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big(\big\{{\mathcal{F}}_{\tilde{\beta}\tilde{\alpha}},{\bm{\theta}}_{\tilde{\beta}\tilde{\alpha}}\big\}_{\tilde{\alpha}\leq\tilde{\beta}}\big)_{\tilde{\alpha},\tilde{\beta}\in{\mathbb{A}}_{pp^{\prime}}^{M}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>≤</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>𝔸</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big(\big\{{\mathcal{F}}_{\tilde{\beta}\tilde{\alpha}},{\bm{\theta}}_{\tilde{\beta}\tilde{\alpha}}\big\}_{\tilde{\alpha}\leq\tilde{\beta}}\big)_{\tilde{\alpha},\tilde{\beta}\in{\mathbb{A}}_{pp^{\prime}}^{M}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmthm30.p1.3" class="ltx_p">satisfying similar conditions as in Definition <a href="#S3.Thmthm29" title="Definition 3.29. ‣ 3.5.2. Scaffolding ‣ 3.5. Additional structures ‣ 3. Abstract constructions of chain complexes and maps over the integers ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.29</span></a> using the factorization of the boundary strata (see Definition <a href="#S3.Thmthm25" title="Definition 3.25. ‣ 3.4.4. Derived orbifold lifts of flow categories and bimodules ‣ 3.4. Derived orbifold charts with stratifications ‣ 3. Abstract constructions of chain complexes and maps over the integers ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.25</span></a> (C)).</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS5.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">3.5.3. </span>Straightening</h4>

<div id="S3.SS5.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS5.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As we will perform FOP perturbations over stratified charts, we need to consider straightenings in the stratified situation.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmthm31" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmthm31.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 3.31</span></span><span id="S3.Thmthm31.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Straightenings)<span id="S3.Thmthm31.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmthm31.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S3.I21" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S3.I21.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S3.I21.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I21.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S3.I21.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathcal{U}},{\mathcal{E}},{\mathcal{S}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathcal{U}},{\mathcal{E}},{\mathcal{S}})</annotation></semantics></math> be an <math id="S3.I21.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔸</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{A}}</annotation></semantics></math>-stratified derived orbifold chart. A <span id="S3.I21.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">straightening</span> consists of a Riemannian metric on <math id="S3.I21.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{U}}</annotation></semantics></math> and a connection on <math id="S3.I21.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{E}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{E}}</annotation></semantics></math>
such that for each <math id="S3.I21.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in{\mathbb{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝔸</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in{\mathbb{A}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the restriction of the metric and the connection onto <math id="S3.I21.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{U}}_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{U}}_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> (which is itself a smooth orbifold) is a straightening of <math id="S3.I21.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathcal{U}}_{\alpha},{\mathcal{E}}|_{{\mathcal{U}}_{\alpha}},{\mathcal{S}}|_{{\mathcal{U}}_{\alpha}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathcal{U}}_{\alpha},{\mathcal{E}}|_{{\mathcal{U}}_{\alpha}},{\mathcal{S}}|_{{\mathcal{U}}_{\alpha}})</annotation></semantics></math> (see Definition <a href="#S2.Thmthm1" title="Definition 2.1. ‣ 2.1.1. Derived orbifold charts ‣ 2.1. Orbifolds and the canonical Whitney stratification on 𝒵_𝑑 ‣ 2. Recap of the FOP natural transformation and multiplicativity ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I21.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S3.I21.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I21.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Consider a system of derived orbifold presentations on an <math id="S3.I21.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔸</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{A}}</annotation></semantics></math>-stratified space <math id="S3.I21.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>. A <span id="S3.I21.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">straightening</span> consists of a collection of straightenings of <math id="S3.I21.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S3.I21.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in{\mathbb{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝔸</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in{\mathbb{A}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that for each pair <math id="S3.I21.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\leq\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\leq\beta</annotation></semantics></math> (with associated chart embedding <math id="S3.I21.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\iota}}_{\beta\alpha}=(\iota_{\beta\alpha},\widehat{\iota}_{\beta\alpha}):C_{\alpha}\hookrightarrow\partial^{\alpha}C_{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝜾</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ι</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ι</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">↪</mo><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>β</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\iota}}_{\beta\alpha}=(\iota_{\beta\alpha},\widehat{\iota}_{\beta\alpha}):C_{\alpha}\hookrightarrow\partial^{\alpha}C_{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>), the domain embedding <math id="S3.I21.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota_{\beta\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ι</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota_{\beta\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> is isometric and the bundle embedding preserves the connection, i.e., the image of the bundle embedding is preserved by the connection <math id="S3.I21.i2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla^{{\mathcal{E}}_{\beta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>β</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla^{{\mathcal{E}}_{\beta}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the restriction of <math id="S3.I21.i2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla^{{\mathcal{E}}_{\alpha}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla^{{\mathcal{E}}_{\alpha}}</annotation></semantics></math> to the image of the bundle embedding coincides with <math id="S3.I21.i2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla^{{\mathcal{E}}_{\alpha}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla^{{\mathcal{E}}_{\alpha}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I21.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S3.I21.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I21.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Consider a derived orbifold lift <math id="S3.I21.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathfrak{D}}^{\mathcal{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔇</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathfrak{D}}^{\mathcal{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> of a topological flow category <math id="S3.I21.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\mathcal{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>T</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\mathcal{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S3.I21.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{P}}</annotation></semantics></math>. A <span id="S3.I21.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">straightening</span> on <math id="S3.I21.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathfrak{D}}^{\mathcal{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔇</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathfrak{D}}^{\mathcal{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> consists of a straightening on all charts <math id="S3.I21.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying the following condition. Fix <math id="S3.I21.i3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;q</annotation></semantics></math>. For each <math id="S3.I21.i3.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\alpha=pr_{1}\cdots r_{l}q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=pr_{1}\cdots r_{l}q</annotation></semantics></math>, there is a product straightening on the associated chart <math id="S3.I21.i3.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="C_{\alpha}=C_{pr_{1}}\times\cdots\times C_{r_{l}q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>C</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.055em">⋯</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>C</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\alpha}=C_{pr_{1}}\times\cdots\times C_{r_{l}q}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then we require that the collection of these straightenings for all <math id="S3.I21.i3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in{\mathbb{A}}_{pq}^{\mathcal{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>𝔸</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in{\mathbb{A}}_{pq}^{\mathcal{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a straightening on the system of derived orbifold presentations of <math id="S3.I21.i3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{pq}^{\mathcal{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{pq}^{\mathcal{P}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I21.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(4)</span> 
<div id="S3.I21.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I21.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">It is straightforward to define the notion of straightenings on a derived orbifold lift of a flow bimodule <math id="S3.I21.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> compatible with existing straightenings on the lifts of the two flow categories <math id="S3.I21.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\mathcal{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>T</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\mathcal{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.I21.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\mathcal{P}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>T</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\mathcal{P}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> with derived orbifold lifts <math id="S3.I21.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathfrak{D}}^{\mathcal{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔇</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathfrak{D}}^{\mathcal{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.I21.i4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathfrak{D}}^{\mathcal{P}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔇</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathfrak{D}}^{\mathcal{P}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Namely, it consists of a straightening on all charts <math id="S3.I21.i4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{M}_{pp^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{M}_{pp^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that: for <math id="S3.I21.i4.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\alpha=pq_{1}\cdots q_{k}q^{\prime}_{k^{\prime}}\cdots q^{\prime}_{1}p^{\prime}\in{\mathbb{A}}_{pp^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝔸</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=pq_{1}\cdots q_{k}q^{\prime}_{k^{\prime}}\cdots q^{\prime}_{1}p^{\prime}\in{\mathbb{A}}_{pp^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S3.I21.i4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\alpha}\neq\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\alpha}\neq\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>, there is a product straightening on the product chart <math id="S3.I21.i4.p1.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="C^{\mathcal{P}}_{pq_{1}}\times\cdots\times C^{M}_{q_{k}q^{\prime}_{k^{\prime}}}\times\cdots\times C^{\mathcal{P}^{\prime}}_{q^{\prime}_{1}p^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.055em">⋯</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>C</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>M</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.055em">⋯</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>C</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\mathcal{P}}_{pq_{1}}\times\cdots\times C^{M}_{q_{k}q^{\prime}_{k^{\prime}}}\times\cdots\times C^{\mathcal{P}^{\prime}}_{q^{\prime}_{1}p^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>; we require that the collection of these straightenings for all <math id="S3.I21.i4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in{\mathbb{A}}_{pp^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝔸</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in{\mathbb{A}}_{pp^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a straightening on the system of derived orbifold presentations of <math id="S3.I21.i4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{pp^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{pp^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS5.SSS4" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">3.5.4. </span>Compatibility</h4>

<div id="S3.SS5.SSS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS5.SSS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We need the three kinds of additional structures (collar structure, scaffolding, and straightening) to be compatible in a certain sense. These compatibility conditions are necessary for the inductive construction of FOP perturbations. For example, once a perturbation is chosen on all boundary strata, it can be canonically extended to a neighborhood of the boundary using the collar structure; meanwhile, there is another automatic extension using the scaffolding. Hence a compatibility requirement between these two structures is necessary. We also need the automatic extensions remain in the class of FOP perturbations, which further requires that the straightening is compatible with the collar structure and the scaffolding.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmthm32" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_rem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmthm32.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark 3.32</span></span><span id="S3.Thmthm32.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmthm32.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmthm32.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In practice the three kinds of structures are constructed in different ways. The collar structure is constructed by the outer-collaring construction, which is very easy and straightforward. Then (see Subsection <a href="#S5.SS8" title="5.8. Constructing scaffolding ‣ 5. Global Kuranishi charts on Floer moduli spaces ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.8</span></a>) we construct scaffolding in the topological category. The scaffolding will play a role in the smoothing process. After smoothing, the topological charts become smooth. Then finally we construct the compatible straightenings.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmthm33" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_rem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmthm33.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark 3.33</span></span><span id="S3.Thmthm33.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmthm33.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmthm33.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the following, we just define the notions of compatibility of a derived orbifold presentation. The relevant compatibility requirements for flow categories and flow bimodules are then reduced to the corresponding requirements for the induced derived orbifold presentations of all relevant topological spaces.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmthm34" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmthm34.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 3.34</span></span><span id="S3.Thmthm34.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmthm34.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmthm34.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Consider a system of derived orbifold presentations <math id="S3.Thmthm34.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{C_{\alpha}\}_{\alpha\in{\mathbb{A}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝔸</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{C_{\alpha}\}_{\alpha\in{\mathbb{A}}}</annotation></semantics></math> of an <math id="S3.Thmthm34.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔸</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{A}}</annotation></semantics></math>-stratified space <math id="S3.Thmthm34.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>. Suppose it is equipped with a collar structure and a scaffolding. We say that they are compatible if the following conditions are satisfied.</p>
<ol id="S3.I22" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S3.I22.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S3.I22.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I22.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given a triple <math id="S3.I22.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&lt;\beta&lt;\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&lt;\beta&lt;\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, we require that the following diagram commutes.</p>
<table id="S3.Ex94" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
