<p id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p3.5" class="ltx_p">By definition,</p>
<table id="S5.Ex183" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex183.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{pr}\in H^{0}\left(\overline{\rm Hom}(\iota_{F_{pr}}^{*}T\mathbb{CP}^{d_{pr}},u^{*}TM)\otimes\iota_{F_{pr}}^{*}{\mathcal{O}}(k)\right)\otimes\overline{H^{0}(\iota_{F_{pr}}^{*}{\mathcal{O}}(k))_{0}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Hom</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>pr</mi></msub><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℂ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>pr</mi></msub></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>TM</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>pr</mi></msub><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mover accent="true"><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{pr}\in H^{0}\left(\overline{\rm Hom}(\iota_{F_{pr}}^{*}T\mathbb{CP}^{d_{pr}},u^{*}TM)\otimes\iota_{F_{pr}}^{*}{\mathcal{O}}(k)\right)\otimes\overline{H^{0}(\iota_{F_{pr}}^{*}{\mathcal{O}}(k))_{0}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p3.6" class="ltx_p">Notice that there are natural linear inclusions</p>
<table id="S5.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex184"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex184.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ H^{0}(\iota_{F_{pr}}^{*}{\mathcal{O}}(k))_{0}\hookrightarrow H^{0}(\iota_{F_{prq}}^{*}{\mathcal{O}}(k))_{0},\ " display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↪</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ H^{0}(\iota_{F_{pr}}^{*}{\mathcal{O}}(k))_{0}\hookrightarrow H^{0}(\iota_{F_{prq}}^{*}{\mathcal{O}}(k))_{0},\ </annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex184.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ H^{0}(\iota_{F_{rq}}^{*}{\mathcal{O}}(k))_{0}\hookrightarrow H^{0}(\iota_{F_{prq}}^{*}{\mathcal{O}}(k))_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↪</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ H^{0}(\iota_{F_{rq}}^{*}{\mathcal{O}}(k))_{0}\hookrightarrow H^{0}(\iota_{F_{prq}}^{*}{\mathcal{O}}(k))_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p3.7" class="ltx_p">defined by extending by zero. Moreover, the linear embeddings (<a href="#S5.E39" title="In 5.4.2. Product construction: the case of two factors ‣ 5.4. Global chart construction III ‣ 5. Global Kuranishi charts on Floer moduli spaces ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.39</span></a>) induce bundle maps</p>
<table id="S5.Ex185" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex185.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\rm Hom}(\iota_{F_{pr}}^{*}T\mathbb{CP}^{d_{pr}},u_{pr}^{*}TM)\otimes\iota_{F_{pr}}^{*}{\mathcal{O}}(k)\to\overline{\rm Hom}(\iota_{F_{prq}}^{*}T\mathbb{CP}^{d_{pq}},u_{prq}^{*}TM)\otimes\iota_{F_{prq}}^{*}{\mathcal{O}}(k)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Hom</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>pr</mi></msub><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℂ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>pr</mi></msub></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>pr</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>TM</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>pr</mi></msub><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Hom</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>prq</mi></msub><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℂ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>pq</mi></msub></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>prq</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>TM</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>prq</mi></msub><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\rm Hom}(\iota_{F_{pr}}^{*}T\mathbb{CP}^{d_{pr}},u_{pr}^{*}TM)\otimes\iota_{F_{pr}}^{*}{\mathcal{O}}(k)\to\overline{\rm Hom}(\iota_{F_{prq}}^{*}T\mathbb{CP}^{d_{pq}},u_{prq}^{*}TM)\otimes\iota_{F_{prq}}^{*}{\mathcal{O}}(k)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p3.8" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="S5.Ex186" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex186.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\rm Hom}(\iota_{F_{rq}}^{*}T\mathbb{CP}^{d_{rq}},u_{rq}^{*}TM)\otimes\iota_{F_{rq}}^{*}{\mathcal{O}}(k)\to\overline{\rm Hom}(\iota_{F_{prq}}^{*}T\mathbb{CP}^{d_{pq}},u_{prq}^{*}TM)\otimes\iota_{F_{prq}}^{*}{\mathcal{O}}(k)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Hom</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>rq</mi></msub><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℂ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>rq</mi></msub></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>rq</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>TM</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>rq</mi></msub><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Hom</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>prq</mi></msub><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℂ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>pq</mi></msub></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>prq</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>TM</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>prq</mi></msub><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\rm Hom}(\iota_{F_{rq}}^{*}T\mathbb{CP}^{d_{rq}},u_{rq}^{*}TM)\otimes\iota_{F_{rq}}^{*}{\mathcal{O}}(k)\to\overline{\rm Hom}(\iota_{F_{prq}}^{*}T\mathbb{CP}^{d_{pq}},u_{prq}^{*}TM)\otimes\iota_{F_{prq}}^{*}{\mathcal{O}}(k)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p3.9" class="ltx_p">covering the inclusion maps between domains.
These are defined by extending elements in <math id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Hom" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Hom</annotation></semantics></math> by zero in the normal directions to <math id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{pr}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{pr}</annotation></semantics></math> resp. <math id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{rq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{rq}</annotation></semantics></math>. As elements of <math id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{0}(\overline{\rm Hom}(\iota_{F_{pr}}^{*}T\mathbb{CP}^{d_{pr}},u^{*}TM)\otimes\iota_{F_{pr}}^{*}{\mathcal{O}}(k))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Hom</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>pr</mi></msub><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℂ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>pr</mi></msub></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>TM</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>pr</mi></msub><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{0}(\overline{\rm Hom}(\iota_{F_{pr}}^{*}T\mathbb{CP}^{d_{pr}},u^{*}TM)\otimes\iota_{F_{pr}}^{*}{\mathcal{O}}(k))</annotation></semantics></math> vanish at nodes (because of the holonomy of <math id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla^{TM}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mo>∇</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla^{TM}</annotation></semantics></math>), one naturally has the linear inclusions</p>
<table id="S5.Ex187" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex187.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{0}\left(\overline{\rm Hom}(\iota_{F_{pr}}^{*}T\mathbb{CP}^{d_{pr}},u_{pr}^{*}TM)\otimes\iota_{F_{pr}}^{*}{\mathcal{O}}(k)\right)\to H^{0}\left(\overline{\rm Hom}(\iota_{F_{prq}}^{*}T\mathbb{CP}^{d_{pq}},u_{prq}^{*}TM)\otimes\iota_{F_{prq}}^{*}{\mathcal{O}}(k)\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Hom</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>pr</mi></msub><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℂ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>pr</mi></msub></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>pr</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>TM</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>pr</mi></msub><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Hom</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>prq</mi></msub><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℂ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>pq</mi></msub></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>prq</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>TM</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>prq</mi></msub><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{0}\left(\overline{\rm Hom}(\iota_{F_{pr}}^{*}T\mathbb{CP}^{d_{pr}},u_{pr}^{*}TM)\otimes\iota_{F_{pr}}^{*}{\mathcal{O}}(k)\right)\to H^{0}\left(\overline{\rm Hom}(\iota_{F_{prq}}^{*}T\mathbb{CP}^{d_{pq}},u_{prq}^{*}TM)\otimes\iota_{F_{prq}}^{*}{\mathcal{O}}(k)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p3.10" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="S5.Ex188" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex188.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{0}\left(\overline{\rm Hom}(\iota_{F_{rq}}^{*}T\mathbb{CP}^{d_{rq}},u_{rq}^{*}TM)\otimes\iota_{F_{rq}}^{*}{\mathcal{O}}(k)\right)\to H^{0}\left(\overline{\rm Hom}(\iota_{F_{prq}}^{*}T\mathbb{CP}^{d_{pq}},u_{prq}^{*}TM)\otimes\iota_{F_{prq}}^{*}{\mathcal{O}}(k)\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Hom</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>rq</mi></msub><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℂ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>rq</mi></msub></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>rq</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>TM</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>rq</mi></msub><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Hom</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>prq</mi></msub><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℂ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>pq</mi></msub></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>prq</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>TM</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>prq</mi></msub><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{0}\left(\overline{\rm Hom}(\iota_{F_{rq}}^{*}T\mathbb{CP}^{d_{rq}},u_{rq}^{*}TM)\otimes\iota_{F_{rq}}^{*}{\mathcal{O}}(k)\right)\to H^{0}\left(\overline{\rm Hom}(\iota_{F_{prq}}^{*}T\mathbb{CP}^{d_{pq}},u_{prq}^{*}TM)\otimes\iota_{F_{prq}}^{*}{\mathcal{O}}(k)\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p3.11" class="ltx_p">Therefore, by taking the sum of the images of <math id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{pr}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{pr}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{rq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{rq}</annotation></semantics></math>, one obtains an element</p>
<table id="S5.Ex189" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex189.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{prq}\in H^{0}\left(\overline{\rm Hom}(\iota_{F_{prq}}^{*}T\mathbb{CP}^{d_{pq}},u_{prq}^{*}TM)\otimes\iota_{F_{prq}}^{*}{\mathcal{O}}(k)\right)\otimes\overline{H^{0}(\iota_{F_{prq}}^{*}{\mathcal{O}}(k))_{0}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Hom</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>prq</mi></msub><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℂ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>pq</mi></msub></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>prq</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>TM</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>prq</mi></msub><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mover accent="true"><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{prq}\in H^{0}\left(\overline{\rm Hom}(\iota_{F_{prq}}^{*}T\mathbb{CP}^{d_{pq}},u_{prq}^{*}TM)\otimes\iota_{F_{prq}}^{*}{\mathcal{O}}(k)\right)\otimes\overline{H^{0}(\iota_{F_{prq}}^{*}{\mathcal{O}}(k))_{0}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p3.12" class="ltx_p">Consider the quadruple <math id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Sigma_{prq},u_{prq},F_{prq},\eta_{prq})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Sigma_{prq},u_{prq},F_{prq},\eta_{prq})</annotation></semantics></math>. One can check that this is a framed cylinder of type <math id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="prq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">prq</annotation></semantics></math> which represents an element <math id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{x}_{prq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{x}_{prq}</annotation></semantics></math> in the thickened moduli space <math id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{prq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{prq}</annotation></semantics></math>. It is also straightforward to see that we just defined a continuous embedding</p>
<table id="S5.Ex190" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex190.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vartheta_{prq}:V_{pr}\times V_{rq}\to\partial^{prq}V_{pq}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϑ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vartheta_{prq}:V_{pr}\times V_{rq}\to\partial^{prq}V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p3.13" class="ltx_p">which is equivariant with respect to the group inclusion <math id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pr}\times G_{rq}\hookrightarrow G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↪</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pr}\times G_{rq}\hookrightarrow G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>. Denote the image of <math id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vartheta_{prq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϑ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vartheta_{prq}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{prq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{prq}</annotation></semantics></math>. The equivariance implies that one can extend <math id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vartheta_{prq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϑ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vartheta_{prq}</annotation></semantics></math> to</p>
<table id="S5.E40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vartheta_{prq}^{\sim}:G_{pq}\times_{G_{prq}}(V_{pr}\times V_{rq})\to\partial^{prq}V_{pq}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϑ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>∼</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vartheta_{prq}^{\sim}:G_{pq}\times_{G_{prq}}(V_{pr}\times V_{rq})\to\partial^{prq}V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5.40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p3.14" class="ltx_p">whose image is denoted (in the same pattern as <math id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p3.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{(d_{0},d_{1})}^{\sim}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{(d_{0},d_{1})}^{\sim}</annotation></semantics></math>) by</p>
<table id="S5.Ex191" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex191.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{prq}^{\sim}\subset\partial^{prq}V_{pq}\subset V_{pq}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>∼</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">⊂</mo><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{prq}^{\sim}\subset\partial^{prq}V_{pq}\subset V_{pq}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmthm51" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_rem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmthm51.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark 5.51</span></span><span id="S5.Thmthm51.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmthm51.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmthm51.p1.1" class="ltx_p">However, the restriction of the Kuranishi map <math id="S5.Thmthm51.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{pq}:V_{pq}\to E_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{pq}:V_{pq}\to E_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> to the stratum <math id="S5.Thmthm51.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{prq}V_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{prq}V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> does not match with the Kuranishi map of the product of <math id="S5.Thmthm51.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{pr}\times S_{rq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{pr}\times S_{rq}</annotation></semantics></math>. For example, if <math id="S5.Thmthm51.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{pr}\in V_{pr}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{pr}\in V_{pr}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.Thmthm51.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{rq}\in V_{rq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{rq}\in V_{rq}</annotation></semantics></math> have orthonormal framings, the corresponding framing on <math id="S5.Thmthm51.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vartheta_{prq}(x_{pr},x_{rq})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϑ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vartheta_{prq}(x_{pr},x_{rq})</annotation></semantics></math> is not necessarily orthonormal (with respect to the <math id="S5.Thmthm51.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-pairing). Nonetheless, the Hermitian matrix part of the Kuranishi maps are given by two different kinds of normalization scheme, which can be interpolated once we have an outer-collaring (see Subsection <a href="#S5.SS7" title="5.7. Outer collaring ‣ 5. Global Kuranishi charts on Floer moduli spaces ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.7</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Just as the space <math id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, for <math id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;r&lt;s&lt;q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;r&lt;s&lt;q</annotation></semantics></math>, the embeddings of the thickened moduli spaces <math id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> fit in to the following commutative diagram</p>
<table id="S5.E41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
