<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5.41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">where the arrows are constructed from (<a href="#S5.E40" title="In 5.4.2. Product construction: the case of two factors ‣ 5.4. Global chart construction III ‣ 5. Global Kuranishi charts on Floer moduli spaces ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.40</span></a>). Indeed, the associativity on the gluing of the underlying map <math id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(u,\Sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(u,\Sigma)</annotation></semantics></math> and the superposition of perturbation sections <math id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> is straightforward from definition, while the associativity of the framing component <math id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> follows from Proposition <a href="#S5.Thmthm22" title="Proposition 5.22. ‣ 5.2.5. Boundary strata of the auxiliary moduli spaces ‣ 5.2. Global chart construction I ‣ 5. Global Kuranishi charts on Floer moduli spaces ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.22</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Embedding obstruction bundles.</span> We now describe how the obstruction bundles <math id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{pr}\to V_{pr}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{pr}\to V_{pr}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{rq}\to V_{rq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{rq}\to V_{rq}</annotation></semantics></math> can be embedded into <math id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> restricted to <math id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{prq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{prq}</annotation></semantics></math>. Recall that</p>
<table id="S5.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex192"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex192.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ E_{pr}=O_{pr}\oplus Q_{pr},\ " display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ E_{pr}=O_{pr}\oplus Q_{pr},\ </annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex192.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ E_{rq}=O_{rq}\oplus Q_{rq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ E_{rq}=O_{rq}\oplus Q_{rq}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p">where the <math id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>O</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O</annotation></semantics></math>-factors are the spaces of the sections <math id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> and the <math id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>-factors are the trivial bundle which are use to normalize the framings. The normalization strategy is to use the <math id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-metric on the domain curves and to require the framings are orthonormal.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Indeed, the embeddings <math id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vartheta_{{prq}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϑ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vartheta_{{prq}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vartheta_{{prq}}^{\sim}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ϑ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>∼</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vartheta_{{prq}}^{\sim}</annotation></semantics></math> described above illustrate how to embed the <math id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>O</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O</annotation></semantics></math>-factors. Hence there are natural bundle maps</p>
<table id="S5.Ex193" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex193.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lx@xy@svg{\hbox{\raise 2.5pt\hbox{\kern 40.04213pt\hbox{\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\hbox{\vtop{\halign{\entry@#!@&amp;&amp;\entry@@#!@\cr&amp;&amp;\cr&amp;&amp;\crcr}}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern-39.81712pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{O_{prq}=O_{pr}\boxplus O_{rq}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 55.55052pt\raise 7.84723pt\hbox{{}\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise-2.37502pt\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\widehat{\vartheta}_{prq}^{O}}$}}}\kern 3.0pt}}}}}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 94.04213pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise-24.3889pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\kern 64.04213pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{}$}}}}}}}{\hbox{\kern 94.04213pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{O_{pq}|_{\partial^{prq}V_{pq}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 121.6982pt\raise-24.27777pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\kern-40.04213pt\raise-31.72221pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{V_{prq}=V_{pr}\times V_{rq}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 59.76181pt\raise-38.13887pt\hbox{{}\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise-1.44444pt\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\vartheta_{prq}}$}}}\kern 3.0pt}}}}}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 101.51309pt\raise-31.72221pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\kern 64.04213pt\raise-31.72221pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{}$}}}}}}}{\hbox{\kern 101.51309pt\raise-31.72221pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{\partial^{prq}V_{pq}}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces}}}}\ignorespaces." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext> <svg style="vertical-align:-61.65148295751825px" height="83.37" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="55.41 61.65 262.07 83.37" width="262.07"> <g transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 55.406295166184535 83.36788360650598) translate(0,3.46) translate(55.41,0)"> <g transform="translate(-55.1,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"> <foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:7.36em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.41" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="101.89"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊞</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></span></span></foreignObject> </g> <path style="--l