<p id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p6.2" class="ltx_p">Moreover, as the <math id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>-bundles are pulled back from the auxiliary spaces <math id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and we have defined the corresponding bundle embeddings, we just pull back these embeddings to the thickened moduli space. Hence we have the bundle maps</p>
