<p id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p6.4" class="ltx_p">Take the <math id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariantization with respect to the embedding <math id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pr}\times G_{rq}\hookrightarrow G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↪</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pr}\times G_{rq}\hookrightarrow G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>, the above diagram lifts to</p>
