<p id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p6.5" class="ltx_p">and we denote the image of <math id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}(E_{prq})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}(E_{prq})</annotation></semantics></math> under the map <math id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\vartheta}_{prq}^{\sim}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ϑ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>∼</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\vartheta}_{prq}^{\sim}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E^{\sim}_{prq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>∼</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E^{\sim}_{prq}</annotation></semantics></math>. For a quadruple of elements <math id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;r&lt;s&lt;q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;r&lt;s&lt;q</annotation></semantics></math>, the following diagram lives over (<a href="#S5.E41" title="In 5.4.2. Product construction: the case of two factors ‣ 5.4. Global chart construction III ‣ 5. Global Kuranishi charts on Floer moduli spaces ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.41</span></a>).</p>
<table id="S5.E42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S5.E42.m1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_markedasmath" height="112.89" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-101.81723120005708px" version="1.1" viewBox="63.50 101.82 457.25 112.89" width="457.25"><g transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 63.497781654570105 112.88683131075308) translate(0,3.46) translate(63.5,0)"><g transform="translate(96.71,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:9.3em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="14.34" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="128.68"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.E42.m1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{G_{pq}(E_{pr}\times E_{rs}\times E_{sq})\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{G_{pq}(E_{pr}\times E_{rs}\times E_{sq})\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 123.02234523504524 -11.569253138458645 L 123.02234523504524 -11.569253138458645" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(47.92,0) translate(0,-32.17)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 7.4 -0.84" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 5.94 4.5" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 123.02234523504524 -11.569253138458645 L 47.92074750069185 -32.17102532171025" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 47.92074750069185 -32.17102532171025 L 47.92074750069185 -32.17102532171025" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 207.34002353641293 -11.569253138458645 L 207.39998612246177 -11.687278087759012" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(282.45,0) translate(0,-32.17)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -5.94 4.5" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -7.4 -0.84" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 207.34002353641293 -11.569253138458645 L 282.4435426071503 -32.17102532171025" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 282.38360113468804 -32.059292221227686 L 282.4435426071503 -32.17102532171025" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(-63.5,0) translate(0,-45.32) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:8.58em;--ltx-fo-height:0.9em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.3em;font-size:10pt;" height="16.6" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 12.45)" width="118.69"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.E42.m1.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{G_{pq}\big(E_{pr}\times\partial^{rsq}E_{rq}\big)\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.055em">×</mo><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{G_{pq}\big(E_{pr}\times\partial^{rsq}E_{rq}\big)\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 43.232517815137676 -57.077625570776256 L 43.27117679226988 -57.13623688728034" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(134.73,0) translate(0,-81.98)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -5.95 4.49" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -7.4 -0.85" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 43.232517815137676 -57.077625570776256 L 134.7240227888906 -81.97474581944228" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 134.7240227888906 -81.89162162885275 L 134.7240227888906 -81.97474581944228" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(266.9,0) translate(0,-45.32) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:8.57em;--ltx-fo-height:0.9em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.3em;font-size:10pt;" height="16.6" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 12.45)" width="118.55"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.E42.m1.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{G_{pq}\big(\partial^{prs}E_{ps}\times E_{sq}\big)\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{G_{pq}\big(\partial^{prs}E_{ps}\times E_{sq}\big)\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 287.10474690180916 -57.077625570776256 L 287.0926910438395 -57.077625570776256" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(195.67,0) translate(0,-81.95)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 7.4 -0.85" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 5.95 4.49" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 287.10474690180916 -57.077625570776256 L 195.67225440270644 -81.94497566228424" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 195.7221035807562 -81.94497566228424 L 195.67225440270644 -81.94497566228424" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(134.73,0) translate(0,-90.25) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.8em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.57" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="52.65"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.E42.m1.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{\partial^{prsq}E_{pq}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{\partial^{prsq}E_{pq}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="0" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5.42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p6.6" class="ltx_p">Beyond the ingredients of showing the commutativity of (<a href="#S5.E41" title="In 5.4.2. Product construction: the case of two factors ‣ 5.4. Global chart construction III ‣ 5. Global Kuranishi charts on Floer moduli spaces ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.41</span></a>), Proposition <a href="#S5.Thmthm26" title="Proposition 5.26. ‣ 5.2.6. Product of the bundle of quadratic forms ‣ 5.2. Global chart construction I ‣ 5. Global Kuranishi charts on Floer moduli spaces ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.26</span></a> covers the associativity of the superposition of the <math id="S5.SS4.SSS2.p6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>-component of the obstruction bundle.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS4.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">5.4.3. </span>The general case</h4>

<div id="S5.SS4.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS4.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Now we describe the product construction in the general situation, i.e. with multi-layered thickenings and multiple breakings. Consider a stratum <math id="S5.SS4.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\alpha=pr_{1}\cdots r_{l}q\in{\mathbb{A}}^{\rm Floer}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝔸</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>Floer</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=pr_{1}\cdots r_{l}q\in{\mathbb{A}}^{\rm Floer}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>. We can form the product chart</p>
<table id="S5.Ex197" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex197.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="K_{\alpha}:=K_{pr_{1}}\times\cdots\times K_{r_{k}q}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mi>K</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.055em">⋯</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>K</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\alpha}:=K_{pr_{1}}\times\cdots\times K_{r_{k}q}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS4.SSS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">whose domain is <math id="S5.SS4.SSS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="V_{\alpha}:=V_{pr_{1}}\times\cdots\times V_{r_{l}q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mi>V</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.055em">⋯</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>V</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\alpha}:=V_{pr_{1}}\times\cdots\times V_{r_{l}q}</annotation></semantics></math> and whose obstruction bundle is</p>
<table id="S5.Ex198" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex198.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{\alpha}:=E_{pr_{1}}\boxplus\cdots\boxplus E_{r_{l}q}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo>⊞</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>⊞</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{\alpha}:=E_{pr_{1}}\boxplus\cdots\boxplus E_{r_{l}q}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS4.SSS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">We would like to construct an equivariant embedding <math id="S5.SS4.SSS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> into <math id="S5.SS4.SSS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{\alpha}V_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{\alpha}V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> and embed the obstruction bundle equivariantly as well.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS4.SSS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS4.SSS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To embed the thickened moduli space, the first step is to unify the number of layers. Recall that in the multi-layered thickening strategy, each moduli space <math id="S5.SS4.SSS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{rs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{rs}</annotation></semantics></math> is thickened to <math id="S5.SS4.SSS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{rs}^{d_{rs}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{rs}^{d_{rs}}</annotation></semantics></math> which depends on the sequence of integers <math id="S5.SS4.SSS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{1}&lt;\cdots&lt;k_{d_{rs}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">&lt;</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">&lt;</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{1}&lt;\cdots&lt;k_{d_{rs}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmthm52" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmthm52.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5.52</span></span><span id="S5.Thmthm52.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmthm52.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmthm52.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmthm52.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There exists a natural <math id="S5.Thmthm52.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{rs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{rs}</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant inclusion</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex199" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex199.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{rs}^{d}\hookrightarrow V_{rs}^{d^{\prime}}\ {\rm if}\ d&lt;d^{\prime}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">↪</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>if</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{rs}^{d}\hookrightarrow V_{rs}^{d^{\prime}}\ {\rm if}\ d&lt;d^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.Thmthm52.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmthm52.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">defined by</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex200" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex200.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\Sigma,u,F,\eta_{1},\ldots,\eta_{d}]\mapsto[\Sigma,u,F,\eta_{1},\ldots,\eta_{d},\underbrace{0,\ldots,0}_{d^{\prime}-d}]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></munder></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\Sigma,u,F,\eta_{1},\ldots,\eta_{d}]\mapsto[\Sigma,u,F,\eta_{1},\ldots,\eta_{d},\underbrace{0,\ldots,0}_{d^{\prime}-d}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.Thmthm52.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmthm52.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where the last <math id="S5.Thmthm52.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{\prime}-d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{\prime}-d</annotation></semantics></math> zeroes are the zero vectors of the bundles of <math id="S5.Thmthm52.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(u,\iota_{F})^{*}E_{k_{d+1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ι</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(u,\iota_{F})^{*}E_{k_{d+1}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.Thmthm52.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ldots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ldots</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.Thmthm52.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(u,\iota_{F})^{*}E_{k_{d^{\prime}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ι</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><msub><mi>k</mi><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(u,\iota_{F})^{*}E_{k_{d^{\prime}}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS4.SSS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S5.SS4.SSS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS4.SSS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS4.SSS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Indeed, as we use <math id="S5.SS4.SSS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> to perturb the equation for <math id="S5.SS4.SSS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="S5.SS4.SSS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j&gt;i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j&gt;i</annotation></semantics></math>, the degree <math id="S5.SS4.SSS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> version of (<a href="#S5.E32" title="In Definition 5.45 (Multi-layered thickening). ‣ 5.3.3. Multi-layered thickening ‣ 5.3. Global chart construction II ‣ 5. Global Kuranishi charts on Floer moduli spaces ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.32</span></a>) implies that the representative <math id="S5.SS4.SSS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Sigma,u,F,\eta_{1},\ldots,\eta_{d},\underbrace{0,\ldots,0}_{d^{\prime}-d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></munder><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Sigma,u,F,\eta_{1},\ldots,\eta_{d},\underbrace{0,\ldots,0}_{d^{\prime}-d})</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the degree <math id="S5.SS4.SSS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> version of (<a href="#S5.E32" title="In Definition 5.45 (Multi-layered thickening). ‣ 5.3.3. Multi-layered thickening ‣ 5.3. Global chart construction II ‣ 5. Global Kuranishi charts on Floer moduli spaces ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.32</span></a>). As the <math id="S5.SS4.SSS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{rs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{rs}</annotation></semantics></math>-action changes the framing <math id="S5.SS4.SSS3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math>, such a map is indeed <math id="S5.SS4.SSS3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{rs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{rs}</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS4.SSS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS4.SSS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Now abbreviate <math id="S5.SS4.SSS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=d_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=d_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="S5.SS4.SSS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\alpha=pr_{1}\cdots r_{l}q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=pr_{1}\cdots r_{l}q</annotation></semantics></math>, one then obtains a <math id="S5.SS4.SSS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant inclusion between the thickened moduli spaces</p>
<table id="S5.Ex201" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex201.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="V_{\alpha}=V^{d_{pr_{1}}}_{pr_{1}}\times\cdots\times V^{d_{r_{l}q}}_{r_{l}q}\hookrightarrow V^{d}_{\alpha}:=V^{d}_{pr_{1}}\times\cdots\times V^{d}_{r_{l}q}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>V</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.055em">⋯</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>V</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">↪</mo><mi>V</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mi>V</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.055em">⋯</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>V</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\alpha}=V^{d_{pr_{1}}}_{pr_{1}}\times\cdots\times V^{d_{r_{l}q}}_{r_{l}q}\hookrightarrow V^{d}_{\alpha}:=V^{d}_{pr_{1}}\times\cdots\times V^{d}_{r_{l}q}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS4.SSS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p">The space <math id="S5.SS4.SSS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{d}_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>α</mi><mi>d</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{d}_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> on the right hand side can be embedded into <math id="S5.SS4.SSS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{\alpha}V_{pq}^{d_{pq}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{\alpha}V_{pq}^{d_{pq}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Indeed, it is straightforward to generalize the construction in the previous single-layered case with only two horizontal levels and the associativity can be verified as before.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS4.SSS3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS4.SSS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS4.SSS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Embedding obstruction bundles</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS4.SSS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS4.SSS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Now for each stratum <math id="S5.SS4.SSS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\alpha=pr_{1}\cdots r_{l}q\in{\mathbb{A}}_{pq}^{\rm Floer}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝔸</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>Floer</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=pr_{1}\cdots r_{l}q\in{\mathbb{A}}_{pq}^{\rm Floer}</annotation></semantics></math>, define the bundles</p>
<table id="S5.Ex202" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex202.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="O_{\alpha}:=O_{pr_{1}\to pq}\oplus\cdots\oplus O_{r_{l}q\to pq}:=O_{pr_{1}}\boxplus\cdots\boxplus O_{r_{l}q}\to V_{\alpha}=V_{pr_{1}}\times\cdots\times V_{r_{l}q}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mi>O</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⊕</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>⊕</mo><mi>O</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mi>O</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo>⊞</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>⊞</mo><mi>O</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>V</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>V</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.055em">⋯</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>V</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{\alpha}:=O_{pr_{1}\to pq}\oplus\cdots\oplus O_{r_{l}q\to pq}:=O_{pr_{1}}\boxplus\cdots\boxplus O_{r_{l}q}\to V_{\alpha}=V_{pr_{1}}\times\cdots\times V_{r_{l}q}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS4.SSS3.p6.2" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="S5.Ex203" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex203.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="Q_{\alpha}:=Q_{pr_{1}\to pq}\oplus\cdots\oplus Q_{r_{l}q\to pq}:=Q_{pr_{1}}\boxplus\cdots\boxplus Q_{r_{l}q}\to V_{\alpha}=V_{pr_{1}}\times\cdots\times V_{r_{l}q}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mi>Q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⊕</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>⊕</mo><mi>Q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mi>Q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo>⊞</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>⊞</mo><mi>Q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>V</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>V</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.055em">⋯</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>V</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\alpha}:=Q_{pr_{1}\to pq}\oplus\cdots\oplus Q_{r_{l}q\to pq}:=Q_{pr_{1}}\boxplus\cdots\boxplus Q_{r_{l}q}\to V_{\alpha}=V_{pr_{1}}\times\cdots\times V_{r_{l}q}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS4.SSS3.p6.3" class="ltx_p">The construction of the two-factor case and the corresponding associativity induce <math id="S5.SS4.SSS3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant bundle embeddings</p>
<table id="S5.Ex204" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex204.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lx@xy@svg{\hbox{\raise 2.5pt\hbox{\kern 35.09947pt\hbox{\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\hbox{\vtop{\halign{\entry@#!@&amp;&amp;\entry@@#!@\cr&amp;&amp;\cr&amp;&amp;\crcr}}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern-35.09947pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{E_{\alpha}:=O_{\alpha}\oplus Q_{\alpha}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 36.12718pt\raise 7.36111pt\hbox{{}\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise-2.86111pt\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\widehat{\vartheta}_{\alpha}=\widehat{\vartheta}_{\alpha}^{O}\oplus\widehat{\vartheta}_{\alpha}^{Q}}$}}}\kern 3.0pt}}}}}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 89.09947pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise-24.3889pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\kern 59.09947pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{}$}}}}}}}{\hbox{\kern 89.09947pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{E_{pq}|_{\partial^{\alpha}V_{pq}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 113.71388pt\raise-24.27777pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\kern-9.87715pt\rais