<section id="S5.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.7. </span>Outer collaring</h3>

<div id="S5.SS7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We need to apply the outer-collaring construction in order to improve the weak K-chart lift constructed above to a K-chart lift and set space for the inductive smoothing procedure. Recall that the outer-collaring construction has been reviewed in Subsection <a href="#S3.SS3" title="3.3. Outer-collaring ‣ 3. Abstract constructions of chain complexes and maps over the integers ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a> in the topological category, including both the case of a single stratified space or a flow category, bimodule, etc. There is no more complexity to generalize to the case of the K-chart lift <math id="S5.SS7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathfrak{K}}^{\rm Floer}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔎</mi><mi>Floer</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathfrak{K}}^{\rm Floer}</annotation></semantics></math>. Indeed, for each pair <math id="S5.SS7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;q</annotation></semantics></math>, if we apply the outer-collaring construction to the thickened moduli space <math id="S5.SS7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> (with a fixed width, say <math id="S5.SS7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>), then one obtains a new <math id="S5.SS7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{A}}_{pq}^{\rm Floer}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝔸</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>Floer</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{A}}_{pq}^{\rm Floer}</annotation></semantics></math>-manifold, denoted by <math id="S5.SS7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{pq}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{pq}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math>. The <math id="S5.SS7.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>-action naturally extends to a <math id="S5.SS7.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>-action on <math id="S5.SS7.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{pq}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{pq}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math>. The obstruction bundle <math id="S5.SS7.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> and the Kuranishi section <math id="S5.SS7.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> are also naturally extended to a bundle <math id="S5.SS7.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{pq}^{+}\to V_{pq}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{pq}^{+}\to V_{pq}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> and a section <math id="S5.SS7.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{pq}^{+}:V_{pq}^{+}\to E_{pq}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{pq}^{+}:V_{pq}^{+}\to E_{pq}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math>. The footprint map <math id="S5.SS7.p1.m14" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\psi_{pq}:S_{pq}^{-1}(0)/G_{pq}\to\overline{\mathcal{M}}{}_{pq}^{\rm Floer}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mmultiscripts><mphantom></mphantom><mrow></mrow><mi>Floer</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{pq}:S_{pq}^{-1}(0)/G_{pq}\to\overline{\mathcal{M}}{}_{pq}^{\rm Floer}</annotation></semantics></math> is also canonically extended to a map</p>
<table id="S5.Ex229" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex229.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\psi_{pq}^{+}:(S_{pq}^{+})^{-1}(0)/G_{pq}\to(\overline{\mathcal{M}}{}_{pq}^{\rm Floer})^{+}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mmultiscripts><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mrow></mrow><mi>Floer</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{pq}^{+}:(S_{pq}^{+})^{-1}(0)/G_{pq}\to(\overline{\mathcal{M}}{}_{pq}^{\rm Floer})^{+}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS7.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where (recall that) <math id="S5.SS7.p1.m15" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(\overline{\mathcal{M}}{}_{pq}^{\rm Floer})^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mmultiscripts><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mrow></mrow><mi>Floer</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\overline{\mathcal{M}}{}_{pq}^{\rm Floer})^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> is the outer-collaring of <math id="S5.SS7.p1.m16" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\overline{\mathcal{M}}{}_{pq}^{\rm Floer}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>Floer</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\mathcal{M}}{}_{pq}^{\rm Floer}</annotation></semantics></math>. Notice that the structure maps required for a K-chart lift of a flow category are also obtained among the new charts via outer-collaring and their properties are still satisfied. In summary, one obtains a K-chart lift <math id="S5.SS7.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathfrak{K}}^{\rm Floer})^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝔎</mi><mi>Floer</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathfrak{K}}^{\rm Floer})^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> of the outer-collared flow category <math id="S5.SS7.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(T^{\rm Floer})^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>Floer</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(T^{\rm Floer})^{+}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS7.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS7.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In a similar way, one can apply the outer-collaring construction to the system of auxiliary moduli spaces. Each space <math id="S5.SS7.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> becomes a new space <math id="S5.SS7.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{d}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{d}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> and the projection maps <math id="S5.SS7.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{pq}:V_{pq}\to B_{d_{pq}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{pq}:V_{pq}\to B_{d_{pq}}</annotation></semantics></math> are extended to <math id="S5.SS7.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{pq}^{+}:V_{pq}^{+}\to B_{d_{pq}}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{pq}^{+}:V_{pq}^{+}\to B_{d_{pq}}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> with listed properties in Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmthm62" title="Theorem 5.62. ‣ 5.6. Weak K-chart lift ‣ 5. Global Kuranishi charts on Floer moduli spaces ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.62</span></a> remain valid.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS7.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS7.p3.1" class="ltx_p">What we need to take care of is the smoothness of the outer-collared auxiliary moduli spaces. Though <math id="S5.SS7.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is a smooth manifold with faces, it is not <span id="S5.SS7.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">a priori</span> clear whether <math id="S5.SS7.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{d}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{d}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> has an automatically induced smooth structure or if the outer-collaring of the maps <math id="S5.SS7.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{(d_{0},d_{1})}:B_{d_{0}}\times B_{d_{1}}\to\partial^{(d_{0},d_{1})}B_{d_{0}+d_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{(d_{0},d_{1})}:B_{d_{0}}\times B_{d_{1}}\to\partial^{(d_{0},d_{1})}B_{d_{0}+d_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math> are still smooth. What we learned from the work of Fukaya–Oh–Ohta–Ono <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx17" title="" class="ltx_ref">FOOO</a>]</cite> is that moduli spaces of pseudoholomorphic curves have a stronger structure near corners which comes from their “exponential decay estimates” associated to the gluing construction. This kind of structure is formalized in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx18" title="" class="ltx_ref">FOOO20</a>, Chapter 25]</cite> under the name “admissible smooth structure.” In short, an admissible structure on a smooth manifold (or orbifold) with faces is an atlas of smooth charts such that the coordinate changes among them satisfy certain exponential decay estimates near the boundary and corner; moreover, the outer-collaring of an admissible smooth manifold or orbifolds automatically carries an admissible smooth structure. This argument applies to our situation of <math id="S5.SS7.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. Indeed, <math id="S5.SS7.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> comes from the moduli space of stable maps into <math id="S5.SS7.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{CP}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℂ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{CP}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> which is an algebraic object. The exponential decay estimate holds automatically, for both the original moduli and the real blowup <math id="S5.SS7.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, the outer-collaring <math id="S5.SS7.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{d}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{d}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> is still smooth and the embeddings</p>
<table id="S5.Ex230" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex230.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{(d_{0},d_{1})}^{+}:B_{d_{0}}^{+}\times B_{d_{1}}^{+}\to B_{d_{0}+d_{1}}^{+}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{(d_{0},d_{1})}^{+}:B_{d_{0}}^{+}\times B_{d_{1}}^{+}\to B_{d_{0}+d_{1}}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS7.p3.2" class="ltx_p">are still smooth.</p>
</div>
<section id="S5.SS7.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">5.7.1. </span>Matching the Kuranishi sections</h4>

<div id="S5.SS7.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS7.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The collection of global Kuranishi charts constructed in the previous section does not have matching Kuranishi maps over boundary or corners. Using the room constructed by the outer-collaring operation, we can connect these Kuranishi maps.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmthm63" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmthm63.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 5.63</span></span><span id="S5.Thmthm63.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmthm63.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmthm63.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmthm63.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There exist a collection of <math id="S5.Thmthm63.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant sections</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex231" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex231.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\check{S}_{pq}^{+}:V_{pq}^{+}\to E_{pq}^{+}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>ˇ</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\check{S}_{pq}^{+}:V_{pq}^{+}\to E_{pq}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.Thmthm63.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmthm63.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">satisfying the following conditions.</span></p>
<ol id="S5.I25" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S5.I25.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S5.I25.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I25.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I25.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The restriction of </span><math id="S5.I25.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\check{S}_{pq}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>ˇ</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\check{S}_{pq}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I25.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> to </span><math id="S5.I25.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{pq}\subset V_{pq}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{pq}\subset V_{pq}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I25.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> coincides with </span><math id="S5.I25.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{pq}:V_{pq}\to E_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{pq}:V_{pq}\to E_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I25.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I25.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S5.I25.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I25.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I25.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">With respect to the direct sum decomposition </span><math id="S5.I25.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{pq}^{+}=O_{pq}^{+}\oplus Q_{pq}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>⊕</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{pq}^{+}=O_{pq}^{+}\oplus Q_{pq}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I25.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, if we write </span><math id="S5.I25.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\check{S}_{pq}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>ˇ</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\check{S}_{pq}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I25.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> as </span><math id="S5.I25.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\check{S}_{pq}^{O,+}\oplus\check{S}_{pq}^{Q,+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>ˇ</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>⊕</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>ˇ</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\check{S}_{pq}^{O,+}\oplus\check{S}_{pq}^{Q,+}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I25.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, then </span><math id="S5.I25.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\check{S}_{pq}^{O,+}=S_{pq}^{O,+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>ˇ</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\check{S}_{pq}^{O,+}=S_{pq}^{O,+}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I25.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I25.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S5.I25.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I25.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I25.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There is a homeomorphism</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex232" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex232.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\psi_{pq}^{+}:(\check{S}_{pq}^{+})^{-1}(0)/G_{pq}\cong\overline{\mathcal{M}}{}_{pq}^{\rm Floer}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>ˇ</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≅</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em">.</mo><mrow></mrow><mi>Floer</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{pq}^{+}:(\check{S}_{pq}^{+})^{-1}(0)/G_{pq}\cong\overline{\mathcal{M}}{}_{pq}^{\rm Floer}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I25.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(4)</span> 
<div id="S5.I25.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I25.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I25.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let </span><math id="S5.I25.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\check{\psi}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ψ</mi><mo>ˇ</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\check{\psi}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I25.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> be the corresponding extension of the footprint map. If we replace </span><math id="S5.I25.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{pq}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{pq}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I25.i4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> by </span><math id="S5.I25.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\check{S}_{pq}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>ˇ</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\check{S}_{pq}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I25.i4.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and replace </span><math id="S5.I25.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{pq}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{pq}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I25.i4.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> by </span><math id="S5.I25.i4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\check{\psi}_{pq}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ψ</mi><mo>ˇ</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\check{\psi}_{pq}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I25.i4.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> for all </span><math id="S5.I25.i4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="pq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">pq</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I25.i4.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, then the collection</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex233" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex233.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathfrak{K}}^{\rm Floer})^{+}:=\Big((K_{pq}^{+})_{p&lt;q},({\bm{\iota}}_{prq}^{+})_{p&lt;r&lt;q}\Big)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝔎</mi><mi>Floer</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜾</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathfrak{K}}^{\rm Floer})^{+}:=\Big((K_{pq}^{+})_{p&lt;q},({\bm{\iota}}_{prq}^{+})_{p&lt;r&lt;q}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.I25.i4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I25.i4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">is a K-chart lift of the flow category </span><math id="S5.I25.i4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(T^{\rm Floer})^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>Floer</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(T^{\rm Floer})^{+}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I25.i4.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS7.SSS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S5.SS7.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS7.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS7.SSS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">The failure of the naively obtained outer-collaring to be a K-chart lift is that the normalization condition (i.e. the section <math id="S5.SS7.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{pq}^{Q,+}:V_{pq}^{+}\to Q_{pq}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{pq}^{Q,+}:V_{pq}^{+}\to Q_{pq}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math>) does not match with the products on the boundary. We need to interpolate between <math id="S5.SS7.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{pq}^{Q,+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{pq}^{Q,+}</annotation></semantics></math> and the products on the collar parts. Here we only describe the situation near a codimension one stratum <math id="S5.SS7.SSS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="prq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">prq</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S5.SS7.SSS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,t)\in V_{pq}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,t)\in V_{pq}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> be a point in the collar region <math id="S5.SS7.SSS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{prq}V_{pq}\times[-1,0]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{prq}V_{pq}\times[-1,0]</annotation></semantics></math>. Geometrically, <math id="S5.SS7.SSS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> is represented by a framed cylinder <math id="S5.SS7.SSS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Sigma,u,\mu,\eta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Sigma,u,\mu,\eta)</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S5.SS7.SSS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma=\Sigma_{pr}\cup\Sigma_{rq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma=\Sigma_{pr}\cup\Sigma_{rq}</annotation></semantics></math> and the map <math id="S5.SS7.SSS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu:\Sigma\to{\mathcal{C}}_{0,2}(d_{pq})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu:\Sigma\to{\mathcal{C}}_{0,2}(d_{pq})</annotation></semantics></math> is represented by a frame</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex234" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex234.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F=(f_{0},\ldots,f_{d_{pq}})\in(H^{0}(L_{u},\Sigma))^{d_{pq}+1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F=(f_{0},\ldots,f_{d_{pq}})\in(H^{0}(L_{u},\Sigma))^{d_{pq}+1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS7.SSS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS7.SSS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Proposition <a href="#S5.Thmthm24" title="Proposition 5.24. ‣ 5.2.5. Boundary strata of the auxiliary moduli spaces ‣ 5.2. Global chart construction I ‣ 5. Global Kuranishi charts on Floer moduli spaces ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.24</span></a> tells us that the underlying map <math id="S5.SS7.SSS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\mu}}:\Sigma\to\mathbb{CP}^{d_{pq}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>ℂ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\mu}}:\Sigma\to\mathbb{CP}^{d_{pq}}</annotation></semantics></math> can be transformed canonically to a map <math id="S5.SS7.SSS1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\mu}}^{\rm normal}:\Sigma\to\mathbb{CP}^{d_{pq}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>normal</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>ℂ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\mu}}^{\rm normal}:\Sigma\to\mathbb{CP}^{d_{pq}}</annotation></semantics></math> via an invertible complex matirx of the form <math id="S5.SS7.SSS1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{d_{pq}+1}+\rho_{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{d_{pq}+1}+\rho_{Q}</annotation></semantics></math>. Choose a smooth cut-off function <math id="S5.SS7.SSS1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi(t)</annotation></semantics></math> which is equal to <math id="S5.SS7.SSS1.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S5.SS7.SSS1.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> near <math id="S5.SS7.SSS1.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-1</annotation></semantics></math> and euqal to <math id="S5.SS7.SSS1.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S5.SS7.SSS1.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> near <math id="S5.SS7.SSS1.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>. Then define</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex235" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex235.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\mu}}^{t}=(I_{d_{pq}+1}+\chi(t)\rho_{Q})\underline{\smash{\mu}}:\Sigma\to\mathbb{CP}^{d_{pq}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>ℂ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\mu}}^{t}=(I_{d_{pq}+1}+\chi(t)\rho_{Q})\underline{\smash{\mu}}:\Sigma\to\mathbb{CP}^{d_{pq}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS7.SSS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS7.SSS1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Then <math id="S5.SS7.SSS1.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\mu}}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>t</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\mu}}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is in normal position for <math id="S5.SS7.SSS1.p2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> near <math id="S5.SS7.SSS1.p2.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-1</annotation></semantics></math> and corresponding to a frame</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex236" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex236.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F^{t}=(f_{0}^{t},\ldots,f_{d_{pq}}^{t})\in(H^{0}(L_{u},\Sigma))^{d_{pq}+1}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F^{t}=(f_{0}^{t},\ldots,f_{d_{pq}}^{t})\in(H^{0}(L_{u},\Sigma))^{d_{pq}+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS7.SSS1.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS7.SSS1.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">(which is well-defined up to <math id="S5.SS7.SSS1.p2.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{C}}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{C}}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>). For those <math id="S5.SS7.SSS1.p2.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> near <math id="S5.SS7.SSS1.p2.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-1</annotation></semantics></math>, the frame <math id="S5.SS7.SSS1.p2.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> can be reconstructed from a frame on the component <math id="S5.SS7.SSS1.p2.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{pr}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{pr}</annotation></semantics></math> and a frame on <math id="S5.SS7.SSS1.p2.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{rq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{rq}</annotation></semantics></math> and one can interpolate between the normalization using from the <math id="S5.SS7.SSS1.p2.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-inner product on <math id="S5.SS7.SSS1.p2.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> and the normalization using the product construction. The situation of the interpolation near deeper strata can be iterated by a routine induction argument.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS7.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">5.7.2. </span>Collar structure</h4>

<div id="S5.SS7.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS7.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The outer-collaring provides an analogous collar structure as in the case of derived orbifold liftings. To save notations we would rather view the collar structure as being given by “interior” collars than “exterior” ones. Therefore, we have obtained a K-chart lift of a flow category over <math id="S5.SS7.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{P}}^{\rm Floer}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>Floer</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{P}}^{\rm Floer}</annotation></semantics></math> such that each chart <math id="S5.SS7.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{pq}=(G_{pq},V_{pq},E_{pq},S_{pq})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{pq}=(G_{pq},V_{pq},E_{pq},S_{pq})</annotation></semantics></math> has a system of collars</p>
<table id="S5.E49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vbox{\lx@xy@svg{\hbox{\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\kern 45.06264pt\hbox{\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\hbox{\vtop{\halign{\entry@#!@&amp;&amp;\entry@@#!@\cr&amp;&amp;\cr&amp;&amp;\crcr}}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern-45.06264pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{E_{pq}|_{\partial^{\alpha}V_{pq}}\times[0,\epsilon)^{{\mathbb{F}}_{\alpha}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 57.76045pt\raise 7.84723pt\hbox{{}\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise-2.37502pt\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\widehat{\theta}_{pq,\alpha}^{\rm collar}}$}}}\kern 3.0pt}}}}}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 99.11127pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise-24.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\kern 69.06264pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{}$}}}}}}}{\hbox{\kern 99.11127pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{E_{pq}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 110.35976pt\raise-25.57895pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\kern-37.24924pt\raise-32.91226pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{\partial^{\alpha}V_{pq}\times[0,\epsilon)^{{\mathbb{F}}_{\alpha}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 54.70273pt\raise-40.14337pt\hbox{{}\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise-2.25891pt\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\theta_{pq,\alpha}^{\rm collar}}$}}}\kern 3.0pt}}}}}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 99.06264pt\raise-32.91226pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\kern 69.06264pt\raise-32.91226pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{}$}}}}}}}{\hbox{\kern 99.06264pt\raise-32.91226pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{V_{pq}}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces}}}}},\ \forall\alpha\in{\mathbb{A}}_{pq}^{\rm Floer}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext> <svg style="vertical-align:-65.55209140716886px" height="87.27" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="62.35 65.55 230.69 87.27" width="230.69"> <g transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 62.35317189580955 87.26849205615659) translate(62.35,0)"> <g transform="translate(-62.35,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"> <foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:8.41em;--ltx-fo-height:0.84em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.37em;font-size:10pt;" height="16.76" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.64)" width="116.41"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></msup></mrow></span></span></foreignObject> </g> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 62.353193009396186 -0.27673578005007266 L 62.353193009396186 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <g transform="translate(79.92,0) translate(0,10.86) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.29)"> <foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.27em;--ltx-fo-height:0.72em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.41" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.99)" width="31.35"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.700em">θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.710em">q</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.710em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.710em">α</mi></mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">collar</mi></msubsup></span></span></foreignObject> </g> <g transform="translate(137.14,0)"> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> </g> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 62.353193009396186 -0.27673578005007266 L 137.14026164361943 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 137.14026164361943 -0.27673578005007266 L 137.14026164361943 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -12.727755637226286 L 0.27673578005007266 -12.727755637226286" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <g transform="translate(0,-33.21)"> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> </g> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -33.208800332088 L 0.27673578005007266 -12.727755637226286" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -33.208800332088 L 0.27673578005007266 -33.208800332088" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <g transform="translate(137.14,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"> <foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.65em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.41" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="22.83"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></span></span></foreignObject> </g> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 152.42806077415852 -11.569253138458645 L 152.98153233425867 -11.569253138458645" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <g transform="translate(152.71,0) translate(0,-35.39)"> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> </g> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 152.42806077415852 -35.39359205010291 L 152.98153233425867 -11.569253138458645" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 152.42806077415852 -35.39359205010291 L 152.98153233425867 -35.39359205010291" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <g transform="translate(-51.54,0) translate(0,-45.54) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"> <foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:6.85em;--ltx-fo-height:0.84em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="15.6" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.64)" width="94.78"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></msup></mrow></span></span></foreignObject> </g> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 51.54179094968305 -45.817433113508805 L 51.54179094968305 -45.263961553408656" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <g transform="translate(75.69,0) translate(0,-55.55) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.13)"> <foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.09em;--ltx-fo-height:0.65em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.2em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.71" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.98)" width="28.93"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.700em">θ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.710em">q</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.710em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.710em">α</mi></mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">collar</mi></msubsup></span></span></foreignObject> </g> <g transform="translate(137.07,0) translate(0,-45.54)"> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> </g> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 51.54179094968305 -45.817433113508805 L 137.07297264300755 -45.263961553408656" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 137.07297264300755 -45.817433113508805 L 137.07297264300755 -45.263961553408656" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <g transform="translate(137.07,0) translate(0,-45.54) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"> <foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.66em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.41" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="22.96"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></span></span></foreignObject> </g> </g> </svg> </mtext><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>𝔸</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>Floer</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vbox{\lx@xy@svg{\hbox{\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\kern 45.06264pt\hbox{\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\hbox{\vtop{\halign{\entry@#!@&amp;&amp;\entry@@#!@\cr&amp;&amp;\cr&amp;&amp;\crcr}}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern-45.06264pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{E_{pq}|_{\partial^{\alpha}V_{pq}}\times[0,\epsilon)^{{\mathbb{F}}_{\alpha}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 57.76045pt\raise 7.84723pt\hbox{{}\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise-2.37502pt\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\widehat{\theta}_{pq,\alpha}^{\rm collar}}$}}}\kern 3.0pt}}}}}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 99.11127pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise-24.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\kern 69.06264pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{}$}}}}}}}{\hbox{\kern 99.11127pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{E_{pq}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 110.35976pt\raise-25.57895pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\kern-37.24924pt\raise-32.91226pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{\partial^{\alpha}V_{pq}\times[0,\epsilon)^{{\mathbb{F}}_{\alpha}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 54.70273pt\raise-40.14337pt\hbox{{}\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise-2.25891pt\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\theta_{pq,\alpha}^{\rm collar}}$}}}\kern 3.0pt}}}}}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 99.06264pt\raise-32.91226pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\kern 69.06264pt\raise-32.91226pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{}$}}}}}}}{\hbox{\kern 99.06264pt\raise-32.91226pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{V_{pq}}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces}}}}},\ \forall\alpha\in{\mathbb{A}}_{pq}^{\rm Floer}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5.49)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS7.SSS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">which are compatible in a sense similar to the requirements of collar structures of a derived orbifold lift stated in Definition <a href="#S3.Thmthm26" title="Definition 3.26. ‣ 3.5.1. Collar structure ‣ 3.5. Additional structures ‣ 3. Abstract constructions of chain complexes and maps over the integers ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.26</span></a>, where one needs to replace the notions for derived orbifold charts by the ones for K-charts, with extra care taken on the equivariance with respect to the Lie group actions. The readers are invited to fill in the details.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS8" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.8. </span>Constructing scaffolding</h3>

<div id="S5.SS8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The stabilization map constructed previously describes the relation between a product chart and the corresponding stratum of a larger thickened moduli space. However, to inductively construct the FOP perturbations, we need to specify such stabilization maps in all such situations and we require that the stabilization maps are compatible in some natural way. Such a requirement was packaged in terms of the notion “scaffolding” for derived orbifold lifts of a flow category and in particular, in the smooth category (see Definition <a href="#S3.Thmthm28" title="Definition 3.28. ‣ 3.5.2. Scaffolding ‣ 3.5. Additional structures ‣ 3. Abstract constructions of chain complexes and maps over the integers ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.28</span></a> and Definition <a href="#S3.Thmthm29" title="Definition 3.29. ‣ 3.5.2. Scaffolding ‣ 3.5. Additional structures ‣ 3. Abstract constructions of chain complexes and maps over the integers ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.29</span></a>). In our construction of the derived orbifold lift of <math id="S5.SS8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(T^{\rm Floer})^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>Floer</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(T^{\rm Floer})^{+}</annotation></semantics></math>, we need a scaffolding-like structure to do smoothing. Hence, we first need such structures in the topological category, also in the equivariant setting but not in the orbifold setting. Below we state what we can construct in this setting; its proof is given in Appendix <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C A proof sketch of Proposition ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a>. Just as (<a href="#S5.E49" title="In 5.7.2. Collar structure ‣ 5.7. Outer collaring ‣ 5. Global Kuranishi charts on Floer moduli spaces ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.49</span></a>), we simplify the notations by pretending that the K-charts are equipped with interior collars. The reader should keep in mind that the following proposition holds only after taking the outer-collaring. In the sequel, the resulting structure from the following proposition will be referred to as a <span id="S5.SS8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">collared scaffolding</span>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmthm64" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmthm64.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 5.64</span></span><span id="S5.Thmthm64.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmthm64.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmthm64.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmthm64.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There exist the following objects.</span></p>
<ol id="S5.I26" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S5.I26.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S5.I26.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I26.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I26.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For each </span><math id="S5.I26.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="pq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">pq</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I26.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and each integer </span><math id="S5.I26.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq d_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq d_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I26.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, a </span><math id="S5.I26.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I26.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-invariant inner product on the bundle </span><math id="S5.I26.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{pq}^{(d)}\to V_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{pq}^{(d)}\to V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I26.i1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. To state the next class of objects, introduce the following notions. Let </span><math id="S5.I26.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{pq,\alpha}\subset O_{pq}|_{V_{\alpha}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{pq,\alpha}\subset O_{pq}|_{V_{\alpha}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I26.i1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> be the orthogonal complement of </span><math id="S5.I26.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{\alpha}\to V_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{\alpha}\to V_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I26.i1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and let </span><math id="S5.I26.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{pq,\alpha}\subset Q_{pq}|_{V_{\alpha}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{pq,\alpha}\subset Q_{pq}|_{V_{\alpha}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I26.i1.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> be the orthogonal complement of </span><math id="S5.I26.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\alpha}\to V_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\alpha}\to V_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I26.i1.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> (with resepct to the trivial inner product on </span><math id="S5.I26.i1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I26.i1.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">). Denote</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex237" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex237.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{pq,\alpha}:=O_{pq,\alpha}\oplus Q_{pq,\alpha}\subset E_{pq}|_{V_{\alpha}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{pq,\alpha}:=O_{pq,\alpha}\oplus Q_{pq,\alpha}\subset E_{pq}|_{V_{\alpha}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.I26.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I26.i1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and its equivariantization</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex238" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex238.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{pq,\alpha}^{\sim}:=G_{pq}\times_{G_{\alpha}}F_{pq,\alpha}\subset E_{pq}|_{V_{\alpha}^{\sim}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>∼</mo></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>α</mi><mo>∼</mo></msubsup></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{pq,\alpha}^{\sim}:=G_{pq}\times_{G_{\alpha}}F_{pq,\alpha}\subset E_{pq}|_{V_{\alpha}^{\sim}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I26.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S5.I26.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I26.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I26.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For each stratum </span><math id="S5.I26.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I26.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, a stratified topological embedding over the poset </span><math id="S5.I26.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{\alpha}{\mathbb{A}}^{\rm Floer}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><msubsup><mi>𝔸</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>Floer</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{\alpha}{\mathbb{A}}^{\rm Floer}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="S5.E50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{pq,\alpha}:{\rm Stab}_{F_{pq,\alpha}}(V_{\alpha})\hookrightarrow\partial^{\alpha}V_{pq}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Stab</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">↪</mo><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{pq,\alpha}:{\rm Stab}_{F_{pq,\alpha}}(V_{\alpha})\hookrightarrow\partial^{\alpha}V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5.50)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.I26.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I26.i2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">whose restriction to </span><math id="S5.I26.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I26.i2.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> coincides with the embedding </span><math id="S5.I26.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota_{pq,\alpha}:V_{\alpha}\hookrightarrow\partial^{\alpha}V_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ι</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">↪</mo><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota_{pq,\alpha}:V_{\alpha}\hookrightarrow\partial^{\alpha}V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I26.i2.p1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> such that its equivariantization</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex239" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex239.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{pq,\alpha}^{\sim}:{\rm Stab}_{F_{pq,\alpha}^{\sim}}(V_{\alpha}^{\sim})\to\partial^{\alpha}V_{pq}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>∼</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Stab</mi><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>∼</mo></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>α</mi><mo>∼</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{pq,\alpha}^{\sim}:{\rm Stab}_{F_{pq,\alpha}^{\sim}}(V_{\alpha}^{\sim})\to\partial^{\alpha}V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.I26.i2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I26.i2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">is an open embedding. This embedding induces a projection map</span></p>
<table id="S5.E51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{pq,\alpha}:\partial^{\alpha}V_{pq}\to V_{\alpha}^{\sim}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.111em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>α</mi><mo>∼</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{pq,\alpha}:\partial^{\alpha}V_{pq}\to V_{\alpha}^{\sim}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5.51)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I26.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S5.I26.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I26.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I26.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For each </span><math id="S5.I26.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq d_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq d_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I26.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, an equivariant bundle isomorphism</span></p>
<table id="S5.E52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\theta}_{pq,\alpha}^{(d),\sim}:\pi_{pq,\alpha}^{*}\Big(O_{pq}^{(d)}|_{V_{\alpha}^{\sim}}\Big)\cong O_{pq}^{(d)}|_{\partial^{\alpha}V_{pq}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em">∼</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>α</mi><mo>∼</mo></msubsup></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≅</mo><msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\theta}_{pq,\alpha}^{(d),\sim}:\pi_{pq,\alpha}^{*}\Big(O_{pq}^{(d)}|_{V_{\alpha}^{\sim}}\Big)\cong O_{pq}^{(d)}|_{\partial^{\alpha}V_{pq}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5.52)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S5.Thmthm64.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmthm64.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">These objects need to satisfy the following list of conditions.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmthm64.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S5.I27" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S5.I27.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(A1)</span> 
<div id="S5.I27.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I27.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I27.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For all </span><math id="S5.I27.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="pq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">pq</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I27.ix1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="S5.I27.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{\prime}&gt;d\geq d_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{\prime}&gt;d\geq d_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I27.ix1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, the inclusion </span><math id="S5.I27.ix1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{pq}^{(d)}\hookrightarrow O_{pq}^{(d^{\prime})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">↪</mo><msubsup><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{pq}^{(d)}\hookrightarrow O_{pq}^{(d^{\prime})}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I27.ix1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> (</span><a href="#S5.E34" title="In 5.3.3. Multi-layered thickening ‣ 5.3. Global chart construction II ‣ 5. Global Kuranishi charts on Floer moduli spaces ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.34</span></a><span id="S5.I27.ix1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">) is isometric.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I27.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(A2)</span> 
<div id="S5.I27.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I27.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I27.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For each stratum </span><math id="S5.I27.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\alpha=pr_{1}\cdots r_{l}q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=pr_{1}\cdots r_{l}q</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I27.ix2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> of </span><math id="S5.I27.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="pq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">pq</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I27.ix2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, the bundle embedding</span></p>
<table id="S5.E53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\iota}_{pq,\alpha}^{(d),\sim}:O_{pq,\alpha}^{(d)}\hookrightarrow O_{pq}^{(d)}|_{\partial^{\alpha}V_{pq}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ι</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em">∼</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>O</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">↪</mo><msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\iota}_{pq,\alpha}^{(d),\sim}:O_{pq,\alpha}^{(d)}\hookrightarrow O_{pq}^{(d)}|_{\partial^{\alpha}V_{pq}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5.53)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.I27.ix2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I27.ix2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">is isometric. By Lemma </span><a href="#S5.Thmthm65" title="Lemma 5.65. ‣ 5.8. Constructing scaffolding ‣ 5. Global Kuranishi charts on Floer moduli spaces ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.65</span></a><span id="S5.I27.ix2.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> below, it follows that, for any intermediate stratum </span><math id="S5.I27.ix2.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\beta=ps_{1}\cdots s_{m}q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=ps_{1}\cdots s_{m}q</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I27.ix2.p1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> between </span><math id="S5.I27.ix2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I27.ix2.p1.2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="S5.I27.ix2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="pq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">pq</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I27.ix2.p1.2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, the following is true. Abbreviate </span><math id="S5.I27.ix2.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\alpha_{0}=pr_{1}\cdots s_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{0}=pr_{1}\cdots s_{1}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I27.ix2.p1.2.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="S5.I27.ix2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ldots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ldots</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I27.ix2.p1.2.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="S5.I27.ix2.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\alpha_{m}=s_{m}\cdots r_{l}q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{m}=s_{m}\cdots r_{l}q</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I27.ix2.p1.2.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> as strata of </span><math id="S5.I27.ix2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ps_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ps_{1}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I27.ix2.p1.2.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="S5.I27.ix2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cdots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⋯</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cdots</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I27.ix2.p1.2.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="S5.I27.ix2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{m}q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{m}q</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I27.ix2.p1.2.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> respectively. Then</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex240" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex240.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{pq,\alpha}\cong O_{pq,\beta}|_{V_{\alpha}}\oplus\left(O_{ps_{1},\alpha_{0}}\boxplus\cdots\boxplus O_{s_{m}q,\alpha_{m}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≅</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></msub><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo>⊞</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>⊞</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{pq,\alpha}\cong O_{pq,\beta}|_{V_{\alpha}}\oplus\left(O_{ps_{1},\alpha_{0}}\boxplus\cdots\boxplus O_{s_{m}q,\alpha_{m}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.I27.ix2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I27.ix2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(We explain the notations here. The bundles </span><math id="S5.I27.ix2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{ps_{1},\alpha_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{ps_{1},\alpha_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I27.ix2.p1.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> etc. in the second summand above are subbundles of </span><math id="S5.I27.ix2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{ps_{1}}|_{V_{\alpha_{0}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{ps_{1}}|_{V_{\alpha_{0}}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I27.ix2.p1.3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> etc. Their product is a subbundle of </span><math id="S5.I27.ix2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{pq}|_{V_{\alpha}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{pq}|_{V_{\alpha}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I27.ix2.p1.3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.) It implies that the bundle </span><math id="S5.I27.ix2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{pq,\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{pq,\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I27.ix2.p1.3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is stratified (linearly) by all strata between </span><math id="S5.I27.ix2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I27.ix2.p1.3.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and the top stratum, where the stratum corresponding to the intermediate stratum </span><math id="S5.I27.ix2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I27.ix2.p1.3.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is the subbundle</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex241" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex241.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{\beta\alpha}:=O_{ps_{1},\alpha_{0}}\boxplus\cdots\boxplus O_{s_{m}q,\alpha_{m}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo>⊞</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>⊞</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{\beta\alpha}:=O_{ps_{1},\alpha_{0}}\boxplus\cdots\boxplus O_{s_{m}q,\alpha_{m}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S5.I27.ix2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I27.ix2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I27.ix2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Similarly, the bundle </span><math id="S5.I27.ix2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{pq,\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{pq,\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I27.ix2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is also stratified by subbundles </span><math id="S5.I27.ix2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\beta\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\beta\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I27.ix2.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> where</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex242" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex242.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\beta\alpha}=Q_{ps_{1},\alpha_{0}}\boxplus\cdots\boxplus Q_{s_{m}q,\alpha_{m}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo>⊞</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>⊞</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\beta\alpha}=Q_{ps_{1},\alpha_{0}}\boxplus\cdots\boxplus Q_{s_{m}q,\alpha_{m}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.I27.ix2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I27.ix2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Denote</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex243" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex243.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\beta\alpha}:=O_{\beta\alpha}\oplus Q_{\beta\alpha}\subset F_{pq,\alpha}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\beta\alpha}:=O_{\beta\alpha}\oplus Q_{\beta\alpha}\subset F_{pq,\alpha}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.I27.ix2.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I27.ix2.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then there is a splitting</span></p>
<table id="S5.E54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{pq,\alpha}=F_{pq,\beta}|_{V_{\alpha}}\oplus F_{\beta\alpha}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{pq,\alpha}=F_{pq,\beta}|_{V_{\alpha}}\oplus F_{\beta\alpha}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5.54)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I27.ix3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(B1)</span> 
<div id="S5.I27.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I27.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I27.ix3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The stabilization maps are stratum-preserving, i.e., for any intermediate stratum </span><math id="S5.I27.ix3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I27.ix3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> between </span><math id="S5.I27.ix3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I27.ix3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and the top stratum, there holds</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex244" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex244.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{pq,\alpha}\Big({\rm Stab}_{F_{\beta\alpha}}(V_{\alpha})\Big)\subset\partial^{\alpha}V_{\beta}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Stab</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">⊂</mo><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>β</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{pq,\alpha}\Big({\rm Stab}_{F_{\beta\alpha}}(V_{\alpha})\Big)\subset\partial^{\alpha}V_{\beta},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.I27.ix3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I27.ix3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where </span><math id="S5.I27.ix3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\beta\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\beta\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I27.ix3.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is viewed as a subbundle of </span><math id="S5.I27.ix3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{pq,\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{pq,\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I27.ix3.p1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> under the splitting (</span><a href="#S5.E54" title="In item (A2) ‣ Proposition 5.64. ‣ 5.8. Constructing scaffolding ‣ 5. Global Kuranishi charts on Floer moduli spaces ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.54</span></a><span id="S5.I27.ix3.p1.2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">), and the space </span><math id="S5.I27.ix3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I27.ix3.p1.2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is identified with its image in </span><math id="S5.I27.ix3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{\beta}V_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>β</mi></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{\beta}V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I27.ix3.p1.2.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> under </span><math id="S5.I27.ix3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota_{pq,\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ι</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota_{pq,\beta}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I27.ix3.p1.2.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I27.ix4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(B2)</span> 
<div id="S5.I27.ix4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I27.ix4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I27.ix4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The above restriction of the stabilization map coincides with the product of stabilization maps. More precisely this means the following. Abbreviate </span><math id="S5.I27.ix4.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\alpha_{0}=pr_{1}\cdots s_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{0}=pr_{1}\cdots s_{1}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I27.ix4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="S5.I27.ix4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ldots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ldots</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I27.ix4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="S5.I27.ix4.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\alpha_{m}=s_{m}\cdots r_{l}q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{m}=s_{m}\cdots r_{l}q</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I27.ix4.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> as strata of </span><math id="S5.I27.ix4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ps_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ps_{1}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I27.ix4.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="S5.I27.ix4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cdots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⋯</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cdots</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I27.ix4.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="S5.I27.ix4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{m}q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{m}q</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I27.ix4.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> respectively. The stabilization maps </span><math id="S5.I27.ix4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{ps_{1},\alpha_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{ps_{1},\alpha_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I27.ix4.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="S5.I27.ix4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cdots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⋯</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cdots</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I27.ix4.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="S5.I27.ix4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{s_{m}q,\alpha_{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{s_{m}q,\alpha_{m}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I27.ix4.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> are germs of homeomorphisms</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex245" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex245.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{ps_{1},\alpha_{0}}:{\rm Stab}_{F_{ps_{1},\alpha_{0}}}(V_{\alpha_{0}})\to\partial^{\alpha_{0}}V_{ps_{1}},\ \cdots,\ \theta_{s_{m}q,\alpha_{m}}:{\rm Stab}_{F_{s_{m}q,\alpha_{m}}}(V_{\alpha_{m}})\to\partial^{\alpha_{m}}V_{s_{m}q}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Stab</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.389em">,</mo><mo rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Stab</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{ps_{1},\alpha_{0}}:{\rm Stab}_{F_{ps_{1},\alpha_{0}}}(V_{\alpha_{0}})\to\partial^{\alpha_{0}}V_{ps_{1}},\ \cdots,\ \theta_{s_{m}q,\alpha_{m}}:{\rm Stab}_{F_{s_{m}q,\alpha_{m}}}(V_{\alpha_{m}})\to\partial^{\alpha_{m}}V_{s_{m}q}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.I27.ix4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I27.ix4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Their product gives a germ of homeomorphisms</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex246" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex246.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\rm Stab}_{F_{ps_{1},\alpha_{0}}\boxplus\cdots\boxplus F_{s_{m}q,\alpha_{m}}}(V_{\alpha})\to\partial^{\alpha_{0}}V_{ps_{1}}\times\cdots\times\partial^{\alpha_{m}}V_{s_{m}q}\hookrightarrow\partial^{\alpha}V_{pq}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Stab</mi><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo>⊞</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>⊞</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.055em">⋯</mo><mo rspace="0.055em">×</mo><msup><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">↪</mo><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm Stab}_{F_{ps_{1},\alpha_{0}}\boxplus\cdots\boxplus F_{s_{m}q,\alpha_{m}}}(V_{\alpha})\to\partial^{\alpha_{0}}V_{ps_{1}}\times\cdots\times\partial^{\alpha_{m}}V_{s_{m}q}\hookrightarrow\partial^{\alpha}V_{pq}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.I27.ix4.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I27.ix4.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Notice that the left hand side is just </span><math id="S5.I27.ix4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm Stab}_{F_{\beta\alpha}}(V_{\alpha})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Stab</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm Stab}_{F_{\beta\alpha}}(V_{\alpha})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I27.ix4.p1.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. We require that</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex247" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex247.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\theta_{pr_{1},\alpha_{0}}\times\cdots\times\theta_{s_{m}q,\alpha_{m}}=\theta_{pq,\alpha}|_{{\rm Stab}_{F_{\beta\alpha}}(V_{\alpha})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.055em">⋯</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>θ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>θ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Stab</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{pr_{1},\alpha_{0}}\times\cdots\times\theta_{s_{m}q,\alpha_{m}}=\theta_{pq,\alpha}|_{{\rm Stab}_{F_{\beta\alpha}}(V_{\alpha})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.I27.ix4.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I27.ix4.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(Compare this conditions with the conditions in Definition </span><a href="#S3.Thmthm29" title="Definition 3.29. ‣ 3.5.2. Scaffolding ‣ 3.5. Additional structures ‣ 3. Abstract constructions of chain complexes and maps over the integers ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.29</span></a><span id="S5.I27.ix4.p1.4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">).</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I27.ix5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(C1)</span> 
<div id="S5.I27.ix5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I27.ix5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I27.ix5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The bundle isomorphisms satisfy the following commutative diagram for all </span><math id="S5.I27.ix5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d&lt;d^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d&lt;d^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I27.ix5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex248" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
