<div id="S5.Thmthm65" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmthm65.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5.65</span></span><span id="S5.Thmthm65.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmthm65.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmthm65.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmthm65.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose the bundles <math id="S5.Thmthm65.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{pq}^{(d)}\to V_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{pq}^{(d)}\to V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> are equipped with <math id="S5.Thmthm65.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>-invariant inner products which satisfy conditions (A1) and (A3) of Proposition <a href="#S5.Thmthm64" title="Proposition 5.64. ‣ 5.8. Constructing scaffolding ‣ 5. Global Kuranishi charts on Floer moduli spaces ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.64</span></a>. Then the following is true. Consider a pair of strata <math id="S5.Thmthm65.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha,\beta\in{\mathbb{A}}_{pq}^{\rm Floer}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>𝔸</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>Floer</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha,\beta\in{\mathbb{A}}_{pq}^{\rm Floer}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S5.Thmthm65.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\alpha=pr_{1}\cdots r_{l}q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=pr_{1}\cdots r_{l}q</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.Thmthm65.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\beta=ps_{1}\cdots s_{m}q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=ps_{1}\cdots s_{m}q</annotation></semantics></math>. Denote <math id="S5.Thmthm65.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\alpha_{0}=pr_{1}\cdots s_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{0}=pr_{1}\cdots s_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.Thmthm65.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ldots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ldots</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.Thmthm65.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\alpha_{m}=s_{m}\cdots r_{l}q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{m}=s_{m}\cdots r_{l}q</annotation></semantics></math>. Consider the bundles</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex258" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex258.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{ps_{1},\alpha_{0}}\to V_{\alpha_{0}},\ \cdots,\ O_{s_{m}q,\alpha_{m}}\to V_{\alpha_{m}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.389em">,</mo><mo rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{ps_{1},\alpha_{0}}\to V_{\alpha_{0}},\ \cdots,\ O_{s_{m}q,\alpha_{m}}\to V_{\alpha_{m}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.Thmthm65.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmthm65.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">whose product is a subbundle</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex259" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex259.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{\beta\alpha}\subset O_{pq}|_{V_{\alpha}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{\beta\alpha}\subset O_{pq}|_{V_{\alpha}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.Thmthm65.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmthm65.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then as subbundles of <math id="S5.Thmthm65.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{pq}|_{V_{\alpha}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{pq}|_{V_{\alpha}}</annotation></semantics></math>, one has</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex260" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex260.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{pq,\alpha}=O_{pq,\beta}|_{V_{\alpha}}\oplus O_{\beta\alpha}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{pq,\alpha}=O_{pq,\beta}|_{V_{\alpha}}\oplus O_{\beta\alpha}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS8.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S5.SS8.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS8.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS8.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Linear algebra.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S6" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">6. </span>Smoothing</h2>

<div id="S6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we use equivariant (relative) smoothing theory to equip the K-chart presentation of various moduli spaces constructed in Section <a href="#S5" title="5. Global Kuranishi charts on Floer moduli spaces ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> with smooth structures after stabilization. The proof is based on induction, which is quite similar to the construction of straightening and coherent FOP perturbations discussed in Section <a href="#S3" title="3. Abstract constructions of chain complexes and maps over the integers ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> and Section <a href="#S4" title="4. Proof of the integral Arnold conjecture ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>. After taking the associated quotient orbifold of the smooth K-chart presentation, we obtain a derived orbifold lift of the Hamiltonian Floer flow category <math id="S6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\rm Floer}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>Floer</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\rm Floer}</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, we explain how to construct a normal complex structure on the resulting derived orbifold lift.</p>
</div>
<section id="S6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.1. </span>Preliminaries</h3>

<div id="S6.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We list out some basic notions relevant for the smoothing theory in this subsection. Then we state the relative smoothing statement Theorem <a href="#S6.Thmthm10" title="Theorem 6.10. ‣ 6.1.2. Stable equivariant smoothings ‣ 6.1. Preliminaries ‣ 6. Smoothing ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.10</span></a> which will proved in Appendix <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B Relative stable equivariant smoothing ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a>. Following that, some elementary technical results in the smoothing construction will be proved.</p>
</div>
<section id="S6.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">6.1.1. </span>Microbundles</h4>

<div id="S6.SS1.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We start by discussing some notions and facts about microbundles and their roles in smoothing theory.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmthm1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmthm1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 6.1</span></span><span id="S6.Thmthm1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmthm1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmthm1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S6.Thmthm1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> be a topological space.</p>
<ol id="S6.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S6.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S6.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A <span id="S6.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">microbundle</span> (of rank <math id="S6.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>) over <math id="S6.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> is a diagram</p>
<table id="S6.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S6.Ex1.m1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_markedasmath" height="21.97" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-7.610350076103501px" version="1.1" viewBox="10.43 7.61 125.84 21.97" width="125.84"><g transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 10.425783513376487 21.96621660607574) translate(0,3.46) translate(10.43,0)"><g transform="translate(-10.43,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.91em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.46" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="12.55"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S6.Ex1.m1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{X\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{X\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 10.425783513376487 -0.27673578005007266 L 10.425783513376487 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(19.48,0) translate(0,6.24) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-2.09)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.38em;--ltx-fo-height:0.3em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="4.17" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 4.17)" width="5.22"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S6.Ex1.m1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.700em">s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{s}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(43.64,0)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 10.425783513376487 -0.27673578005007266 L 43.63458384546449 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 43.63458384546449 -0.27673578005007266 L 43.63458384546449 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(43.64,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.68em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.46" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="9.42"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S6.Ex1.m1.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{{\mathscr{E}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℰ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{{\mathscr{E}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 61.35365470441789 -0.27673578005007266 L 61.35365470441789 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(71.74,0) translate(0,7.18) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-1.14)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.41em;--ltx-fo-height:0.3em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.14em;font-size:10pt;" height="6.05" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 4.17)" width="5.7"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S6.Ex1.m1.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.700em">p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{p}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(94.56,0)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 61.35365470441789 -0.27673578005007266 L 94.5624550365059 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 94.5624550365059 -0.27673578005007266 L 94.5624550365059 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(94.56,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.91em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.46" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="12.55"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S6.Ex1.m1.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{X}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I1.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S6.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathscr{E}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℰ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathscr{E}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a topological space, <math id="S6.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> are continuous maps satisfying</p>
<ol id="S6.I1.i1.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S6.I1.i1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(a)</span> 
<div id="S6.I1.i1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I1.i1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S6.I1.i1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\circ s={\rm Id}_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>Id</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\circ s={\rm Id}_{X}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I1.i1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(b)</span> 
<div id="S6.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">for each <math id="S6.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in X</annotation></semantics></math> there exist a neighborhood <math id="S6.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{x}\subset X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{x}\subset X</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S6.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, a neighborhood <math id="S6.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathscr{V}}_{x}\subset{\mathscr{E}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒱</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℰ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathscr{V}}_{x}\subset{\mathscr{E}}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S6.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, and a homeomorphism</p>
<table id="S6.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{x}:U_{x}\times{\mathbb{R}}^{n}\to{\mathscr{V}}_{x}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒱</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{x}:U_{x}\times{\mathbb{R}}^{n}\to{\mathscr{V}}_{x}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">for which <math id="S6.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\circ h_{x}={\rm pr}_{U_{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>pr</mi><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\circ h_{x}={\rm pr}_{U_{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{x}|_{U_{x}\times\{0\}}=s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{x}|_{U_{x}\times\{0\}}=s</annotation></semantics></math>. Here <math id="S6.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm pr}_{U_{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>pr</mi><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm pr}_{U_{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the natural projection onto the factor <math id="S6.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{x}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S6.I1.i1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Often we use a single symbol <math id="S6.I1.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathscr{E}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℰ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathscr{E}}</annotation></semantics></math> to denote a microbundle.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S6.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given two microbundles over <math id="S6.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> (not necessarily of the same rank)</p>
<table id="S6.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.EGx19.1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
