<p id="S6.Thmthm25.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Assume that these data satisfy the following compatibility condition.</p>
<ol id="S6.I11" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S6.I11.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(A)</span> 
<div id="S6.I11.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I11.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each triple of strata <math id="S6.I11.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\leq\beta\leq\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\leq\beta\leq\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> one has <math id="S6.I11.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{\gamma\beta}\circ\phi_{\beta\alpha}=\phi_{\gamma\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{\gamma\beta}\circ\phi_{\beta\alpha}=\phi_{\gamma\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I11.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(B)</span> 
<div id="S6.I11.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I11.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The bundle embeddings are induced from products. Namely, given a stratum <math id="S6.I11.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\alpha=pr_{1}\cdots r_{l}q\in{\mathbb{A}}^{\mathcal{P}}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝔸</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=pr_{1}\cdots r_{l}q\in{\mathbb{A}}^{\mathcal{P}}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exist equivariant isometric linear embeddings</p>
<table id="S6.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{r_{i}r_{i+1}}:R_{r_{i}r_{i+1}}\hookrightarrow R_{pq}\text{ for }i=0,\dots,l" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">↪</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> for </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{r_{i}r_{i+1}}:R_{r_{i}r_{i+1}}\hookrightarrow R_{pq}\text{ for }i=0,\dots,l</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I11.ix2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">with respect to the group embeddings <math id="S6.I11.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{r_{i}r_{i+1}}\hookrightarrow G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">↪</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{r_{i}r_{i+1}}\hookrightarrow G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="S6.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\phi_{pq,\alpha}=\phi_{pq,pr_{1}}\times\cdots\times\phi_{pq,r_{l}q}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.055em">⋯</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{pq,\alpha}=\phi_{pq,pr_{1}}\times\cdots\times\phi_{pq,r_{l}q},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I11.ix2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">and <math id="S6.I11.ix2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{\beta\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{\beta\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> for a general pair <math id="S6.I11.ix2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\leq\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\leq\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> is constructed similarly using the corresponding factorization.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS2.SSS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.SSS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Given a stabilization containing <math id="S6.SS2.SSS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{{\bm{R}}_{pq}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{{\bm{R}}_{pq}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS2.SSS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\phi_{\beta\alpha}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\phi_{\beta\alpha}\}</annotation></semantics></math> we can define another K-chart lift for <math id="S6.SS2.SSS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\mathcal{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>T</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\mathcal{P}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Its collection of Kuranishi charts are</p>
<table id="S6.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{K}_{pq}:=(G_{pq},\widehat{V}_{pq},\widehat{E}_{pq},\widehat{S}_{pq}):={\rm Stab}_{R_{pq}}(K_{pq});" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Stab</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>;</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{K}_{pq}:=(G_{pq},\widehat{V}_{pq},\widehat{E}_{pq},\widehat{S}_{pq}):={\rm Stab}_{R_{pq}}(K_{pq});</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS2.SSS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">its collection of chart embeddings</p>
<table id="S6.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\bm{\iota}}_{prq}:\widehat{K}_{pr}\times\widehat{K}_{rq}\to\partial^{prq}\widehat{K}_{pq}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜾</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\bm{\iota}}_{prq}:\widehat{K}_{pr}\times\widehat{K}_{rq}\to\partial^{prq}\widehat{K}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS2.SSS3.p2.3" class="ltx_p">are defined as follows. Given <math id="S6.SS2.SSS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{pr},e_{pr})\in\widehat{V}_{pr}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{pr},e_{pr})\in\widehat{V}_{pr}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.SS2.SSS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{rq},e_{rq})\in\widehat{V}_{rq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{rq},e_{rq})\in\widehat{V}_{rq}</annotation></semantics></math>, define</p>
<table id="S6.Ex48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\iota}_{prq}((x_{pr},e_{pr}),(x_{rq},e_{rq}))=(\iota_{prq}(x_{pr},x_{rq}),\phi_{pq,prq}(e_{pr},e_{rq}))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ι</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ι</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\iota}_{prq}((x_{pr},e_{pr}),(x_{rq},e_{rq}))=(\iota_{prq}(x_{pr},x_{rq}),\phi_{pq,prq}(e_{pr},e_{rq}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS2.SSS3.p2.4" class="ltx_p">which is clearly equivariant with respect to the group map <math id="S6.SS2.SSS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pr}\times G_{rq}\to G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pr}\times G_{rq}\to G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmthm26" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmthm26.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 6.26</span></span><span id="S6.Thmthm26.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmthm26.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmthm26.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmthm26.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The data <math id="S6.Thmthm26.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\widehat{K}_{pq}\}_{p&lt;q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\widehat{K}_{pq}\}_{p&lt;q}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S6.Thmthm26.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\widehat{\bm{\iota}}_{prq}\}_{p&lt;r&lt;q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝛊</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\widehat{\bm{\iota}}_{prq}\}_{p&lt;r&lt;q}</annotation></semantics></math> is a K-chart lift of <math id="S6.Thmthm26.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\mathcal{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>T</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\mathcal{P}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS2.SSS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S6.SS2.SSS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.SSS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS2.SSS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">This follows directly from the definition.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS2.SSS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.SSS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We need to equip a stabilization certain extra structures.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmthm27" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmthm27.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 6.27</span></span><span id="S6.Thmthm27.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmthm27.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmthm27.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Suppose the K-chart lift <math id="S6.Thmthm27.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathfrak{K}}^{\mathcal{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔎</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathfrak{K}}^{\mathcal{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> is equipped with a collar structure. Then a stabilization is called <span id="S6.Thmthm27.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">collared</span> if there are equivariant bundle isomorphisms</p>
<table id="S6.Ex49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S6.Ex49.m1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_markedasmath" height="69.44" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-57.10995047191738px" version="1.1" viewBox="62.15 57.11 188.78 69.44" width="188.78"><g transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 62.15381741078378 69.4418474732881) translate(0,3.46) translate(62.15,0)"><g transform="translate(-62.15,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:8.38em;--ltx-fo-height:0.84em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.37em;font-size:10pt;" height="16.76" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.64)" width="116.01"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S6.Ex49.m1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\textstyle{R_{pq}|_{\partial^{\alpha}V_{pq}}\times[0,\epsilon)^{{\mathbb{F}}_{\alpha}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{R_{pq}|_{\partial^{\alpha}V_{pq}}\times[0,\epsilon)^{{\mathbb{F}}_{\alpha}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 62.15381741078378 -0.27673578005007266 L 62.15381741078378 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(95.