</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS2.SSS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.SSS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Note that although our stabilization is constructed using product bundles, the stabilization maps are not necessarily induced from the linear maps between the representations. Therefore, the above definition is not entirely superfluous.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS2.SSS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.SSS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">We will also use not-necessarily-trivial inner products on those trivial bundles <math id="S6.SS2.SSS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> in the construction.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmthm28" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmthm28.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 6.28</span></span><span id="S6.Thmthm28.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmthm28.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmthm28.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S6.Thmthm28.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathfrak{K}}^{\mathcal{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔎</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathfrak{K}}^{\mathcal{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> be a K-chart lift of <math id="S6.Thmthm28.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\mathcal{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>T</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\mathcal{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> equipped with a collar structure and a collared stabilization <math id="S6.Thmthm28.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathfrak{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℜ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathfrak{R}}</annotation></semantics></math>. A <span id="S6.Thmthm28.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">collared system of inner products</span> on <math id="S6.Thmthm28.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathfrak{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℜ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathfrak{R}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a collection of <math id="S6.Thmthm28.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant inner products on the bundle <math id="S6.Thmthm28.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<ol id="S6.I12" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S6.I12.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S6.I12.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I12.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All the embeddings <math id="S6.I12.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{\beta\alpha}:R_{\alpha}\to R_{\beta}|_{\partial^{\alpha}V_{\beta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>β</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{\beta\alpha}:R_{\alpha}\to R_{\beta}|_{\partial^{\alpha}V_{\beta}}</annotation></semantics></math> are isometric.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I12.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S6.I12.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I12.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The collar isomorphisms are isometric.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS2.SSS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.SSS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Suppose <math id="S6.SS2.SSS3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathfrak{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℜ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathfrak{R}}</annotation></semantics></math> is equipped with a collared system of inner products. Then define</p>
<table id="S6.Ex51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\beta\alpha}\subset R_{\beta}|_{V_{\alpha}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\beta\alpha}\subset R_{\beta}|_{V_{\alpha}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS2.SSS3.p7.2" class="ltx_p">to be the orthogonal complement of <math id="S6.SS2.SSS3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S6.SS2.SSS3.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\beta}|_{V_{\alpha}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\beta}|_{V_{\alpha}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then by basic linear algebra one can see that whenever <math id="S6.SS2.SSS3.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\leq\beta\leq\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\leq\beta\leq\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, as subbundles of <math id="S6.SS2.SSS3.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\gamma}|_{V_{\alpha}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\gamma}|_{V_{\alpha}}</annotation></semantics></math>, one has</p>
<table id="S6.Ex52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\gamma\alpha}=R_{\gamma\beta}|_{V_{\alpha}}\oplus R_{\beta\alpha}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\gamma\alpha}=R_{\gamma\beta}|_{V_{\alpha}}\oplus R_{\beta\alpha}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS2.SSS3.p7.3" class="ltx_p">Then the original scaffolding can be extended to include the extra pieces <math id="S6.SS2.SSS3.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\beta\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\beta\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>. Indeed, define</p>
<table id="S6.Ex53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{F}_{\beta\alpha}:=\pi^{*}F_{\beta\alpha}\oplus\pi^{*}R_{\beta\alpha}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{F}_{\beta\alpha}:=\pi^{*}F_{\beta\alpha}\oplus\pi^{*}R_{\beta\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS2.SSS3.p7.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S6.SS2.SSS3.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> denotes (temporarily) the projection <math id="S6.SS2.SSS3.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{pq}\times{\bm{R}}_{pq}\to V_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{pq}\times{\bm{R}}_{pq}\to V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> and the induced projection <math id="S6.SS2.SSS3.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\alpha}\times{\bm{R}}_{\alpha}\to V_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\alpha}\times{\bm{R}}_{\alpha}\to V_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>. The stabilization described in Proposition <a href="#S5.Thmthm64" title="Proposition 5.64. ‣ 5.8. Constructing scaffolding ‣ 5. Global Kuranishi charts on Floer moduli spaces ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.64</span></a> is also extended to a map</p>
<table id="S6.Ex54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm Stab}_{\widehat{F}_{pq,\alpha}}(\widehat{V}_{\alpha})\to\partial^{\alpha}\widehat{V}_{pq}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Stab</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm Stab}_{\widehat{F}_{pq,\alpha}}(\widehat{V}_{\alpha})\to\partial^{\alpha}\widehat{V}_{pq}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS2.SSS3.p7.5" class="ltx_p">After taking the equivariantization, we obtain a map</p>
<table id="S6.Ex55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}\times_{G_{\alpha}}({\rm Stab}_{\widehat{F}_{pq,\alpha}}(\widehat{V}_{\alpha}))\to\widehat{V}_{pq}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Stab</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}\times_{G_{\alpha}}({\rm Stab}_{\widehat{F}_{pq,\alpha}}(\widehat{V}_{\alpha}))\to\widehat{V}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS2.SSS3.p7.6" class="ltx_p">which defines an equivariant open embedding. We would like to remark that the orthogonal complement of the <math id="S6.SS2.SSS3.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariantization of <math id="S6.SS2.SSS3.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{pq,\alpha}\to V_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{pq,\alpha}\to V_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S6.SS2.SSS3.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{pq}|_{G_{pq}(V_{\alpha})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{pq}|_{G_{pq}(V_{\alpha})}</annotation></semantics></math> is not necessarily a product bundle. Therefore, some extra care needs to be taken in the smoothing process.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS2.SSS4" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">6.2.4. </span>An induction scheme of stabilization</h4>

<div id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the smoothing process, the construction of successive stabilizations is elementary but complicated. In general, the stabilizations are constructed inductively, similar to many other inductive constructions. We would like to describe how the induction can be carried out. We first look at the simple case when a moduli space has strata of codimension at most 2. Assume <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;q</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{P}}^{\rm Floer}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>Floer</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{P}}^{\rm Floer}</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> be the domain of a global Kuranishi chart of <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\overline{\mathcal{M}}{}_{pq}^{\rm Floer}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>Floer</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\mathcal{M}}{}_{pq}^{\rm Floer}</annotation></semantics></math>. In the following discussion, we assume that the tangent microbundle of the underlying thickened moduli space of the relevant K-charts admits a vector bundle lift, which is the necessary condition for us to apply the smoothing theory. Moreover, in the discussion of extending the smoothing relatively, we assume that the lifts are compatible in a suitable sense. The construction of vector bundle lifts and the precise meaning of compatibility will be detailed in Section <a href="#S6.SS4" title="6.4. Proof of Theorem ‣ 6. Smoothing ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Note that we also need to endow the vector bundle <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{pq}\to V_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{pq}\to V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> with a smooth structure after suitable stabilization. However, this is rather straightforward after smoothing <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>: we can simply approximate the classifying map of <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> by a smooth map which stays in the same homotopy class.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The case with no boundary or corner.</span> When <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> has no boundary or corner, then it is the initial step of the induction. One can find a trivial <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>-bundle <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{pq}\times{\bm{R}}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{pq}\times{\bm{R}}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> induced by a suitable representation <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> needed for stable smoothing.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The case with only codimension one boundary strata.</span> When <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> has only codimension one boundary strata, without loss of generality, suppose there is only one boundary stratum <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{prq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{prq}</annotation></semantics></math>. Using the induction hypothesis, suppose <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{pr}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{pr}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{rq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{rq}</annotation></semantics></math> have been given. Consider the representation <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{pr}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{pr}</annotation></semantics></math> resp. <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{rq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{rq}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pr}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pr}</annotation></semantics></math> resp. <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{rq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{rq}</annotation></semantics></math>. By Frobenius reciprocity (see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx38" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sep07</a>, Theorem 7.47]</cite>), there exist orthogonal representations <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{pr}^{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{pr}^{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> resp. <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{rq}^{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{rq}^{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> which contains <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pr}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pr}</annotation></semantics></math> resp. <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{rq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{rq}</annotation></semantics></math> as subrepresentations of <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pr}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pr}</annotation></semantics></math> resp. <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{rq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{rq}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then define</p>
<table id="S6.Ex56" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{pq}={\bm{R}}_{pr}^{pq}\oplus{\bm{R}}_{rq}^{pq}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>⊕</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{pq}={\bm{R}}_{pr}^{pq}\oplus{\bm{R}}_{rq}^{pq}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p4.2" class="ltx_p">which is an orthogonal <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>-representation.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Now we define the bundle embeddings required for stabilization. We introduce more notations. Over the product <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{prq}=V_{pr}\times V_{rq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{prq}=V_{pr}\times V_{rq}</annotation></semantics></math>, define</p>
<table id="S6.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.Ex57"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ R_{pr\to pq}:=R_{pr}\boxplus\{0\},\ " display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊞</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ R_{pr\to pq}:=R_{pr}\boxplus\{0\},\ </annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex57.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ R_{rq\to pq}:=\{0\}\boxplus R_{rq}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊞</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ R_{rq\to pq}:=\{0\}\boxplus R_{rq}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p5.2" class="ltx_p">Then</p>
<table id="S6.Ex58" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{prq}=R_{pr\to pq}\oplus R_{rq\to pq}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{prq}=R_{pr\to pq}\oplus R_{rq\to pq}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p5.3" class="ltx_p">We would like the bundle embedding <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{pq,prq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{pq,prq}</annotation></semantics></math> to be the sum of</p>
<table id="S6.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.Ex59"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ \phi_{pr\to pq}:R_{pr\to pq}\to R_{pq}|_{\partial^{prq}V_{pq}},\ " display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ \phi_{pr\to pq}:R_{pr\to pq}\to R_{pq}|_{\partial^{prq}V_{pq}},\ </annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex59.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ \phi_{rq\to pq}:R_{rq\to pq}\to R_{pq}|_{\partial^{prq}V_{pq}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ \phi_{rq\to pq}:R_{rq\to pq}\to R_{pq}|_{\partial^{prq}V_{pq}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p5.4" class="ltx_p">Indeed, <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{pr\to pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{pr\to pq}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{rq\to pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{rq\to pq}</annotation></semantics></math> are the ones canonically induced from the linear inclusions</p>
<table id="S6.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.Ex60"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ {\bm{R}}_{pr}\hookrightarrow{\bm{R}}_{pr}^{pq}\hookrightarrow{\bm{R}}_{pq},\ " display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">↪</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">↪</mo><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ {\bm{R}}_{pr}\hookrightarrow{\bm{R}}_{pr}^{pq}\hookrightarrow{\bm{R}}_{pq},\ </annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex60.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ {\bm{R}}_{rq}\hookrightarrow{\bm{R}}_{rq}^{pq}\hookrightarrow{\bm{R}}_{pq}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">↪</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">↪</mo><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ {\bm{R}}_{rq}\hookrightarrow{\bm{R}}_{rq}^{pq}\hookrightarrow{\bm{R}}_{pq}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p5.5" class="ltx_p">Then all the requirements of Definition <a href="#S6.Thmthm25" title="Definition 6.25. ‣ 6.2.3. Stabilizing the K-chart lift ‣ 6.2. Pre-smoothing operations and stable complex structures ‣ 6. Smoothing ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.25</span></a> are automatically satisfied. In addition, for the purpose of stable smoothing, one can also take an additional direct sum to <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> by another orthogonal <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>-space <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{pq,0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{pq,0}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Note that in this final step, we need to apply the relative smoothing result Theorem <a href="#S6.Thmthm10" title="Theorem 6.10. ‣ 6.1.2. Stable equivariant smoothings ‣ 6.1. Preliminaries ‣ 6. Smoothing ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.10</span></a>. Indeed, the space <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{prq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{prq}</annotation></semantics></math> admits a smooth structure by taking the product of smooth structures on <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{pr}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{pr}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{rq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{rq}</annotation></semantics></math>, whose existence is based on the induction hypothesis. Then the equivariantization <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}(R_{prq})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}(R_{prq})</annotation></semantics></math> has a smooth structure. Denote by <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}(R_{prq}^{\perp})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>⟂</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}(R_{prq}^{\perp})</annotation></semantics></math> the equivariantization of the orthogonal complement of <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{prq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{prq}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{pq}|_{V_{prq}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{pq}|_{V_{prq}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Using the projection map <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{prq}\to V_{prq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{prq}\to V_{prq}</annotation></semantics></math>, the vector bundle <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}(R_{prq}^{\perp})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>⟂</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}(R_{prq}^{\perp})</annotation></semantics></math> can be pulled back to <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}(R_{prq})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}(R_{prq})</annotation></semantics></math> and the total space of this vector bundle can be endowed with a smooth structure, by approximating the classifying map. This in turn equips <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{pq}|_{\partial^{prq}V_{pq}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{pq}|_{\partial^{prq}V_{pq}}</annotation></semantics></math> with a smooth structure. Using the collar structure</p>
<table id="S6.Ex61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{prq}V_{pq}\times[0,\epsilon)\to V_{pq}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{prq}V_{pq}\times[0,\epsilon)\to V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p6.2" class="ltx_p">which extends to a collar structure of the stabilized charts, we see that an open neighborhood of <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{pq}|_{\partial^{prq}V_{pq}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{pq}|_{\partial^{prq}V_{pq}}</annotation></semantics></math> has a smooth structure using the product decomposition</p>
<table id="S6.Ex62" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{pq}|_{\partial^{prq}V_{pq}}\times[0,\epsilon)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{pq}|_{\partial^{prq}V_{pq}}\times[0,\epsilon).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p6.3" class="ltx_p">By replacing the open interval <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> by a closed interval of the form <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,\frac{\epsilon}{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,\frac{\epsilon}{2}]</annotation></semantics></math>, a suitable compatibility between the vector bundle lifts guarantees that we can apply Theorem <a href="#S6.Thmthm10" title="Theorem 6.10. ‣ 6.1.2. Stable equivariant smoothings ‣ 6.1. Preliminaries ‣ 6. Smoothing ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.10</span></a> to obtain the <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p6.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> orthogonal representation <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p6.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{pq,0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{pq,0}</annotation></semantics></math> which induces a stabilized smoothing for <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p6.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> extending the previously constructed stabilized smoothings on <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p6.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{pr}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{pr}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p6.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{rq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{rq}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmthm29" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_rem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmthm29.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark 6.29</span></span><span id="S6.Thmthm29.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmthm29.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmthm29.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We hope that the above arguments showcase the importance of applying Frobenius reciprocity, approximations of classifying maps of equivariant vector bundles, and the relative smoothing result in our inductive construction. Moreover, as we can see from above, outer-collaring conveniently provide us with an automatic smoothing near the boundary stratum. Additionally, it is important to keep in mind that the compatibility between the vector bundle lifts of tangent microbundles of the total space and boundary stratum is crucial for the application of Theorem <a href="#S6.Thmthm10" title="Theorem 6.10. ‣ 6.1.2. Stable equivariant smoothings ‣ 6.1. Preliminaries ‣ 6. Smoothing ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.10</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The case with only codimension one or two strata.</span> Now we consider the case when <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{A}}_{pq}^{\mathcal{P}}=\{pq,prq,psq,prsq\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔸</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{A}}_{pq}^{\mathcal{P}}=\{pq,prq,psq,prsq\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Suppose the representations</p>
<table id="S6.Ex63" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{pr},\ {\bm{R}}_{rs},\ {\bm{R}}_{sq},{\bm{R}}_{ps},{\bm{R}}_{rq}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{pr},\ {\bm{R}}_{rs},\ {\bm{R}}_{sq},{\bm{R}}_{ps},{\bm{R}}_{rq}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p7.2" class="ltx_p">are chosen so that they induce compatible stabilized smoothings except the top stratum <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>. Define the bundles <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{pr\to pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{pr\to pq}</annotation></semantics></math> etc. in a way similar to the previous case. Suppose we have also defined bundle embeddings</p>
<table id="S6.Ex64" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{pr\to ps},\ \phi_{rs\to ps},\ \phi_{rs\to rq},\ \phi_{sq\to rq}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{pr\to ps},\ \phi_{rs\to ps},\ \phi_{rs\to rq},\ \phi_{sq\to rq}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p7.3" class="ltx_p">In addition, we make the following assumptions, which basically says that for <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ps" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ps</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="rq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">rq</annotation></semantics></math>, the stabilization data are constructed as in the previous case.</p>
<ol id="S6.I13" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S6.I13.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S6.I13.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I13.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S6.I13.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{ps}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{ps}</annotation></semantics></math> is the direct sum</p>
<table id="S6.Ex65" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{ps}={\bm{R}}_{pr}^{ps}\oplus{\bm{R}}_{rs}^{ps}\oplus{\bm{R}}_{ps,0}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>⊕</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{ps}={\bm{R}}_{pr}^{ps}\oplus{\bm{R}}_{rs}^{ps}\oplus{\bm{R}}_{ps,0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I13.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">of orthogonal <math id="S6.I13.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{ps}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{ps}</annotation></semantics></math>-spaces such that <math id="S6.I13.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{pr}^{ps}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{pr}^{ps}</annotation></semantics></math> resp. <math id="S6.I13.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{rs}^{ps}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{rs}^{ps}</annotation></semantics></math> contains <math id="S6.I13.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{pr}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{pr}</annotation></semantics></math> resp. <math id="S6.I13.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{rs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{rs}</annotation></semantics></math> as subrepresentations of <math id="S6.I13.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pr}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pr}</annotation></semantics></math> resp. <math id="S6.I13.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{rs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{rs}</annotation></semantics></math>. Similarly, there is a direct sum</p>
<table id="S6.Ex66" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{rq}={\bm{R}}_{rs}^{rq}\oplus{\bm{R}}_{sq}^{rq}\oplus{\bm{R}}_{rq,0}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>⊕</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{rq}={\bm{R}}_{rs}^{rq}\oplus{\bm{R}}_{sq}^{rq}\oplus{\bm{R}}_{rq,0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I13.i1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">of orthogonal <math id="S6.I13.i1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{rq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{rq}</annotation></semantics></math>-spaces such that <math id="S6.I13.i1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{rs}^{rq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{rs}^{rq}</annotation></semantics></math> resp. <math id="S6.I13.i1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{sq}^{rq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{sq}^{rq}</annotation></semantics></math> contains <math id="S6.I13.i1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{rs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{rs}</annotation></semantics></math> resp. <math id="S6.I13.i1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{sq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{sq}</annotation></semantics></math> as subrepresentations of <math id="S6.I13.i1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{rs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{rs}</annotation></semantics></math> resp. <math id="S6.I13.i1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{sq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{sq}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I13.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S6.I13.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I13.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The bundle embedding</p>
<table id="S6.Ex67" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{pr\to ps}:R_{pr\to ps}\to R_{ps}|_{\partial^{prs}V_{ps}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{pr\to ps}:R_{pr\to ps}\to R_{ps}|_{\partial^{prs}V_{ps}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I13.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">is induced from the linear inclusion <math id="S6.I13.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{pr}\hookrightarrow{\bm{R}}_{pr}^{ps}\hookrightarrow{\bm{R}}_{ps}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">↪</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">↪</mo><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{pr}\hookrightarrow{\bm{R}}_{pr}^{ps}\hookrightarrow{\bm{R}}_{ps}</annotation></semantics></math>. Similar requirement applies to other bundle embeddings.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Now we define an orthogonal <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>-space <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>. There are two codimension one strata, <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="prq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">prq</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="psq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">psq</annotation></semantics></math>. For the <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pr}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pr}</annotation></semantics></math>-space <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{pr}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{pr}</annotation></semantics></math>, by Frobenius reciprocity, there is a <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>-orthogonal space <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{pr}^{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{pr}^{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> which contains <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{pr}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{pr}</annotation></semantics></math> as a subrepresentation of <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pr}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pr}</annotation></semantics></math>. We choose similarly <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p8.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{rq}^{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{rq}^{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p8.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{ps}^{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{ps}^{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p8.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{sq}^{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{sq}^{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>. For the purpose of stable smoothing, we choose another <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p8.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>-orthogonal space <math id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p8.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{pq,0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{pq,0}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is constructed similarly as the case of one boundary stratum by applying relative smoothing. Then define</p>
<table id="S6.Ex68" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{pq}:=\Big({\bm{R}}_{pr}^{pq}\oplus{\bm{R}}_{rq}^{pq}\Big)\oplus\Big({\bm{R}}_{ps}^{pq}\oplus{\bm{R}}_{sq}^{pq}\Big)\oplus{\bm{R}}_{pq,0}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>⊕</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>⊕</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{pq}:=\Big({\bm{R}}_{pr}^{pq}\oplus{\bm{R}}_{rq}^{pq}\Big)\oplus\Big({\bm{R}}_{ps}^{pq}\oplus{\bm{R}}_{sq}^{pq}\Big)\oplus{\bm{R}}_{pq,0}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p8.2" class="ltx_p">We rewrite this decomposition as</p>
<table id="S6.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{pq}={\bm{R}}_{pq,r}\oplus{\bm{R}}_{pq,s}\oplus{\bm{R}}_{pq,0}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{pq}={\bm{R}}_{pq,r}\oplus{\bm{R}}_{pq,s}\oplus{\bm{R}}_{pq,0}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6.6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p8.3" class="ltx_p">Then we want to define the bundle embeddings into</p>
<table id="S6.Ex69" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{pq}:=R_{pq,r}\oplus R_{pq,s}\oplus R_{pq,0}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{pq}:=R_{pq,r}\oplus R_{pq,s}\oplus R_{pq,0}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p8.4" class="ltx_p">This time the bundle embeddings are not purely induced from linear maps between the representations.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p9" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S6.I14" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S6.I14.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S6.I14.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I14.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We define <math id="S6.I14.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{pr\to pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{pr\to pq}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.I14.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{sq\to pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{sq\to pq}</annotation></semantics></math>. We only describe <math id="S6.I14.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{pr\to pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{pr\to pq}</annotation></semantics></math> in detail. With respect to (<a href="#S6.E6" title="In 6.2.4. An induction scheme of stabilization ‣ 6.2. Pre-smoothing operations and stable complex structures ‣ 6. Smoothing ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.6</span></a>), we write</p>
<table id="S6.Ex70" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{pr\to pq}=\phi_{pr,r}\oplus\phi_{pr,s}\oplus 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊕</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{pr\to pq}=\phi_{pr,r}\oplus\phi_{pr,s}\oplus 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I14.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We define <math id="S6.I14.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{pr,r}:R_{pr\to pq}\to R_{pq,r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{pr,r}:R_{pr\to pq}\to R_{pq,r}</annotation></semantics></math> to be the one induced from the linear inclusion</p>
<table id="S6.Ex71" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{pr}\hookrightarrow{\bm{R}}_{pr}^{pq}\hookrightarrow{\bm{R}}_{pq,r}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">↪</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">↪</mo><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{pr}\hookrightarrow{\bm{R}}_{pr}^{pq}\hookrightarrow{\bm{R}}_{pq,r}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I14.i1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">For <math id="S6.I14.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{pr,s}:R_{pr\to pq}\to R_{pq,s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{pr,s}:R_{pr\to pq}\to R_{pq,s}</annotation></semantics></math>, notice that it is defined over <math id="S6.I14.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{prq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{prq}</annotation></semantics></math>. We first define it over <math id="S6.I14.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{prsq}V_{prq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{prsq}V_{prq}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is induced from the existing bundle map</p>
<table id="S6.Ex72" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{pr\to ps}:R_{pr\to ps}\to R_{ps}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{pr\to ps}:R_{pr\to ps}\to R_{ps}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I14.i1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">and its equivariantization and stabilization (by the bundle associated to the scaffolding), composed with the linear inclusion</p>
<table id="S6.Ex73" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{ps}\hookrightarrow R_{ps}^{pq}\hookrightarrow R_{pq,s}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">↪</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">↪</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{ps}\hookrightarrow R_{ps}^{pq}\hookrightarrow R_{pq,s}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I14.i1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">To extend to the whole <math id="S6.I14.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{prq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{prq}</annotation></semantics></math>, we use the collar structure and a cut-off function on <math id="S6.I14.i1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{prq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{prq}</annotation></semantics></math> which is supported in the collar region near <math id="S6.I14.i1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{prsq}V_{prq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{prsq}V_{prq}</annotation></semantics></math> and which only depends on the collar coordinate.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I14.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S6.I14.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I14.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We define <math id="S6.I14.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{rs\to pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{rs\to pq}</annotation></semantics></math>. Again, we write <math id="S6.I14.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{rs\to pq}=\phi_{rs,r}\oplus\phi_{rs,s}\oplus 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊕</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{rs\to pq}=\phi_{rs,r}\oplus\phi_{rs,s}\oplus 0</annotation></semantics></math>. The first component <math id="S6.I14.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{rs,r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{rs,r}</annotation></semantics></math> is induced from the bundle map</p>
<table id="S6.Ex74" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{rs\to rq}:R_{rs\to rq}\to R_{rq}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{rs\to rq}:R_{rs\to rq}\to R_{rq}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I14.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">composed with the linear inclusion <math id="S6.I14.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{rq}\hookrightarrow{\bm{R}}_{rq}^{pq}\hookrightarrow{\bm{R}}_{pq,r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">↪</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">↪</mo><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{rq}\hookrightarrow{\bm{R}}_{rq}^{pq}\hookrightarrow{\bm{R}}_{pq,r}</annotation></semantics></math>; the second component <math id="S6.I14.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{rs,s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{rs,s}</annotation></semantics></math> is induced from the bundle map</p>
<table id="S6.Ex75" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{rs\to ps}:R_{rs\to ps}\to R_{ps}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{rs\to ps}:R_{rs\to ps}\to R_{ps}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I14.i2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">composed with the linear inclusion <math id="S6.I14.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{ps}\hookrightarrow{\bm{R}}_{ps}^{pq}\hookrightarrow{\bm{R}}_{pq,s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">↪</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">↪</mo><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{ps}\hookrightarrow{\bm{R}}_{ps}^{pq}\hookrightarrow{\bm{R}}_{pq,s}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I14.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S6.I14.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I14.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The definitions of <math id="S6.I14.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{ps\to pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{ps\to pq}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.I14.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{rq\to pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{rq\to pq}</annotation></semantics></math> is similar to the case of <math id="S6.I14.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{pr\to pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{pr\to pq}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.I14.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{sq\to pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{sq\to pq}</annotation></semantics></math>. We only describe in detail the bundle map <math id="S6.I14.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{ps\to pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{ps\to pq}</annotation></semantics></math> (which should be defined over <math id="S6.I14.i3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{psq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{psq}</annotation></semantics></math>). We write <math id="S6.I14.i3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{ps\to pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{ps\to pq}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="S6.I14.i3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{ps,r}\oplus\phi_{ps,s}\oplus 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊕</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{ps,r}\oplus\phi_{ps,s}\oplus 0</annotation></semantics></math>. The second component <math id="S6.I14.i3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{ps,s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{ps,s}</annotation></semantics></math> is naturally induced from the linear inclusion <math id="S6.I14.i3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{ps}\hookrightarrow{\bm{R}}_{ps}^{pq}\hookrightarrow{\bm{R}}_{pq,s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">↪</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">↪</mo><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{ps}\hookrightarrow{\bm{R}}_{ps}^{pq}\hookrightarrow{\bm{R}}_{pq,s}</annotation></semantics></math>, For the first component <math id="S6.I14.i3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{ps,r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{ps,r}</annotation></semantics></math>, we decompose it further as</p>
<table id="S6.Ex76" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{ps,r}=\phi_{ps,pr}\oplus\phi_{ps,rs}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{ps,r}=\phi_{ps,pr}\oplus\phi_{ps,rs}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I14.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We first define it over the boundary stratum <math id="S6.I14.i3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{prsq}V_{psq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{prsq}V_{psq}</annotation></semantics></math> and then use a cut-off function to turn it off as we leave this stratum towards the interior of <math id="S6.I14.i3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{psq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{psq}</annotation></semantics></math>. Consider the composition of orthogonal projections</p>
<table id="S6.Ex77" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{ps}\to{\bm{R}}_{pr}^{ps}\oplus{\bm{R}}_{rs}^{ps}\to{\bm{R}}_{pr}\oplus{\bm{R}}_{rs}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>⊕</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{ps}\to{\bm{R}}_{pr}^{ps}\oplus{\bm{R}}_{rs}^{ps}\to{\bm{R}}_{pr}\oplus{\bm{R}}_{rs}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I14.i3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">which induces a bundle map</p>
<table id="S6.Ex78" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{ps\to pq}|_{V_{prsq}}\to R_{pr\to pq}|_{V_{prsq}}\oplus R_{rs\to pq}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{ps\to pq}|_{V_{prsq}}\to R_{pr\to pq}|_{V_{prsq}}\oplus R_{rs\to pq}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I14.i3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Then using the linear inclusions <math id="S6.I14.i3.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{pr}\to{\bm{R}}_{pr}^{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{pr}\to{\bm{R}}_{pr}^{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> and the map <math id="S6.I14.i3.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{rs\to rq}\to R_{rq}\to R_{rq}^{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{rs\to rq}\to R_{rq}\to R_{rq}^{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>, one defines the map <math id="S6.I14.i3.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{ps,r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{ps,r}</annotation></semantics></math> over the closed set <math id="S6.I14.i3.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{prsq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{prsq}</annotation></semantics></math>. One can then equivariantize, stabilize to define it over <math id="S6.I14.i3.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{prsq}V_{psq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{prsq}V_{psq}</annotation></semantics></math>. Lastly, use a cut-off function to extend this component to a neighborhood.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmthm30" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_rem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmthm30.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark 6.30</span></span><span id="S6.Thmthm30.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmthm30.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmthm30.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We put effort on defining the embeddings maps between charts in the above discussions, which contains certain distinct features than the case with fewer strata because the bundle maps are no longer linear. We would like to remark that the compatibility between the stabilized smoothings of <math id="S6.Thmthm30.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{prq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{prq}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.Thmthm30.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{psq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{psq}</annotation></semantics></math> near their common stratum <math id="S6.Thmthm30.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{prsq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{prsq}</annotation></semantics></math> is already guaranteed by the inductive nature of our construction.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.SSS4.p10.1" class="ltx_p">The above inductive strategy, especially the case with codimension two strata, indicates that it seems difficult to construct a stabilization of K-chart lifts of a flow category using purely linear maps between representations. This brings in an extra layer of complexity in the following smoothing process because we would like the bundle embeddings also to be smooth.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.3. </span>The main theorem about smoothing</h3>

<div id="S6.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We state the main theorem on smoothing the outer-collared K-chart lift of <math id="S6.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(T^{\rm Floer})^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>Floer</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(T^{\rm Floer})^{+}</annotation></semantics></math>. In the following, a smoothing on a <math id="S6.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔸</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{A}}</annotation></semantics></math>-manifold <math id="S6.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> equipped with a collar structure (Definition <a href="#S3.Thmthm26" title="Definition 3.26. ‣ 3.5.1. Collar structure ‣ 3.5. Additional structures ‣ 3. Abstract constructions of chain complexes and maps over the integers ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.26</span></a>) is called a <span id="S6.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">collared smoothing</span> if the smoothing is equal to the product of the standard smooth structure on <math id="S6.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[0,\epsilon)^{{\mathbb{F}}_{\alpha}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,\epsilon)^{{\mathbb{F}}_{\alpha}}</annotation></semantics></math> and a smoothing on <math id="S6.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{\alpha}V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{\alpha}V</annotation></semantics></math> over the collar region <math id="S6.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\partial^{\alpha}V\times[0,\epsilon)^{{\mathbb{F}}_{\alpha}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{\alpha}V\times[0,\epsilon)^{{\mathbb{F}}_{\alpha}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The same notion is also used for a smoothing of a vector bundle.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmthm31" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmthm31.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 6.31</span></span><span id="S6.Thmthm31.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmthm31.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmthm31.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmthm31.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Given the outer-collared K-chart lift <math id="S6.Thmthm31.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathfrak{K}}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔎</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathfrak{K}}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> of the outer-collared flow category <math id="S6.Thmthm31.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(T^{{\rm Floer}})^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>Floer</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(T^{{\rm Floer}})^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> equipped with a collared scaffolding (see Proposition <a href="#S5.Thmthm64" title="Proposition 5.64. ‣ 5.8. Constructing scaffolding ‣ 5. Global Kuranishi charts on Floer moduli spaces ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.64</span></a>), there exist the following objects. We revome the “<math id="S6.Thmthm31.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>+</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+</annotation></semantics></math>” to make the notations more succinct.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmthm31.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S6.I15" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S6.I15.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S6.I15.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I15.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I15.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">A stabilization of </span><math id="S6.I15.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathfrak{K}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔎</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathfrak{K}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I15.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> (see Definition </span><a href="#S6.Thmthm25" title="Definition 6.25. ‣ 6.2.3. Stabilizing the K-chart lift ‣ 6.2. Pre-smoothing operations and stable complex structures ‣ 6. Smoothing ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.25</span></a><span id="S6.I15.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">), given by a collection of orthogonal </span><math id="S6.I15.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I15.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-spaces </span><math id="S6.I15.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I15.i1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and a collection of bundle embeddings.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I15.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S6.I15.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I15.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I15.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">A collared </span><math id="S6.I15.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I15.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-smoothing on </span><math id="S6.I15.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}_{pq}:=V_{pq}\times{\bm{R}}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}_{pq}:=V_{pq}\times{\bm{R}}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I15.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I15.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S6.I15.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I15.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I15.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">A collared bundle </span><math id="S6.I15.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I15.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-smoothing on the </span><math id="S6.I15.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(n)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I15.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-bundle </span><math id="S6.I15.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{O}_{pq}\to\widehat{V}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{O}_{pq}\to\widehat{V}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I15.i3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, where </span><math id="S6.I15.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{O}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{O}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I15.i3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is the pullback of </span><math id="S6.I15.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I15.i3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> under the natural projection </span><math id="S6.I15.i3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}_{pq}\to V_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}_{pq}\to V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I15.i3.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I15.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(4)</span> 
<div id="S6.I15.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I15.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I15.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">A collared </span><math id="S6.I15.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I15.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-invariant inner product on the trivial bundle </span><math id="S6.I15.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{pq}\to V_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{pq}\to V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I15.i4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> inducing an inner product on the vector bundle </span><math id="S6.I15.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{R}_{pq}\to\widehat{V}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{R}_{pq}\to\widehat{V}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I15.i4.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, where </span><math id="S6.I15.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{R}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{R}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I15.i4.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is the pullback of </span><math id="S6.I15.i4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I15.i4.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> under the natural projection </span><math id="S6.I15.i4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}_{pq}\to V_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}_{pq}\to V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I15.i4.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I15.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(5)</span> 
<div id="S6.I15.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I15.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I15.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">A collared </span><math id="S6.I15.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I15.i5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-smoothing on the </span><math id="S6.I15.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(n)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I15.i5.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-bundles </span><math id="S6.I15.i5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{R}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{R}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I15.i5.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S6.Thmthm31.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmthm31.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">These objects satisfy the following conditions.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmthm31.p3" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S6.I16" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S6.I16.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(A)</span> 
<div id="S6.I16.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I16.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I16.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The smoothing of </span><math id="S6.I16.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I16.ix1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> induces a smooth bundle structure </span><math id="S6.I16.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{Q}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{Q}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I16.ix1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> as it is induced from the </span><math id="S6.I16.ix1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I16.ix1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-representation </span><math id="S6.I16.ix1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{Q}}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑸</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{Q}}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I16.ix1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. Then the smooth structures on </span><math id="S6.I16.ix1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{O}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{O}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I16.ix1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="S6.I16.ix1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{R}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{R}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I16.ix1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> induce a smooth structure on the obstruction bundle</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex79" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{E}_{pq}=\widehat{O}_{pq}\oplus\widehat{Q}_{pq}\oplus\widehat{R}_{pq}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{E}_{pq}=\widehat{O}_{pq}\oplus\widehat{Q}_{pq}\oplus\widehat{R}_{pq}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I16.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(B)</span> 
<div id="S6.I16.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I16.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I16.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Boundary smoothings are given by products and stabilizations. More precisely, this means the following. For any stratum </span><math id="S6.I16.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\alpha=pr_{1}\cdots r_{l}q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=pr_{1}\cdots r_{l}q</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I16.ix2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> of </span><math id="S6.I16.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{A}}^{\rm Floer}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝔸</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>Floer</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{A}}^{\rm Floer}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I16.ix2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, the smoothings on </span><math id="S6.I16.ix2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}_{pr_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}_{pr_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I16.ix2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="S6.I16.ix2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ldots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ldots</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I16.ix2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="S6.I16.ix2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}_{r_{l}q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}_{r_{l}q}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I16.ix2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> induce a smooth structure on the prodcut </span><math id="S6.I16.ix2.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widehat{V}_{\alpha}=\widehat{V}_{pr_{1}}\times\cdots\times\widehat{V}_{r_{l}q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.055em">⋯</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}_{\alpha}=\widehat{V}_{pr_{1}}\times\cdots\times\widehat{V}_{r_{l}q}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I16.ix2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and its equivariantization </span><math id="S6.I16.ix2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}_{\alpha}^{\sim}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>α</mi><mo>∼</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}_{\alpha}^{\sim}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I16.ix2.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">; the smooth bundle structures on </span><math id="S6.I16.ix2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{O}_{pr_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{O}_{pr_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I16.ix2.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="S6.I16.ix2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ldots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ldots</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I16.ix2.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="S6.I16.ix2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{O}_{r_{l}q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{O}_{r_{l}q}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I16.ix2.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> induce a smooth structure on the bundle </span><math id="S6.I16.ix2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{O}_{\alpha}^{\sim}\to\widehat{V}_{\alpha}^{\sim}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>α</mi><mo>∼</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>α</mi><mo>∼</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{O}_{\alpha}^{\sim}\to\widehat{V}_{\alpha}^{\sim}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I16.ix2.p1.1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">; there is also a canonical smooth bundle structure on </span><math id="S6.I16.ix2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\alpha}^{\sim}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>α</mi><mo>∼</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\alpha}^{\sim}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I16.ix2.p1.1.13" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> as it is induced from trivial bundles. Then</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S6.I16.ix2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S6.I16.ix2.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S6.I16.ix2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(a)</span> 
<div id="S6.I16.ix2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I16.ix2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I16.ix2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The embedding </span><math id="S6.I16.ix2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}_{\alpha}\hookrightarrow\partial^{\alpha}\widehat{V}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>α</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">↪</mo><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}_{\alpha}\hookrightarrow\partial^{\alpha}\widehat{V}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I16.ix2.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is smooth.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I16.ix2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(b)</span> 
<div id="S6.I16.ix2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I16.ix2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I16.ix2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The bundle embedding </span><math id="S6.I16.ix2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{O}_{\alpha}\hookrightarrow\widehat{O}_{pq}|_{\partial^{\alpha}\widehat{V}_{pq}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">↪</mo><msub><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{O}_{\alpha}\hookrightarrow\widehat{O}_{pq}|_{\partial^{\alpha}\widehat{V}_{pq}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I16.ix2.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and the bundle embedding </span><math id="S6.I16.ix2.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{R}_{\alpha}\hookrightarrow\widehat{R}_{pq}|_{\partial^{\alpha}\widehat{V}_{pq}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">↪</mo><msub><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{R}_{\alpha}\hookrightarrow\widehat{R}_{pq}|_{\partial^{\alpha}\widehat{V}_{pq}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I16.ix2.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> are smooth bundle embeddings. It follows that the orthogonal complement </span><math id="S6.I16.ix2.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{O}_{pq,\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{O}_{pq,\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I16.ix2.I1.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and the orthogonal complement </span><math id="S6.I16.ix2.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{R}_{pq,\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{R}_{pq,\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I16.ix2.I1.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> are smooth bundles over </span><math id="S6.I16.ix2.I1.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I16.ix2.I1.i2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. It follows that the bundle</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex80" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{F}_{pq,\alpha}=\widehat{O}_{pq,\alpha}\oplus\widehat{Q}_{pq,\alpha}\oplus\widehat{R}_{pq,\alpha}\to\widehat{V}_{\alpha}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{F}_{pq,\alpha}=\widehat{O}_{pq,\alpha}\oplus\widehat{Q}_{pq,\alpha}\oplus\widehat{R}_{pq,\alpha}\to\widehat{V}_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I16.ix2.I1.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I16.ix2.I1.i2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">is smooth, where the smooth structure on </span><math id="S6.I16.ix2.I1.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{Q}_{pq,\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{Q}_{pq,\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I16.ix2.I1.i2.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is induced from the orthogonal complement of the </span><math id="S6.I16.ix2.I1.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I16.ix2.I1.i2.p1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-subrepresentation </span><math id="S6.I16.ix2.I1.i2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{Q}}_{\alpha}\hookrightarrow{\bm{Q}}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑸</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">↪</mo><msub><mi>𝑸</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{Q}}_{\alpha}\hookrightarrow{\bm{Q}}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I16.ix2.I1.i2.p1.2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I16.ix2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(c)</span> 
<div id="S6.I16.ix2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I16.ix2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I16.ix2.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The stabilization map</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex81" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex81.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\theta}_{pq,\alpha}:{\rm Stab}_{\widehat{F}_{pq,\alpha}}\Big(\widehat{V}_{\alpha}\Big)\to\partial^{\alpha}V_{pq}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Stab</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>α</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\theta}_{pq,\alpha}:{\rm Stab}_{\widehat{F}_{pq,\alpha}}\Big(\widehat{V}_{\alpha}\Big)\to\partial^{\alpha}V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I16.ix2.I1.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I16.ix2.I1.i3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(which is the </span><math id="S6.I16.ix2.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{pq,\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{pq,\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I16.ix2.I1.i3.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> in (</span><a href="#S5.E50" title="In item 2 ‣ Proposition 5.64. ‣ 5.8. Constructing scaffolding ‣ 5. Global Kuranishi charts on Floer moduli spaces ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.50</span></a><span id="S6.I16.ix2.I1.i3.p1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">) lifted) is a smooth embedding.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I16.ix2.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(d)</span> 
<div id="S6.I16.ix2.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I16.ix2.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I16.ix2.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let </span><math id="S6.I16.ix2.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\pi}_{pq,\alpha}:\partial^{\alpha}\widehat{V}_{pq}\to\widehat{V}_{\alpha}^{\sim}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.111em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>α</mi><mo>∼</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\pi}_{pq,\alpha}:\partial^{\alpha}\widehat{V}_{pq}\to\widehat{V}_{\alpha}^{\sim}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.I16.ix2.I1.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> be the projection map induced from the stabilization map above, which is smooth. Then bundle isomorphism</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex82" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\vartheta}_{pq,\alpha}:\widehat{\pi}_{pq,\alpha}^{*}\Big(\widehat{O}_{pq}|_{\widehat{V}_{\alpha}}\Big)\to\widehat{O}_{pq}|_{\partial^{\alpha}\widehat{V}_{pq}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ϑ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><msub><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>α</mi></msub></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\vartheta}_{pq,\alpha}:\widehat{\pi}_{pq,\alpha}^{*}\Big(\widehat{O}_{pq}|_{\widehat{V}_{\alpha}}\Big)\to\widehat{O}_{pq}|_{\partial^{\alpha}\widehat{V}_{pq}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I16.ix2.I1.i4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I16.ix2.I1.i4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(included in the scaffolding) is smooth.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Assuming this theorem, it is straightforward to construct a derived orbifold lift of the flow category <math id="S6.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(T^{\rm Floer})^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>Floer</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(T^{\rm Floer})^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> by taking group quotients. Remove the <math id="S6.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\cdot}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mo>⋅</mo><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\cdot}</annotation></semantics></math> from the notation. Define</p>
<table id="S6.Ex83" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex83.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{pq}=({\mathcal{U}}_{pq},{\mathcal{E}}_{pq},{\mathcal{S}}_{pq},\psi_{pq})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{pq}=({\mathcal{U}}_{pq},{\mathcal{E}}_{pq},{\mathcal{S}}_{pq},\psi_{pq})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S6.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{U}}_{pq}=V_{pq}/G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{U}}_{pq}=V_{pq}/G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{E}}_{pq}=E_{pq}/G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{E}}_{pq}=E_{pq}/G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{S}}_{pq}:{\mathcal{U}}_{pq}\to{\mathcal{E}}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{S}}_{pq}:{\mathcal{U}}_{pq}\to{\mathcal{E}}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> is the induced orbibundle section, and <math id="S6.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\psi_{pq}:{\mathcal{S}}_{pq}^{-1}(0)\to\overline{\mathcal{M}}{}_{pq}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mmultiscripts><mphantom></mphantom><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{pq}:{\mathcal{S}}_{pq}^{-1}(0)\to\overline{\mathcal{M}}{}_{pq}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> is the induced footprint map. Moreover, for <math id="S6.SS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\alpha=pr_{1}\cdots r_{l}q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=pr_{1}\cdots r_{l}q</annotation></semantics></math>, one has the natural identification</p>
<table id="S6.Ex84" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex84.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="K_{\alpha}/G_{\alpha}\cong C_{\alpha}:=C_{pr_{1}}\times\cdots\times C_{r_{l}q}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>G</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>≅</mo><mi>C</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mi>C</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.055em">⋯</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>C</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\alpha}/G_{\alpha}\cong C_{\alpha}:=C_{pr_{1}}\times\cdots\times C_{r_{l}q}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The scaffolding in the K-chart sense also descends to a scaffolding in the D-chart sense. Indeed, for <math id="S6.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha,\beta\in{\mathbb{A}}_{pq}^{\rm Floer}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>𝔸</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>Floer</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha,\beta\in{\mathbb{A}}_{pq}^{\rm Floer}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S6.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\leq\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\leq\beta</annotation></semantics></math>, the bundle</p>
<table id="S6.Ex85" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex85.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}_{\beta\alpha}:=F_{\beta\alpha}/G_{\alpha}\to{\mathcal{U}}_{\alpha}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}_{\beta\alpha}:=F_{\beta\alpha}/G_{\alpha}\to{\mathcal{U}}_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">is a smooth orbifold vector bundle over <math id="S6.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{U}}_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{U}}_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then the stabilization map <math id="S6.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm Stab}_{F_{\beta}\alpha}(V_{\alpha})\to\partial^{\alpha}V_{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Stab</mi><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>β</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm Stab}_{F_{\beta}\alpha}(V_{\alpha})\to\partial^{\alpha}V_{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math> induces</p>
<table id="S6.Ex86" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex86.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\theta}}_{\beta\alpha}:{\rm Stab}_{{\mathcal{F}}_{\beta\alpha}}(C_{\alpha})\to\partial^{\alpha}C_{\beta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Stab</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>β</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\theta}}_{\beta\alpha}:{\rm Stab}_{{\mathcal{F}}_{\beta\alpha}}(C_{\alpha})\to\partial^{\alpha}C_{\beta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS3.p3.3" class="ltx_p">One checkes directly that the data <math id="S6.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathcal{F}}_{\beta\alpha},{\bm{\theta}}_{\beta\alpha})_{\alpha\leq\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathcal{F}}_{\beta\alpha},{\bm{\theta}}_{\beta\alpha})_{\alpha\leq\beta}</annotation></semantics></math> form a scaffolding in the D-presentation of <math id="S6.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\overline{\mathcal{M}}{}_{pq}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\mathcal{M}}{}_{pq}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math>. It should be pointed out that these derived orbifold charts are effective due to the geometric construction.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmthm32" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmthm32.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 6.32</span></span><span id="S6.Thmthm32.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmthm32.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmthm32.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmthm32.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The D-chart lift of <math id="S6.Thmthm32.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(T^{\rm Floer})^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>Floer</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(T^{\rm Floer})^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> induced from <math id="S6.Thmthm32.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{C_{pq}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{C_{pq}\}</annotation></semantics></math> equipped with the compatible collar structure and scaffolding can be upgraded to an oriented and normally complex derived orbifold lift by doing a further stabilization of the corresponding K-chart lift.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S6.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">In the case of a single chart <math id="S6.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathcal{U}}_{pq},{\mathcal{E}}_{pq},{\mathcal{S}}_{pq},\psi_{pq})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathcal{U}}_{pq},{\mathcal{E}}_{pq},{\mathcal{S}}_{pq},\psi_{pq})</annotation></semantics></math>, recall that <math id="S6.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{U}}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{U}}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> is obtained from a quotient <math id="S6.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}_{pq}/G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}_{pq}/G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>, such that</span></p>
<ol id="S6.I17" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S6.I17.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S6.I17.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I17.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The space <math id="S6.I17.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> is equal to the product <math id="S6.I17.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{pq}\times{\bm{R}}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{pq}\times{\bm{R}}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I17.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S6.I17.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I17.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">There is a <math id="S6.I17.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{1}_{\rm loc}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>loc</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{1}_{\rm loc}</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="S6.I17.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>-bundle structure <math id="S6.I17.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{pq}:V_{pq}\to B_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{pq}:V_{pq}\to B_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> which ensures that the tangent space of the smoothing of <math id="S6.I17.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> is isotopic to the direct sum</p>
<table id="S6.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{pq}\oplus T^{\rm vt}V_{pq}\oplus\pi^{*}TB_{pq}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>vt</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{pq}\oplus T^{\rm vt}V_{pq}\oplus\pi^{*}TB_{pq},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6.7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I17.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where we abuse the notation to denote the corresponding bundles obtained by the pullback under the natural projection map <math id="S6.I17.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}_{pq}\to V_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}_{pq}\to V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S6.SS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">The first simple obervation is that the stabilizing factors <math id="S6.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> can be taken to be unitary representations. We can simply use <math id="S6.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{pq}\oplus{\bm{i}}{\bm{R}}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi>𝒊</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{pq}\oplus{\bm{i}}{\bm{R}}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> instead of a possibly real representation <math id="S6.SS3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, the bundle inclusions <math id="S6.SS3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\alpha}\oplus{\bm{i}}R_{\alpha}\hookrightarrow R_{pq}\oplus{\bm{i}}R_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi>𝒊</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↪</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi>𝒊</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\alpha}\oplus{\bm{i}}R_{\alpha}\hookrightarrow R_{pq}\oplus{\bm{i}}R_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> are then complex linear and the inner products on the trivial bundles <math id="S6.SS3.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{pq}\oplus{\bm{i}}R_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi>𝒊</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{pq}\oplus{\bm{i}}R_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> become Hermitian.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">We would like to do a further stabilization to the (already smoothed) K-chart lift. Indeed, we stabilize by the <math id="S6.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>-representation <math id="S6.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{Q}}_{d_{pq}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑸</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{Q}}_{d_{pq}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S6.SS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{Q}_{pq}^{\prime}\to\widehat{V}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{Q}_{pq}^{\prime}\to\widehat{V}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> be the trivial bundle (to be distinguished from the original <math id="S6.SS3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>-bundle). Notice that the bundle inclusions <math id="S6.SS3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\delta}\hookrightarrow Q_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">↪</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\delta}\hookrightarrow Q_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S6.SS3.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\delta}\subset B_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\delta}\subset B_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S6.SS3.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in{\mathbb{A}}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝔸</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in{\mathbb{A}}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined via a linear inclusion <math id="S6.SS3.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{Q}}_{\delta}\to{\bm{Q}}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑸</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>𝑸</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{Q}}_{\delta}\to{\bm{Q}}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> the corresponding bundle. Then there are natural bundle inclusions</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex87" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex87.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{Q}_{\alpha}^{\prime}\to\widehat{Q}_{pq}^{\prime}|_{\widehat{V}_{\alpha}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>α</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{Q}_{\alpha}^{\prime}\to\widehat{Q}_{pq}^{\prime}|_{\widehat{V}_{\alpha}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS3.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">As this bundle map is induced from linear map between representation spaces, it is automatically smooth. Hence we obtained another smooth K-chart lift whose K-charts are</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex88" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex88.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\widehat{K}}_{pq}={\rm Stab}_{\widehat{Q}_{pq}^{\prime}}\widehat{K}_{pq}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Stab</mi><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\widehat{K}}_{pq}={\rm Stab}_{\widehat{Q}_{pq}^{\prime}}\widehat{K}_{pq}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS3.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">It induces a new D-chart lift.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now we consider the normal complex structures on this new D-chart lift. Indeed, the obstruction bundles are now all complex. Indeed,</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex89" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex89.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widehat{\widehat{E}}_{pq}=\widehat{\widehat{O}}_{pq}\oplus\widehat{\widehat{R}}_{pq}\oplus\widehat{\widehat{Q}}_{pq}\oplus\widehat{\widehat{Q}}{}_{pq}^{\prime}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊕</mo><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊕</mo><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊕</mo><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\widehat{E}}_{pq}=\widehat{\widehat{O}}_{pq}\oplus\widehat{\widehat{R}}_{pq}\oplus\widehat{\widehat{Q}}_{pq}\oplus\widehat{\widehat{Q}}{}_{pq}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS3.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">and we give the last two summands the natural complex structure.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now the quotient orbifold</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex90" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex90.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\widehat{V}}_{pq}/G_{pq}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\widehat{V}}_{pq}/G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS3.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">is normally complex. Indeed, (<a href="#S6.E7" title="In item 2 ‣ Proof. ‣ 6.3. The main theorem about smoothing ‣ 6. Smoothing ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.7</span></a>) becomes</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex91" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex91.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="T\widehat{\widehat{V}}_{pq}\cong\big(R_{pq}\otimes{\mathbb{C}}\big)\oplus T^{\rm vt}V_{pq}\oplus(\pi_{pq}^{*}TB_{d_{pq}}\oplus\widehat{\widehat{Q}}{}_{d_{pq}}^{\prime})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>ℂ</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>vt</mi></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mi>T</mi><msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo>⊕</mo><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>^</mo></mover><mmultiscripts><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo><mprescripts></mprescripts><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\widehat{\widehat{V}}_{pq}\cong\big(R_{pq}\otimes{\mathbb{C}}\big)\oplus T^{\rm vt}V_{pq}\oplus(\pi_{pq}^{*}TB_{d_{pq}}\oplus\widehat{\widehat{Q}}{}_{d_{pq}}^{\prime}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS3.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">As shown in Proposition <a href="#S5.Thmthm27" title="Proposition 5.27. ‣ 5.2.7. Normal complex structure ‣ 5.2. Global chart construction I ‣ 5. Global Kuranishi charts on Floer moduli spaces ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.27</span></a>, the quotient of the last summand above is normally complex. Moreover, by Lemma <a href="#S6.Thmthm23" title="Lemma 6.23. ‣ 6.2.2. Vertical stable complex structures ‣ 6.2. Pre-smoothing operations and stable complex structures ‣ 6. Smoothing ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.23</span></a> and Corollary <a href="#S6.Thmthm24" title="Corollary 6.24. ‣ 6.2.2. Vertical stable complex structures ‣ 6.2. Pre-smoothing operations and stable complex structures ‣ 6. Smoothing ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.24</span></a>, the quotient of <math id="S6.SS3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\rm vt}V_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>vt</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\rm vt}V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> is also normally complex.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">To obtain a normal complex structure on the D-chart lift, we further check:</span></p>
<ol id="S6.I18" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S6.I18.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S6.I18.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I18.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A complex structure on the scaffolding. Indeed, the original difference bundles</p>
<table id="S6.Ex92" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex92.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{F}_{pq,\alpha}=\widehat{O}_{pq,\alpha}\oplus\widehat{Q}_{pq,\alpha}\oplus\widehat{R}_{pq,\alpha}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{F}_{pq,\alpha}=\widehat{O}_{pq,\alpha}\oplus\widehat{Q}_{pq,\alpha}\oplus\widehat{R}_{pq,\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I18.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">is already complex as explained below. First, the bundle <math id="S6.I18.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{O}_{pq,\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{O}_{pq,\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> is complex because we can choose the metric on the <math id="S6.I18.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>O</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O</annotation></semantics></math>-bundles to be Hermitian. The factor <math id="S6.I18.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{pq,\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{pq,\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> is complex because it consists of “off-diagonal” Hermitian matrices. As mentioned above, the stabilization in the smoothing can be chosen to be complex representations, therefore <math id="S6.I18.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{R}_{pq,\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{R}_{pq,\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> also has a complex structure. Then the further stabilization by <math id="S6.I18.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{Q}}_{d_{pq}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑸</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{Q}}_{d_{pq}}</annotation></semantics></math> gives an extra copy of <math id="S6.I18.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{Q}_{pq,\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{Q}_{pq,\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> which is complex as well.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I18.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S6.I18.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I18.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Compatibility between the information on the product boundary charts and the information on the restriction of the chart to the boundary. This follows from the constructions <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx1" title="" class="ltx_ref">AB21</a>, Section 11]</cite> by incorporating the geometry of the broken trajectories from the thick-and-thin decomposition of the domains.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I18.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S6.I18.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I18.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The compatibility with collars follows from the construction.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S6.SS3.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">By examing conditions of Definition <a href="#S3.Thmthm36" title="Definition 3.36. ‣ 3.6. Normal complex structure and orientations on flow categories ‣ 3. Abstract constructions of chain complexes and maps over the integers ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.36</span></a> we obtained a normal complex structure on this (further stabilized) D-chart lift of <math id="S6.SS3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(T^{\rm Floer})^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>Floer</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(T^{\rm Floer})^{+}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS3.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS3.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">For any capped orbit <math id="S6.SS3.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\in T^{\rm Floer}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>Floer</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in T^{\rm Floer}</annotation></semantics></math>, we define its associated virtual vector space to be</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex93" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex93.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(V_{p}^{+},V_{p}^{-}):=(V_{\underline{\smash{p}}}^{+},V_{\underline{\smash{p}}}^{-})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><munder accentunder="true"><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><munder accentunder="true"><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(V_{p}^{+},V_{p}^{-}):=(V_{\underline{\smash{p}}}^{+},V_{\underline{\smash{p}}}^{-}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS3.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the right hand side is constructed before Lemma <a href="#S6.Thmthm23" title="Lemma 6.23. ‣ 6.2.2. Vertical stable complex structures ‣ 6.2. Pre-smoothing operations and stable complex structures ‣ 6. Smoothing ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.23</span></a>. Then the existence of orientation (Definition <a href="#S3.Thmthm43" title="Definition 3.43. ‣ 3.6. Normal complex structure and orientations on flow categories ‣ 3. Abstract constructions of chain complexes and maps over the integers ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.43</span></a>) is a classical result in Floer theory <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx10" title="" class="ltx_ref">FH93</a>]</cite>. For a modern exposition, the reader could refer to <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Par16</a>, Section C.13]</cite>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="S6.SS3.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">6.3.1. </span>Constructing straightening</h4>

<div id="S6.SS3.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS3.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We sketch how to construct a straightening on the D-chart lift which is compatible with the existing collar and scaffolding structures. This construction relies on the concrete geometric feature of the obstruction bundles. We do not know if instead the straightening can be constructed in a more abstract level.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS3.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS3.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We start with moduli spaces without boundary or corners. Let <math id="S6.SS3.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> be the D-chart. Then by the method of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx6" title="" class="ltx_ref">BX22</a>, Lemma 3.15, Lemma 3.20]</cite>, one can construct a straightening on the pair <math id="S6.SS3.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathcal{U}}_{pq},{\mathcal{E}}_{pq})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathcal{U}}_{pq},{\mathcal{E}}_{pq})</annotation></semantics></math>. Indeed, notice that there are a sequence of obstruction bundles <math id="S6.SS3.SSS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{E}}_{pq}^{(d)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{E}}_{pq}^{(d)}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S6.SS3.SSS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq d_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq d_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>. We can actually construct, not just a connection on <math id="S6.SS3.SSS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{E}}_{pq}^{(d_{0})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{E}}_{pq}^{(d_{0})}</annotation></semantics></math> for the lowest <math id="S6.SS3.SSS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{0}=d_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{0}=d_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> (which is required for straightening), but actually a sequence of metrics on all <math id="S6.SS3.SSS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{E}}_{pq}^{(d)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{E}}_{pq}^{(d)}</annotation></semantics></math> and metric connections such that the natural inclusion <math id="S6.SS3.SSS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{E}}_{pq}^{(d)}\hookrightarrow{\mathcal{E}}_{pq}^{(d^{\prime})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">↪</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{E}}_{pq}^{(d)}\hookrightarrow{\mathcal{E}}_{pq}^{(d^{\prime})}</annotation></semantics></math> (for <math id="S6.SS3.SSS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d&lt;d^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d&lt;d^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>) preserves the metric and connection.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS3.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS3.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Inductively, suppose we have constructed such compatible structures for all <math id="S6.SS3.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{rs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{rs}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S6.SS3.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{rs}&lt;d_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{rs}&lt;d_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>. These structures induce metrics and metric connections on the difference bundles <math id="S6.SS3.SSS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}_{\beta\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}_{\beta\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>. Now consider the chart <math id="S6.SS3.SSS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>. Over a lowest stratum <math id="S6.SS3.SSS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\alpha=pr_{1}\cdots r_{l}q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=pr_{1}\cdots r_{l}q</annotation></semantics></math>, the existing structures induce metrics and metric connections on <math id="S6.SS3.SSS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{E}}_{\beta}^{(d)}|_{{\mathcal{U}}_{\alpha}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{E}}_{\beta}^{(d)}|_{{\mathcal{U}}_{\alpha}}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S6.SS3.SSS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq d_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq d_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> and proper strata between <math id="S6.SS3.SSS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS3.SSS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="pq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">pq</annotation></semantics></math>. We would like to extend the metric and connection to <math id="S6.SS3.SSS1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{E}}_{pq}^{(d)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{E}}_{pq}^{(d)}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S6.SS3.SSS1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{U}}_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{U}}_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S6.SS3.SSS1.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq d_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq d_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>. Starting from the lowest <math id="S6.SS3.SSS1.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{0}=d_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{0}=d_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>. Properties proved in Lemma <a href="#S5.Thmthm54" title="Lemma 5.54. ‣ 5.4.4. More on obstruction bundles ‣ 5.4. Global chart construction III ‣ 5. Global Kuranishi charts on Floer moduli spaces ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.54</span></a> shows that we can first extend the metric and metric connection to the sum <math id="S6.SS3.SSS1.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{E}}_{pr_{l}\to pq}^{(d_{0})}+{\mathcal{E}}_{r_{1}q\to pq}^{(d_{0})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{E}}_{pr_{l}\to pq}^{(d_{0})}+{\mathcal{E}}_{r_{1}q\to pq}^{(d_{0})}</annotation></semantics></math>. This will be compatible with all existing metrics and connections. Then we extend (arbitrarily but satisfying the requirement for straightening) to <math id="S6.SS3.SSS1.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{E}}_{pq}^{(d_{0})}|_{{\mathcal{U}}_{\alpha}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{E}}_{pq}^{(d_{0})}|_{{\mathcal{U}}_{\alpha}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then it induces a metric and connection on the difference bundle <math id="S6.SS3.SSS1.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}_{pq,\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}_{pq,\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>. Via the stabilization map from <math id="S6.SS3.SSS1.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{U}}_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{U}}_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S6.SS3.SSS1.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{\alpha}{\mathcal{U}}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{\alpha}{\mathcal{U}}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>, one obtains a metric on <math id="S6.SS3.SSS1.p3.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{\alpha}{\mathcal{U}}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{\alpha}{\mathcal{U}}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> which is straightened. Next, we can inductively construct metrics and connections on <math id="S6.SS3.SSS1.p3.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{E}}_{pq}^{(d)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{E}}_{pq}^{(d)}</annotation></semantics></math> for higher <math id="S6.SS3.SSS1.p3.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>. Once we finished for the lowest stratum <math id="S6.SS3.SSS1.p3.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, we can use the collar structure to extend to all nearby higher strata. For a next stratum <math id="S6.SS3.SSS1.p3.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>, we carry out the induction from <math id="S6.SS3.SSS1.p3.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> above again. We omit the details.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.4. </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S6.Thmthm31" title="Theorem 6.31. ‣ 6.3. The main theorem about smoothing ‣ 6. Smoothing ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.31</span></a></h3>

<div id="S6.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To save notations, we remove all the superscript “<sup id="S6.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_sup">+</sup>” which indicates the outer-collaring. Instead, we keep in mind that all objects and structures have corresponding collar structures or respect the collar structure.</p>
</div>
<section id="S6.SS4.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">6.4.1. </span>Smoothing charts without boundary</h4>

<div id="S6.SS4.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS4.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Consider a moduli space <math id="S6.SS4.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> of Floer trajectories which has no codimension one strata. Let <math id="S6.SS4.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{pq}=(G_{pq},V_{pq},E_{pq},S_{pq})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{pq}=(G_{pq},V_{pq},E_{pq},S_{pq})</annotation></semantics></math> be the global Kuranishi chart constructed. Then <math id="S6.SS4.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> has no boundary or corner and one can apply Lashof’s smoothing theory directly. In this case there is no outer-collaring to the chart. The projection <math id="S6.SS4.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{pq}:V_{pq}\to B_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{pq}:V_{pq}\to B_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="S6.SS4.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant <math id="S6.SS4.SSS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{1}_{\rm loc}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>loc</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{1}_{\rm loc}</annotation></semantics></math> fiberwise smooth topological submersion. Then by the existence of <math id="S6.SS4.SSS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant fiberwise submersions (Lemma <a href="#S6.Thmthm21" title="Lemma 6.21. ‣ 6.1.4. Fiberwise submersions ‣ 6.1. Preliminaries ‣ 6. Smoothing ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.21</span></a>), one can choose a <math id="S6.SS4.SSS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant fiberwise submersion of <math id="S6.SS4.SSS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> which induces an isotopy class of <math id="S6.SS4.SSS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>-vector bundle reductions of <math id="S6.SS4.SSS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\mu}V_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\mu}V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>. By Lashof’s theorem (Theorem <a href="#S6.Thmthm9" title="Theorem 6.9. ‣ 6.1.2. Stable equivariant smoothings ‣ 6.1. Preliminaries ‣ 6. Smoothing ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.9</span></a>) on stable <math id="S6.SS4.SSS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-smoothings, there exists a stable <math id="S6.SS4.SSS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>-smoothing on <math id="S6.SS4.SSS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., a finite-dimensional orthogonal representation <math id="S6.SS4.SSS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S6.SS4.SSS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> and a <math id="S6.SS4.SSS1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>-invariant smooth structure on the product</p>
<table id="S6.Ex94" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex94.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}_{pq}:=V_{pq}\times{\bm{R}}_{pq}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}_{pq}:=V_{pq}\times{\bm{R}}_{pq}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS4.SSS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S6.SS4.SSS1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\pi}_{pq}:\widehat{V}_{pq}\to B_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\pi}_{pq}:\widehat{V}_{pq}\to B_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> be composition <math id="S6.SS4.SSS1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}_{pq}\to V_{pq}\to B_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}_{pq}\to V_{pq}\to B_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then there is an isomorphism of <math id="S6.SS4.SSS1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant vector bundles</p>
<table id="S6.Ex95" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex95.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\widehat{V}_{pq}\cong T^{\rm vt}\widehat{V}_{pq}\oplus\widehat{\pi}_{pq}^{*}TB_{pq}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>vt</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\widehat{V}_{pq}\cong T^{\rm vt}\widehat{V}_{pq}\oplus\widehat{\pi}_{pq}^{*}TB_{pq}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS4.SSS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">(However, the projection <math id="S6.SS4.SSS1.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\pi}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\pi}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> may not be smooth and the fibers may not be smooth submanifolds.)</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS4.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS4.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Moreover one can give smooth structures on the obstruction bundles. Indeed, one can inductively construct a structure of smooth equivariant <math id="S6.SS4.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(n)</annotation></semantics></math>-bundles on <math id="S6.SS4.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{O}_{pq}^{(d)}\to\widehat{V}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{O}_{pq}^{(d)}\to\widehat{V}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S6.SS4.SSS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq d_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq d_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S6.SS4.SSS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{O}_{pq}^{(d)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{O}_{pq}^{(d)}</annotation></semantics></math> is a smooth subbundle of <math id="S6.SS4.SSS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{O}_{pq}^{(d+1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{O}_{pq}^{(d+1)}</annotation></semantics></math> by smoothing the relevant equivariant classifying map. The bundle <math id="S6.SS4.SSS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{R}_{pq}\to\widehat{V}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{R}_{pq}\to\widehat{V}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is the trivial bundle with fiber <math id="S6.SS4.SSS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> automatically has a smooth structure. We also use the inner product on <math id="S6.SS4.SSS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> to equip the bundle <math id="S6.SS4.SSS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{R}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{R}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> with an inner product structure, which is a smooth inner product.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS4.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">6.4.2. </span>Smoothing charts with boundary and corners</h4>

<div id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Now consider a chart <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{pq}=(G_{pq},V_{pq},E_{pq},S_{pq})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{pq}=(G_{pq},V_{pq},E_{pq},S_{pq})</annotation></semantics></math>. We have assumed that <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> has a collar structure which was actually constructed via outer-collaring. We need to construct a stable smoothing which is of “product type” near the boundary and which extends the existing stable smoothings. We first state the induction hypothesis. As an initial remark, we induct on the energy of the moduli spaces <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Induction Hypothesis I. Stabilization.</span> Suppose we have the following data.</p>
<ol id="S6.I19" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S6.I19.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S6.I19.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I19.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">An orthogonal <math id="S6.I19.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{rs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{rs}</annotation></semantics></math>-representation <math id="S6.I19.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{rs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{rs}</annotation></semantics></math> for each <math id="S6.I19.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="rs" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">rs</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S6.I19.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{rs}&lt;d_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{rs}&lt;d_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>. We define a bundle</p>
<table id="S6.Ex96" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex96.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{uv\to rs}^{\sim}\to\partial^{ruvs}V_{rs}\ {\rm whenever}\ ruvs\in{\mathbb{A}}_{rs}^{\rm Floer}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>∼</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>whenever</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>𝔸</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi>Floer</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{uv\to rs}^{\sim}\to\partial^{ruvs}V_{rs}\ {\rm whenever}\ ruvs\in{\mathbb{A}}_{rs}^{\rm Floer}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I19.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">as follows. Consider the product <math id="S6.I19.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{ruvs}=V_{ru}\times V_{uv}\times V_{vs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{ruvs}=V_{ru}\times V_{uv}\times V_{vs}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then the trivial bundle <math id="S6.I19.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{uv}=V_{uv}\times{\bm{R}}_{uv}\to V_{uv}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{uv}=V_{uv}\times{\bm{R}}_{uv}\to V_{uv}</annotation></semantics></math> is pulled back to <math id="S6.I19.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{ruvs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{ruvs}</annotation></semantics></math>. Via the stabilization map <math id="S6.I19.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm Stab}_{F_{rs,ruvs}}(V_{ruvs})\hookrightarrow\partial^{ruvs}V_{rs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Stab</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">↪</mo><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm Stab}_{F_{rs,ruvs}}(V_{ruvs})\hookrightarrow\partial^{ruvs}V_{rs}</annotation></semantics></math> this trivial bundle is pulled back to a trivial bundle. Then using the <math id="S6.I19.i1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{rs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{rs}</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariantization we obtain a not-necessarily-trivial vector bundle</p>
<table id="S6.Ex97" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex97.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{uv\to rs}^{\sim}\to\partial^{ruvs}V_{rs}\cong G_{rs}\times_{G_{ruvs}}({\rm Stab}_{F_{rs,ruvs}}(V_{ruvs}))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>∼</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Stab</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{uv\to rs}^{\sim}\to\partial^{ruvs}V_{rs}\cong G_{rs}\times_{G_{ruvs}}({\rm Stab}_{F_{rs,ruvs}}(V_{ruvs})).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I19.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S6.I19.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I19.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A <math id="S6.I19.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{rs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{rs}</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant bundle embedding</p>
<table id="S6.Ex98" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex98.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{uv\to rs}:R_{uv\to rs}\to R_{rs}|_{\partial^{ruvs}V_{rs}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{uv\to rs}:R_{uv\to rs}\to R_{rs}|_{\partial^{ruvs}V_{rs}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I19.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S6.I19.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I19.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each <math id="S6.I19.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\alpha=ru_{1}\cdots u_{l}s\in{\mathbb{A}}_{rs}^{\rm Floer}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>r</mi><mi>u</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>u</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝔸</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>Floer</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=ru_{1}\cdots u_{l}s\in{\mathbb{A}}_{rs}^{\rm Floer}</annotation></semantics></math>, define a bundle map</p>
<table id="S6.Ex99" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex99.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{rs,\alpha}:R_{\alpha}:=R_{ru_{1}}\boxplus\cdots\boxplus R_{u_{l}s}\to R_{rs}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo>⊞</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>⊞</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{rs,\alpha}:R_{\alpha}:=R_{ru_{1}}\boxplus\cdots\boxplus R_{u_{l}s}\to R_{rs}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I19.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">to be the sum of the maps <math id="S6.I19.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{ru_{1}\to rs},\ldots,\phi_{u_{l}s\to rs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{ru_{1}\to rs},\ldots,\phi_{u_{l}s\to rs}</annotation></semantics></math>. We require that the bundle map is actually a bundle embedding. This induces bundle embeddings</p>
<table id="S6.Ex100" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex100.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{\beta\alpha}:R_{\alpha}\to R_{\beta}\ \alpha\leq\beta,\ \alpha,\beta\in{\mathbb{A}}_{rs}^{\rm Floer}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>𝔸</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi>Floer</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{\beta\alpha}:R_{\alpha}\to R_{\beta}\ \alpha\leq\beta,\ \alpha,\beta\in{\mathbb{A}}_{rs}^{\rm Floer}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I19.i3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">We require that the collection <math id="S6.I19.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{R_{rs}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{R_{rs}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and the collection <math id="S6.I19.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\phi_{\beta\alpha}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\phi_{\beta\alpha}\}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy the requirements for stabilization of a K-chart lift (see Definition <a href="#S6.Thmthm25" title="Definition 6.25. ‣ 6.2.3. Stabilizing the K-chart lift ‣ 6.2. Pre-smoothing operations and stable complex structures ‣ 6. Smoothing ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.25</span></a>) up to level <math id="S6.I19.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., the K-charts for moduli spaces <math id="S6.I19.i3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{rs}^{\rm Floer}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi>Floer</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{rs}^{\rm Floer}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S6.I19.i3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{rs}&lt;d_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{rs}&lt;d_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> are equipped with stabilizations induced from <math id="S6.I19.i3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{rs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{rs}</annotation></semantics></math> with compatibility conditions satisfied.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I19.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(4)</span> 
<div id="S6.I19.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I19.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We also assume we have a <math id="S6.I19.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{rs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{rs}</annotation></semantics></math>-invariant inner product on the trivial bundle <math id="S6.I19.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{rs}\to V_{rs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{rs}\to V_{rs}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S6.I19.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{rs}&lt;d_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{rs}&lt;d_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> such that the bundle maps <math id="S6.I19.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{rs,\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{rs,\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> are all isometric.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Moreover, we assume that the representations <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{rs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{rs}</annotation></semantics></math> and bundle embeddings <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{uv\to rs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{uv\to rs}</annotation></semantics></math> are of the following particular forms. (One can see the discussion in Section <a href="#S6.SS2.SSS4" title="6.2.4. An induction scheme of stabilization ‣ 6.2. Pre-smoothing operations and stable complex structures ‣ 6. Smoothing ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.2.4</span></a> for why we impose the following requirement.)</p>
<ol id="S6.I20" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S6.I20.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S6.I20.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I20.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We have a <math id="S6.I20.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{rs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{rs}</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant orthogonal decomposition</p>
<table id="S6.Ex101" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex101.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{rs}={\bm{R}}_{rs,-}\oplus{\bm{R}}_{rs,0}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo></mrow></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{rs}={\bm{R}}_{rs,-}\oplus{\bm{R}}_{rs,0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I20.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and a <math id="S6.I20.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{rs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{rs}</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant orthogonal decomposition</p>
<table id="S6.Ex102" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex102.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{rs,-}=\bigoplus_{r&lt;w&lt;s}{\bm{R}}_{rs,w}=\bigoplus_{r&lt;w&lt;s}{\bm{R}}_{rw}^{rs}\oplus{\bm{R}}_{ws}^{rs}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⨁</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⨁</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></munder><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{rs,-}=\bigoplus_{r&lt;w&lt;s}{\bm{R}}_{rs,w}=\bigoplus_{r&lt;w&lt;s}{\bm{R}}_{rw}^{rs}\oplus{\bm{R}}_{ws}^{rs}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I20.i1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Intuitively, <math id="S6.I20.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{rs,-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{rs,-}</annotation></semantics></math> comes from lower stratum via Frobenius reciprocity, and <math id="S6.I20.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{rs,0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{rs,0}</annotation></semantics></math> is chosen so that a relative smoothing exists. Then one has the (trivial) bundles <math id="S6.I20.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{rs,-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{rs,-}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.I20.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{rs,0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{rs,0}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.I20.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{rw}^{rs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{rw}^{rs}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.I20.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{ws}^{rs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{ws}^{rs}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S6.I20.i1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{rs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{rs}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I20.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S6.I20.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I20.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Whenever <math id="S6.I20.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r&lt;w&lt;s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r&lt;w&lt;s</annotation></semantics></math>, the representations <math id="S6.I20.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{rw}^{rs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{rw}^{rs}</annotation></semantics></math> resp. <math id="S6.I20.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{ws}^{rs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{ws}^{rs}</annotation></semantics></math> contains <math id="S6.I20.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{rw}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{rw}</annotation></semantics></math> resp. <math id="S6.I20.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{ws}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{ws}</annotation></semantics></math> as orthogonal subrepresentations of <math id="S6.I20.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{rw}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{rw}</annotation></semantics></math> resp. <math id="S6.I20.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{ws}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{ws}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I20.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S6.I20.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I20.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For all <math id="S6.I20.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="uv\prec rs" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>≺</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">uv\prec rs</annotation></semantics></math> (which implies <math id="S6.I20.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\leq u&lt;v\leq s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\leq u&lt;v\leq s</annotation></semantics></math>), abbreviate <math id="S6.I20.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{uv}=\phi_{uv\to rs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{uv}=\phi_{uv\to rs}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then the range of <math id="S6.I20.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{uv}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{uv}</annotation></semantics></math> is contained in <math id="S6.I20.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{rs,-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{rs,-}</annotation></semantics></math> and can be written as</p>
<table id="S6.Ex103" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex103.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{uv}=\bigoplus_{r&lt;w&lt;s}\phi_{uv,w},\ \phi_{uv,w}:R_{uv\to rs}\to R_{rs,w}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⨁</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{uv}=\bigoplus_{r&lt;w&lt;s}\phi_{uv,w},\ \phi_{uv,w}:R_{uv\to rs}\to R_{rs,w}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I20.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Moreover, for each <math id="S6.I20.i3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>, the map <math id="S6.I20.i3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{uv,w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{uv,w}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the following conditions. We write <math id="S6.I20.i3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{uv,w}:R_{uv\to rs}\to R_{rs,w}=R_{rw}^{rs}\oplus R_{ws}^{rs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>⊕</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{uv,w}:R_{uv\to rs}\to R_{rs,w}=R_{rw}^{rs}\oplus R_{ws}^{rs}</annotation></semantics></math> as the sum <math id="S6.I20.i3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{uv,rw}\oplus\phi_{uv,ws}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{uv,rw}\oplus\phi_{uv,ws}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<ol id="S6.I20.i3.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S6.I20.i3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(a)</span> 
<div id="S6.I20.i3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I20.i3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S6.I20.i3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\leq u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\leq u</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S6.I20.i3.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{uv,rw}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{uv,rw}=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, over the stratum <math id="S6.I20.i3.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{rwuvs}\subset V_{ruvs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{rwuvs}\subset V_{ruvs}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.I20.i3.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{uv,ws}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{uv,ws}</annotation></semantics></math> is induced from the bundle map</p>
<table id="S6.Ex104" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S6.Ex104.m1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_markedasmath" height="69.95" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-53.041805712302825px" version="1.1" viewBox="25.59 53.04 159.54 69.95" width="159.54"><g transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 25.594544242456674 69.95366192695361) translate(0,3.46) translate(25.59,0)"><g transform="translate(-25.59,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.1em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.65" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="42.89"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S6.Ex104.m1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{R_{uv\to ws}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{R_{uv\to ws}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 25.594544242456674 -0.27673578005007266 L 25.594544242456674 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(36.74,0) translate(0,8.46) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-2.42)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.55em;--ltx-fo-height:0.49em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.14em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.73)" width="35.34"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S6.Ex104.m1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\phi_{uv\to ws}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.710em">v</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.710em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.710em">s</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\phi_{uv\to ws}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(100.58,0)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 25.594544242456674 -0.27673578005007266 L 100.5809884752923 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 100.5809884752923 -0.27673578005007266 L 100.5809884752923 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -9.805804155370053 L 0.27673578005007266 -9.805804155370053" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(0,-33.21)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -33.208800332088 L 0.27673578005007266 -9.805804155370053" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -33.208800332088 L 0.27673578005007266 -33.208800332088" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(100.58,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.79em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.53" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="24.79"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S6.Ex104.m1.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{R_{ws}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{R_{ws}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 116.85183619964629 -9.685900096859001 L 117.40530775974644 -9.685900096859001" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(117.13,0) translate(0,-33.21)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 116.85183619964629 -33.208800332088 L 117.40530775974644 -9.685900096859001" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 116.85183619964629 -33.208800332088 L 117.40530775974644 -33.208800332088" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(-23.03,0) translate(0,-43.36) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.73em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.53" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="37.75"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S6.Ex104.m1.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{V_{wuvs}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{V_{wuvs}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 23.02651981339508 -43.63264139549389 L 23.02651981339508 -43.07916983539375" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(100.32,0) translate(0,-43.36)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 23.02651981339508 -43.63264139549389 L 100.31434498965469 -43.07916983539375" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 100.31434498965469 -43.63264139549389 L 100.31434498965469 -43.07916983539375" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(100.32,0) translate(0,-43.36) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.83em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.53" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="25.33"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S6.Ex104.m1.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{V_{ws}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{V_{ws}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I20.i3.I1.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and the linear inclusion <math id="S6.I20.i3.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{ws}\hookrightarrow{\bm{R}}_{ws}^{rs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">↪</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{ws}\hookrightarrow{\bm{R}}_{ws}^{rs}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I20.i3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(b)</span> 
<div id="S6.I20.i3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I20.i3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S6.I20.i3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\geq v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\geq v</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S6.I20.i3.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{uv,ws}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{uv,ws}=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, over the stratum <math id="S6.I20.i3.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{ruvws}\subset V_{ruvs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{ruvws}\subset V_{ruvs}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.I20.i3.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{uv,rw}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{uv,rw}</annotation></semantics></math> is induced from the bundle map</p>
<table id="S6.Ex105" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S6.Ex105.m1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_markedasmath" height="69.95" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-53.041805712302825px" version="1.1" viewBox="25.70 53.04 159.96 69.95" width="159.96"><g transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 25.701041173453284 69.95366192695361) translate(0,3.46) translate(25.7,0)"><g transform="translate(-25.7,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.11em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.65" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="43.1"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S6.Ex105.m1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{R_{uv\to rw}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{R_{uv\to rw}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 25.701041173453284 -0.27673578005007266 L 25.701041173453284 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(36.73,0) translate(0,8.46) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-2.42)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.57em;--ltx-fo-height:0.49em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.14em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.73)" width="35.59"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S6.Ex105.m1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\phi_{uv\to rw}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.710em">v</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.710em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.710em">w</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\phi_{uv\to rw}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(100.69,0)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 25.701041173453284 -0.27673578005007266 L 100.68748540628891 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 100.68748540628891 -0.27673578005007266 L 100.68748540628891 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -9.805804155370053 L 0.27673578005007266 -9.805804155370053" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(0,-33.21)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -33.208800332088 L 0.27673578005007266 -9.805804155370053" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -33.208800332088 L 0.27673578005007266 -33.208800332088" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(100.69,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.81em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.53" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="25.01"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S6.Ex105.m1.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{R_{rw}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{R_{rw}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 117.06483006163951 -9.685900096859001 L 117.61830162173966 -9.685900096859001" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(117.34,0) translate(0,-33.21)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 117.06483006163951 -33.208800332088 L 117.61830162173966 -9.685900096859001" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 117.06483006163951 -33.208800332088 L 117.61830162173966 -33.208800332088" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(-23.13,0) translate(0,-43.36) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.74em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.53" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="37.96"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S6.Ex105.m1.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{V_{ruvw}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{V_{ruvw}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 23.13301674439169 -43.63264139549389 L 23.13301674439169 -43.07916983539375" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(100.42,0) translate(0,-43.36)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 23.13301674439169 -43.63264139549389 L 100.42084192065128 -43.07916983539375" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 100.42084192065128 -43.63264139549389 L 100.42084192065128 -43.07916983539375" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(100.42,0) translate(0,-43.36) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.85em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.53" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="25.54"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S6.Ex105.m1.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{V_{rw}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{V_{rw}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I20.i3.I1.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and the linear inclusion <math id="S6.I20.i3.I1.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{rw}\hookrightarrow{\bm{R}}_{rw}^{rs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">↪</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{rw}\hookrightarrow{\bm{R}}_{rw}^{rs}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I20.i3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(c)</span> 
<div id="S6.I20.i3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I20.i3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S6.I20.i3.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u&lt;w&lt;v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u&lt;w&lt;v</annotation></semantics></math>, then the following is true. Consider the inclusion</p>
<table id="S6.Ex106" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex106.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{uw}\oplus{\bm{R}}_{wv}\hookrightarrow{\bm{R}}_{uw}^{uv}\oplus{\bm{R}}_{wv}^{uv}\hookrightarrow{\bm{R}}_{uv}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↪</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>⊕</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↪</mo><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{uw}\oplus{\bm{R}}_{wv}\hookrightarrow{\bm{R}}_{uw}^{uv}\oplus{\bm{R}}_{wv}^{uv}\hookrightarrow{\bm{R}}_{uv}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I20.i3.I1.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The orthogonal projection</p>
<table id="S6.Ex107" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex107.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{uv}\to{\bm{R}}_{uw}\oplus{\bm{R}}_{wv}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{uv}\to{\bm{R}}_{uw}\oplus{\bm{R}}_{wv}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I20.i3.I1.i3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">is <math id="S6.I20.i3.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{uwv}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{uwv}</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant, hence induces a bundle map</p>
<table id="S6.Ex108" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex108.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{uv}|_{V_{uwv}}\to R_{uw}\boxplus R_{wv}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊞</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{uv}|_{V_{uwv}}\to R_{uw}\boxplus R_{wv}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I20.i3.I1.i3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">On the other hand, there are bundle embeddings</p>
<table id="S6.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.Ex109"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex109.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ R_{uw\to rw}\hookrightarrow R_{rw}\hookrightarrow R_{rw}^{rs},\ " display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">↪</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">↪</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ R_{uw\to rw}\hookrightarrow R_{rw}\hookrightarrow R_{rw}^{rs},\ </annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex109.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ R_{wv\to ws}\hookrightarrow R_{ws}\hookrightarrow R_{ws}^{rs}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">↪</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">↪</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ R_{wv\to ws}\hookrightarrow R_{ws}\hookrightarrow R_{ws}^{rs}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I20.i3.I1.i3.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Then over the stratum <math id="S6.I20.i3.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{ruwvs}\subset V_{ruvs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{ruwvs}\subset V_{ruvs}</annotation></semantics></math>, the map <math id="S6.I20.i3.I1.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{uv,w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{uv,w}</annotation></semantics></math> is the composition</p>
<table id="S6.Ex110" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex110.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\underline{\smash{uv\to rs}}}|_{V_{\underline{\smash{ruwvs}}}}\to R_{\underline{\smash{uw\to rs}}}\oplus R_{\underline{\smash{wv\to rs}}}\to R_{rw}^{rs}\oplus R_{ws}^{rs}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>⊕</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\underline{\smash{uv\to rs}}}|_{V_{\underline{\smash{ruwvs}}}}\to R_{\underline{\smash{uw\to rs}}}\oplus R_{\underline{\smash{wv\to rs}}}\to R_{rw}^{rs}\oplus R_{ws}^{rs}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I20.i3.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(d)</span> 
<div id="S6.I20.i3.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I20.i3.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If none of the above happends, then <math id="S6.I20.i3.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{uv,w}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{uv,w}=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Moreover, the bundles and bundle maps will be added with <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\cdot}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mo>⋅</mo><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\cdot}</annotation></semantics></math> when lifted to the stabilizations <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}_{rs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}_{rs}</annotation></semantics></math>. Such lifts are canonical.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Induction Hypothesis II. Fiberwise submersion.</span> Whenever <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{rs}&lt;d_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{rs}&lt;d_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have chosen a <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{rs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{rs}</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant fiberwise submersion (Definition <a href="#S6.Thmthm18" title="Definition 6.18. ‣ 6.1.4. Fiberwise submersions ‣ 6.1. Preliminaries ‣ 6. Smoothing ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.18</span></a>) of <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\pi}_{rs}:\widehat{V}_{rs}\to B_{rs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\pi}_{rs}:\widehat{V}_{rs}\to B_{rs}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is a microbundle isomorphism</p>
<table id="S6.Ex111" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex111.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\mu}\widehat{V}_{rs}\cong T^{\rm vt}_{\mu}\widehat{V}_{rs}\oplus\widehat{\pi}_{rs}^{*}T_{\mu}B_{d_{rs}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi>μ</mi><mi>vt</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\mu}\widehat{V}_{rs}\cong T^{\rm vt}_{\mu}\widehat{V}_{rs}\oplus\widehat{\pi}_{rs}^{*}T_{\mu}B_{d_{rs}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">which is the canonical projection map on the second component. Together with the structure of <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\rm loc}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>loc</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\rm loc}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> fiberwise smooth <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{rs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{rs}</annotation></semantics></math>-bundle on <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\pi}_{rs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\pi}_{rs}</annotation></semantics></math>, this provides an isotopy class of vector bundle lifts</p>
<table id="S6.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\rm vt}\widehat{V}_{rs}\oplus\widehat{\pi}_{rs}^{*}TB_{d_{rs}}\to T_{\mu}\widehat{V}_{rs}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>vt</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\rm vt}\widehat{V}_{rs}\oplus\widehat{\pi}_{rs}^{*}TB_{d_{rs}}\to T_{\mu}\widehat{V}_{rs},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6.8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p">where the isotopy class is fixed by Equation (<a href="#S6.E3" title="In 6.1.4. Fiberwise submersions ‣ 6.1. Preliminaries ‣ 6. Smoothing ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.3</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Induction Hypothesis III. Stable smoothings and bundle smoothings.</span> Whenever <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{rs}&lt;d_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{rs}&lt;d_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have chosen a <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{rs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{rs}</annotation></semantics></math>-invariant smoothing on <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}_{rs}:=V_{rs}\times{\bm{R}}_{rs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}_{rs}:=V_{rs}\times{\bm{R}}_{rs}</annotation></semantics></math> in the <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{rs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{rs}</annotation></semantics></math>-isotopy class corresponding to stable isotopy class of the vector bundle lift (<a href="#S6.E8" title="In 6.4.2. Smoothing charts with boundary and corners ‣ 6.4. Proof of Theorem ‣ 6. Smoothing ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.8</span></a>). Moreover, we have chosen a structure of smooth <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{rs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{rs}</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(n)</annotation></semantics></math>-bundle on <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{O}_{rs}^{(d)}\to\widehat{V}_{rs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{O}_{rs}^{(d)}\to\widehat{V}_{rs}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq d_{rs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq d_{rs}</annotation></semantics></math> and a structure of smooth <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{rs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{rs}</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(n)</annotation></semantics></math>-bundle on <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{R}_{rs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{R}_{rs}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Before we state the conditions about these structures, we summarize a few consequences of these induction hypotheses. First, the stable smoothings induce, for each stratum <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\alpha=pr_{1}\cdots r_{l}q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=pr_{1}\cdots r_{l}q</annotation></semantics></math>, a <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant smooth structure on the product</p>
<table id="S6.Ex112" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex112.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widehat{V}_{\alpha}=\widehat{V}_{pr_{1}}\times\cdots\times\widehat{V}_{r_{k}q}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.055em">⋯</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}_{\alpha}=\widehat{V}_{pr_{1}}\times\cdots\times\widehat{V}_{r_{k}q}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p">and hence a <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant smooth structure on <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}_{\alpha}^{\sim}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>α</mi><mo>∼</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}_{\alpha}^{\sim}</annotation></semantics></math> by taking the equivariantization. Second, the smooth structures on the vector bundles induce smooth structures on the product bundles <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{O}_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{O}_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{R}_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{R}_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>. Third, as the bundle <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{rs}\to V_{rs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{rs}\to V_{rs}</annotation></semantics></math> is trivial, the pullback <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{Q}_{rs}\to\widehat{V}_{rs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{Q}_{rs}\to\widehat{V}_{rs}</annotation></semantics></math> is automatically smooth. Similarly, the bundle</p>
<table id="S6.Ex113" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex113.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{Q}_{rs,\alpha}=(\widehat{Q}_{\alpha})^{\bot}\to\widehat{V}_{\alpha}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊥</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{Q}_{rs,\alpha}=(\widehat{Q}_{\alpha})^{\bot}\to\widehat{V}_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p5.3" class="ltx_p">is smooth because it comes from a product bundle.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Now we state the conditions.</p>
<ol id="S6.I21" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S6.I21.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S6.I21.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I21.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The bundle embedding</p>
<table id="S6.Ex114" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex114.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\phi}_{\beta\alpha}:\widehat{R}_{\alpha}\to\widehat{R}_{\beta}|_{\partial^{\alpha}\widehat{V}_{\beta}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\phi}_{\beta\alpha}:\widehat{R}_{\alpha}\to\widehat{R}_{\beta}|_{\partial^{\alpha}\widehat{V}_{\beta}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I21.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">is smooth.<span id="footnote19" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">19</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">19</sup>
                      <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">19</span>
                      
                      
                      
                    This is not automatic as this bundle embedding is not purely induced from linear maps between representation spaces.</span></span></span> This implies that the orthogonal complement</p>
<table id="S6.Ex115" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex115.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{R}_{rs,\alpha}\to\widehat{V}_{\alpha}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{R}_{rs,\alpha}\to\widehat{V}_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I21.i1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">is a smooth bundle.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I21.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S6.I21.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I21.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Whenever <math id="S6.I21.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{\prime}&gt;d\geq d_{rs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{\prime}&gt;d\geq d_{rs}</annotation></semantics></math>, the natural bundle embedding <math id="S6.I21.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{O}_{rs}^{(d)}\to\widehat{O}_{rs}^{(d^{\prime})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{O}_{rs}^{(d)}\to\widehat{O}_{rs}^{(d^{\prime})}</annotation></semantics></math> induced from (<a href="#S5.E34" title="In 5.3.3. Multi-layered thickening ‣ 5.3. Global chart construction II ‣ 5. Global Kuranishi charts on Floer moduli spaces ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.34</span></a>) is smooth.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I21.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S6.I21.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I21.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For all <math id="S6.I21.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq d_{rs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq d_{rs}</annotation></semantics></math>, the bundle embedding</p>
<table id="S6.Ex116" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex116.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\phi}_{uv\to rs}:\widehat{O}_{uv\to rs}^{(d)}\to\widehat{O}_{rs}^{(d)}|_{\partial^{ruvs}V_{rs}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\phi}_{uv\to rs}:\widehat{O}_{uv\to rs}^{(d)}\to\widehat{O}_{rs}^{(d)}|_{\partial^{ruvs}V_{rs}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I21.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">is smooth. This implies that (when <math id="S6.I21.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=d_{rs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=d_{rs}</annotation></semantics></math>) the orthogonal complement</p>
<table id="S6.Ex117" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex117.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{O}_{rs,\alpha}\to V_{\alpha}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{O}_{rs,\alpha}\to V_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I21.i3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">is a smooth bundle.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I21.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(4)</span> 
<div id="S6.I21.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I21.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">It follows that</p>
<table id="S6.Ex118" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex118.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{F}_{rs,\alpha}:=\widehat{O}_{rs,\alpha}\oplus\widehat{Q}_{rs,\alpha}\oplus\widehat{R}_{rs,\alpha}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{F}_{rs,\alpha}:=\widehat{O}_{rs,\alpha}\oplus\widehat{Q}_{rs,\alpha}\oplus\widehat{R}_{rs,\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I21.i4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">over the smooth manifold with corners <math id="S6.I21.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> is smooth. Then we require that the stabilization map</p>
<table id="S6.Ex119" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex119.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\theta}_{rs,\alpha}:{\rm Stab}_{\widehat{F}_{rs,\alpha}}(\widehat{V}_{\alpha})\to\partial^{\alpha}\widehat{V}_{rs}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Stab</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\theta}_{rs,\alpha}:{\rm Stab}_{\widehat{F}_{rs,\alpha}}(\widehat{V}_{\alpha})\to\partial^{\alpha}\widehat{V}_{rs}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I21.i4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">is a germ of diffeomorphisms onto an open set. These structures ensure that the projection map</p>
<table id="S6.Ex120" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex120.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\pi}_{rs,\alpha}:\partial^{\alpha}V_{rs}\to\widehat{V}_{\alpha}^{\sim}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.111em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>α</mi><mo>∼</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\pi}_{rs,\alpha}:\partial^{\alpha}V_{rs}\to\widehat{V}_{\alpha}^{\sim}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I21.i4.p1.4" class="ltx_p">is smooth.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I21.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(5)</span> 
<div id="S6.I21.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I21.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For all <math id="S6.I21.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq d_{rs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq d_{rs}</annotation></semantics></math>, the bundle isomorphism</p>
<table id="S6.Ex121" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex121.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\psi}_{rs,\alpha}:\widehat{\pi}_{rs,\alpha}^{*}\Big(\widehat{O}_{rs}^{(d)}|_{\widehat{V}_{\alpha}^{\sim}}\Big)\to\widehat{O}_{rs}^{(d)}|_{\partial^{\alpha}V_{rs}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ψ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><msub><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>α</mi><mo>∼</mo></msubsup></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\psi}_{rs,\alpha}:\widehat{\pi}_{rs,\alpha}^{*}\Big(\widehat{O}_{rs}^{(d)}|_{\widehat{V}_{\alpha}^{\sim}}\Big)\to\widehat{O}_{rs}^{(d)}|_{\partial^{\alpha}V_{rs}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I21.i5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">is smooth.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I21.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(6)</span> 
<div id="S6.I21.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I21.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The existing smoothings (on both domains and bundles) respect the corner structures. Namely, for all <math id="S6.I21.i6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="rs" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">rs</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S6.I21.i6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{rs}&lt;d_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{rs}&lt;d_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>, item (B) of Theorem <a href="#S6.Thmthm31" title="Theorem 6.31. ‣ 6.3. The main theorem about smoothing ‣ 6. Smoothing ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.31</span></a> is satisfied.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Now we start to construct the stabilized smoothings corresponding to the Kuranishi chart <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Inductive Construction I. We construct an orthogonal <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>-space <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> (which defines the trivial bundle <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{pq}\to V_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{pq}\to V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>) and bundle embeddings</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex122" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex122.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{rs\to pq}:R_{rs\to pq}\to R_{pq}|_{\partial^{prsq}V_{pq}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{rs\to pq}:R_{rs\to pq}\to R_{pq}|_{\partial^{prsq}V_{pq}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">which, together with the existing stabilizations and bundle embeddings, satisfy the conditions required for stabilizations.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S6.I22" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S6.I22.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S6.I22.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I22.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Firstly, we need to find an orthogonal <math id="S6.I22.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>-representation <math id="S6.I22.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> such that the stabilization <math id="S6.I22.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{pq}=V_{pq}\times{\bm{R}}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{pq}=V_{pq}\times{\bm{R}}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> receives embeddings from <math id="S6.I22.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S6.I22.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in{\mathbb{A}}^{\rm Floer}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>𝔸</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>Floer</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in{\mathbb{A}}^{\rm Floer}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.I22.i1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I22.i1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To start, for each <math id="S6.I22.i1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;w&lt;q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;w&lt;q</annotation></semantics></math>, consider the <math id="S6.I22.i1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pw}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pw}</annotation></semantics></math>-representation <math id="S6.I22.i1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{pw}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{pw}</annotation></semantics></math> and the <math id="S6.I22.i1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{wq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{wq}</annotation></semantics></math>-representation <math id="S6.I22.i1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{wq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{wq}</annotation></semantics></math> granted by the induction hypothesis. By Frobenius reciprocity, there exist an orthogonal <math id="S6.I22.i1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>-representation <math id="S6.I22.i1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{pw}^{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{pw}^{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> which contains <math id="S6.I22.i1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{pw}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{pw}</annotation></semantics></math> as a subrepresentation of <math id="S6.I22.i1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pw}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pw}</annotation></semantics></math>, and an orthogonal <math id="S6.I22.i1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>-representation <math id="S6.I22.i1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{wq}^{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{wq}^{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> which contains <math id="S6.I22.i1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{wq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{wq}</annotation></semantics></math> as a subrepresentation of <math id="S6.I22.i1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{wq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{wq}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then define</p>
<table id="S6.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{pq}:=\bigoplus_{p&lt;w&lt;q}{\bm{R}}_{pw}^{pq}\oplus{\bm{R}}_{wq}^{pq}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⨁</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></munder><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{pq}:=\bigoplus_{p&lt;w&lt;q}{\bm{R}}_{pw}^{pq}\oplus{\bm{R}}_{wq}^{pq}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6.9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I22.i1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">which is an orthogonal <math id="S6.I22.i1.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>-space. Now we define the bundle embeddings</p>
<table id="S6.Ex123" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex123.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{rs\to pq}:R_{rs\to pq}\to R_{pq}|_{\partial^{prsq}V_{pq}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{rs\to pq}:R_{rs\to pq}\to R_{pq}|_{\partial^{prsq}V_{pq}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I22.i1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">We abbreviate the decomposition <a href="#S6.E9" title="In item 1 ‣ 6.4.2. Smoothing charts with boundary and corners ‣ 6.4. Proof of Theorem ‣ 6. Smoothing ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.9</span></a> as</p>
<table id="S6.Ex124" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex124.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{pq}=\bigoplus_{w}{\bm{R}}_{pq,w}=\bigoplus_{p&lt;w&lt;q}{\bm{R}}_{pw}^{pq}\oplus{\bm{R}}_{wq}^{pq}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⨁</mo><mi>w</mi></munder><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⨁</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></munder><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{pq}=\bigoplus_{w}{\bm{R}}_{pq,w}=\bigoplus_{p&lt;w&lt;q}{\bm{R}}_{pw}^{pq}\oplus{\bm{R}}_{wq}^{pq}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I22.i1.p2.4" class="ltx_p">Abbreviate the bundle embedding to be defined by <math id="S6.I22.i1.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{rs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{rs}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then we define it to be the direct sum</p>
<table id="S6.Ex125" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex125.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{rs}=\bigoplus_{w}\phi_{rs,w}=\bigoplus_{w}\phi_{rs,pw}\oplus\phi_{rs,wq}\ {\rm where}\ \phi_{rs,w}:R_{rs\to pq}\to R_{pq,w}|_{\partial^{prsq}V_{pq}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⨁</mo><mi>w</mi></munder><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⨁</mo><mi>w</mi></munder><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>where</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{rs}=\bigoplus_{w}\phi_{rs,w}=\bigoplus_{w}\phi_{rs,pw}\oplus\phi_{rs,wq}\ {\rm where}\ \phi_{rs,w}:R_{rs\to pq}\to R_{pq,w}|_{\partial^{prsq}V_{pq}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I22.i1.p2.5" class="ltx_p">In fact, for each <math id="S6.I22.i1.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>, one can define the restriction of <math id="S6.I22.i1.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{rs,w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{rs,w}</annotation></semantics></math> to the corresponding stratum involving <math id="S6.I22.i1.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>, such as <math id="S6.I22.i1.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="pwrsq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">pwrsq</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.I22.i1.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="prswq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">prswq</annotation></semantics></math>, or <math id="S6.I22.i1.p2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="prwsq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">prwsq</annotation></semantics></math> in the form described in <span id="S6.I22.i1.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Induction Hypothesis I</span>. These are all codimension-1 boundary strata of <math id="S6.I22.i1.p2.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="prsq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">prsq</annotation></semantics></math>. Then using the collar structure of existing objects and a cut-off function which only depends on the collar coordinate, one can turn off the corresponding maps <math id="S6.I22.i1.p2.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{rs,w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{rs,w}</annotation></semantics></math> once we go away from this corner. On the other hand, if <math id="S6.I22.i1.p2.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w=r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w=r</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S6.I22.i1.p2.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w=s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w=s</annotation></semantics></math>, we just have a bundle embedding coming from the induction hypothesis. One can check that the newly constructed objects still satisfy the requirement for a stabilization up to level <math id="S6.I22.i1.p2.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> (see Definition <a href="#S6.Thmthm25" title="Definition 6.25. ‣ 6.2.3. Stabilizing the K-chart lift ‣ 6.2. Pre-smoothing operations and stable complex structures ‣ 6. Smoothing ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.25</span></a>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I22.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S6.I22.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I22.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Secondly, we would like to construct an inner product on <math id="S6.I22.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.I22.i2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I22.i2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We start from a minimal <math id="S6.I22.i2.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\alpha=pr_{1}\cdots r_{l}q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=pr_{1}\cdots r_{l}q</annotation></semantics></math>. Notice that inside <math id="S6.I22.i2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{pq}|_{\partial^{\alpha}V_{pq}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{pq}|_{\partial^{\alpha}V_{pq}}</annotation></semantics></math>, there are a collection of embedded subbundles <math id="S6.I22.i2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\beta\to pq}|_{\partial^{\alpha}V_{pq}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\beta\to pq}|_{\partial^{\alpha}V_{pq}}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S6.I22.i2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S6.I22.i2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\leq\beta&lt;pq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\leq\beta&lt;pq</annotation></semantics></math> with an inner product equipped. We first check that, for any pair <math id="S6.I22.i2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta,\beta^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta,\beta^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> of such strata, their inner products agree on the overlap</p>
<table id="S6.Ex126" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex126.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\beta\to pq}\cap R_{\beta^{\prime}\to pq}\subset R_{pq}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\beta\to pq}\cap R_{\beta^{\prime}\to pq}\subset R_{pq}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I22.i2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">In fact the intersection <math id="S6.I22.i2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{\beta}V_{pq}\cap\partial^{\beta^{\prime}}V_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>β</mi></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">∩</mo><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{\beta}V_{pq}\cap\partial^{\beta^{\prime}}V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> is a deeper stratum <math id="S6.I22.i2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{\beta\#\beta^{\prime}}V_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{\beta\#\beta^{\prime}}V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>. Here <math id="S6.I22.i2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\#\beta^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\#\beta^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> stands for the stratum described by the word which includes all the intermediate capped orbits in <math id="S6.I22.i2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.I22.i2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> between <math id="S6.I22.i2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.I22.i2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>. We can in fact check from the explicit construction that</p>
<table id="S6.Ex127" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex127.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\beta\to pq}\cap R_{\beta^{\prime}\to pq}=R_{\beta\#\beta^{\prime}\to pq}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\beta\to pq}\cap R_{\beta^{\prime}\to pq}=R_{\beta\#\beta^{\prime}\to pq}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I22.i2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Hence by induction hypothesis, the inner products agrees on overlaps.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.I22.i2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I22.i2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Now there are two special codimension one strata, <math id="S6.I22.i2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1}=pr_{1}q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1}=pr_{1}q</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.I22.i2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{l}=pr_{l}q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{l}=pr_{l}q</annotation></semantics></math>. We can check that</p>
<table id="S6.Ex128" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex128.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\beta\to pq}\subset R_{\beta_{1}\to pq}+R_{\beta_{l}\to pq}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\beta\to pq}\subset R_{\beta_{1}\to pq}+R_{\beta_{l}\to pq}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I22.i2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Hence we can define an inner product on the sum <math id="S6.I22.i2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\beta_{1}\to pq}+R_{\beta_{l}\to pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\beta_{1}\to pq}+R_{\beta_{l}\to pq}</annotation></semantics></math> which extends the existing ones. Then extend arbitrarily to <math id="S6.I22.i2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> over this stratum.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.I22.i2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I22.i2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Inductively, we can use the collar structure near <math id="S6.I22.i2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> to extend the inner product on <math id="S6.I22.i2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{\alpha}V_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{\alpha}V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> to a neighborhood. Then the same argument above can be applied to construct an inner product inductively on <math id="S6.I22.i2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Inductive Construction II. We construct smooth bundle structures on the obstruction bundles <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{O}_{pq}^{(d)}\to\widehat{V}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{O}_{pq}^{(d)}\to\widehat{V}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq d_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq d_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial\widehat{V}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial\widehat{V}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span> The construction is inductive on strata <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p10.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\alpha=pr_{1}\cdots r_{l}q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=pr_{1}\cdots r_{l}q</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="pq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">pq</annotation></semantics></math>. We start with a minimal <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>. Then there are the vector bundles</p>
<table id="S6.Ex129" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex129.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="O_{\alpha}^{(d)}\to V_{\alpha}=V_{pr_{1}}\times\cdots\times V_{r_{l}q},\ \forall d\geq d_{pq}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>α</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>V</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>V</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.055em">⋯</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>V</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>d</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{\alpha}^{(d)}\to V_{\alpha}=V_{pr_{1}}\times\cdots\times V_{r_{l}q},\ \forall d\geq d_{pq}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p10.2" class="ltx_p">Denote by its pullback to <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> by</p>
<table id="S6.Ex130" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex130.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{O}_{\alpha}^{(d)}\to\widehat{V}_{\alpha}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{O}_{\alpha}^{(d)}\to\widehat{V}_{\alpha}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p10.3" class="ltx_p">The induction hypothesis granted a smooth <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(n)</annotation></semantics></math>-bundle structure on it which is the product of each individual factor. Notice that this is a subbundle of <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{O}_{pq}^{(d)}|_{\widehat{V}_{\alpha}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>α</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{O}_{pq}^{(d)}|_{\widehat{V}_{\alpha}}</annotation></semantics></math>. We would like to extend this smooth structure to a smooth structure on <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{O}_{pq}|_{\widehat{V}_{\alpha}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>α</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{O}_{pq}|_{\widehat{V}_{\alpha}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p11.1" class="ltx_p">Start with <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=d_{0}=d_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=d_{0}=d_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> and remember <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{O}_{pq}=\widehat{O}_{pq}^{(d_{0})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{O}_{pq}=\widehat{O}_{pq}^{(d_{0})}</annotation></semantics></math>. Consider any intermediate stratum <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p11.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\beta=ps_{1}\cdots s_{m}q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=ps_{1}\cdots s_{m}q</annotation></semantics></math>. Then one has the inclusion induced by (<a href="#S5.E53" title="In item (A2) ‣ Proposition 5.64. ‣ 5.8. Constructing scaffolding ‣ 5. Global Kuranishi charts on Floer moduli spaces ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.53</span></a>)</p>
<table id="S6.Ex131" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex131.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{O}_{\alpha}^{(d_{0})}\subset\widehat{O}_{\beta}^{(d_{0})}|_{\widehat{V}_{\alpha}}\subset\widehat{O}_{pq}|_{\widehat{V}_{\alpha}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>α</mi></msub></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>α</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{O}_{\alpha}^{(d_{0})}\subset\widehat{O}_{\beta}^{(d_{0})}|_{\widehat{V}_{\alpha}}\subset\widehat{O}_{pq}|_{\widehat{V}_{\alpha}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p11.2" class="ltx_p">Notice that by the induction hypothesis, the smooth structure on <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{O}_{\beta}^{(d_{0})}|_{\widehat{V}_{\alpha}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>α</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{O}_{\beta}^{(d_{0})}|_{\widehat{V}_{\alpha}}</annotation></semantics></math> extends the smooth structure on <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{O}_{\alpha}^{(d_{0})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{O}_{\alpha}^{(d_{0})}</annotation></semantics></math>. This requires that the smooth structure on <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{O}_{pq}|_{\widehat{V}_{\alpha}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>α</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{O}_{pq}|_{\widehat{V}_{\alpha}}</annotation></semantics></math> needs to be an extension of all such smooth structures. Indeed, consider two codimension one strata, <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="pr_{1}q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">pr_{1}q</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="pr_{l}q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">pr_{l}q</annotation></semantics></math>. Consider the two bundles</p>
<table id="S6.EGx25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.Ex132"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex132.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ \widehat{O}_{pr_{l}\to pq}^{(d_{0})}|_{\widehat{V}_{\alpha}},\ " display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>α</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ \widehat{O}_{pr_{l}\to pq}^{(d_{0})}|_{\widehat{V}_{\alpha}},\ </annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex132.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ \widehat{O}_{r_{1}q\to pq}^{(d_{0})}|_{\widehat{V}_{\alpha}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>α</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ \widehat{O}_{r_{1}q\to pq}^{(d_{0})}|_{\widehat{V}_{\alpha}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p11.3" class="ltx_p">Abbreviate them temporarily by <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{O}_{r_{l}}^{(d_{0})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{O}_{r_{l}}^{(d_{0})}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p11.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{O}_{r_{1}}^{(d_{0})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{O}_{r_{1}}^{(d_{0})}</annotation></semantics></math> respectively. Then it is easy to see that for any intermediate stratum <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>, one has</p>
<table id="S6.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{O}_{\beta}^{(d_{0})}|_{\widehat{V}_{\alpha}}\subset\widehat{O}_{r_{l}}^{(d_{0})}+\widehat{O}_{r_{1}}^{(d_{0})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>α</mi></msub></msub><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{O}_{\beta}^{(d_{0})}|_{\widehat{V}_{\alpha}}\subset\widehat{O}_{r_{l}}^{(d_{0})}+\widehat{O}_{r_{1}}^{(d_{0})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6.10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p11.4" class="ltx_p">Then Lemma <a href="#S6.Thmthm33" title="Lemma 6.33. ‣ 6.4.2. Smoothing charts with boundary and corners ‣ 6.4. Proof of Theorem ‣ 6. Smoothing ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.33</span></a> below provides a smooth structure on the sum <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p11.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{O}_{r_{l}}^{(d_{0})}+\widehat{O}_{r_{1}}^{(d_{0})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{O}_{r_{l}}^{(d_{0})}+\widehat{O}_{r_{1}}^{(d_{0})}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then we extend this extension to <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p11.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{O}_{pq}|_{\widehat{V}_{\alpha}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>α</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{O}_{pq}|_{\widehat{V}_{\alpha}}</annotation></semantics></math> by choosing an arbitrary smooth structure on its orthogonal complement.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmthm33" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmthm33.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 6.33</span></span><span id="S6.Thmthm33.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmthm33.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmthm33.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmthm33.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S6.Thmthm33.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> be a smooth manifold and let <math id="S6.Thmthm33.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E\to M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E\to M</annotation></semantics></math> be a topological vector bundle equipped with an inner product. Let <math id="S6.Thmthm33.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{1},E_{2}\subset E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{1},E_{2}\subset E</annotation></semantics></math> be subbundles such that <math id="S6.Thmthm33.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E=E_{1}+E_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E=E_{1}+E_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, suppose <math id="S6.Thmthm33.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.Thmthm33.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> are equipped with structures of smooth vector bundles with respect to which the restriction of the inner product is smooth, such that the intersection <math id="S6.Thmthm33.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{1}\cap E_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{1}\cap E_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is both a smooth subbundle of <math id="S6.Thmthm33.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and a smooth subbundle of <math id="S6.Thmthm33.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then there exists a unique smooth bundle structure of <math id="S6.Thmthm33.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> which extends the smooth bundle structures on <math id="S6.Thmthm33.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.Thmthm33.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> such that the inner product is smooth.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS4.SSS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">Define a smooth vector bundle <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E^{\prime}\to M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E^{\prime}\to M</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> as</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex133" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex133.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E^{\prime}:=E_{1}^{\prime}\oplus E_{2}^{\prime}\oplus(E_{1}\cap E_{2})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>⊕</mo><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E^{\prime}:=E_{1}^{\prime}\oplus E_{2}^{\prime}\oplus(E_{1}\cap E_{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p12.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p12.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{1}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{1}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> resp. <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{2}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{2}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is the orthogonal complement of <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{1}\cap E_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{1}\cap E_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p12.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> resp. <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p12.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then there is an canonical isometric bundle isomorphism <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p12.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E^{\prime}\to E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E^{\prime}\to E</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p13.1" class="ltx_p">As <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{O}_{pq,\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{O}_{pq,\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> is the orthogonal complement of <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{O}_{\alpha}^{(d_{0})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{O}_{\alpha}^{(d_{0})}</annotation></semantics></math>, the above smooth structure induces a smooth structure on <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{O}_{pq}|_{\widehat{V}_{\alpha}}\to\widehat{V}_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>α</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{O}_{pq}|_{\widehat{V}_{\alpha}}\to\widehat{V}_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>, hence one on <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{O}_{pq,\alpha}\to\widehat{V}_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{O}_{pq,\alpha}\to\widehat{V}_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>. On the other hand, run the same argument as above, one can cook up a smooth <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(n)</annotation></semantics></math>-bundle structure on <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{R}_{pq}|_{\widehat{V}_{\alpha}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>α</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{R}_{pq}|_{\widehat{V}_{\alpha}}</annotation></semantics></math> which extends existing ones. Hence the orthogonal complement <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p13.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{R}_{pq,\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{R}_{pq,\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> is a smooth <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p13.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(n)</annotation></semantics></math>-bundle. The bundle <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p13.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{Q}_{pq,\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{Q}_{pq,\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is essentially trivial, automatically carries a smooth structure. Hence the bundle</p>
<table id="S6.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{F}_{pq,\alpha}=\widehat{O}_{pq,\alpha}\oplus\widehat{Q}_{pq,\alpha}\oplus\widehat{R}_{pq,\alpha}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{F}_{pq,\alpha}=\widehat{O}_{pq,\alpha}\oplus\widehat{Q}_{pq,\alpha}\oplus\widehat{R}_{pq,\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6.11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p13.2" class="ltx_p">is smooth. Then the stabilization map (see (<a href="#S5.E50" title="In item 2 ‣ Proposition 5.64. ‣ 5.8. Constructing scaffolding ‣ 5. Global Kuranishi charts on Floer moduli spaces ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.50</span></a>))</p>
<table id="S6.Ex134" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex134.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\theta}_{pq,\alpha}:{\rm Stab}_{\widehat{F}_{pq,\alpha}}(\widehat{V}_{\alpha})\to\partial^{\alpha}\widehat{V}_{pq}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Stab</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\theta}_{pq,\alpha}:{\rm Stab}_{\widehat{F}_{pq,\alpha}}(\widehat{V}_{\alpha})\to\partial^{\alpha}\widehat{V}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p13.3" class="ltx_p">and its equivariantization induce a smooth structure on the stratum <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p13.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{\alpha}\widehat{V}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{\alpha}\widehat{V}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p14.1" class="ltx_p">Next we can inductively construct smooth structures on the bundle <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{O}_{pq}^{(d)}|_{V_{pq,\underline{\smash{\alpha}}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mrow></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{O}_{pq}^{(d)}|_{V_{pq,\underline{\smash{\alpha}}}}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq d_{0}=d_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq d_{0}=d_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>. This is similar to the construction of inner products. We omit the details. Using equivariantizations and the bundle isomorphisms coming from the stabilization map associated to <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{F}_{pq,\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{F}_{pq,\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>, one obtains smooth structures on the bundle <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{O}_{pq}^{(d)}|_{\partial^{\alpha}\widehat{V}_{pq}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{O}_{pq}^{(d)}|_{\partial^{\alpha}\widehat{V}_{pq}}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p14.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq d_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq d_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>. Using the collar structure, we extend slightly to a neighborhood of <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p14.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{\alpha}\widehat{V}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{\alpha}\widehat{V}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> inside <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p14.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p15.1" class="ltx_p">We can carry on the induction for all strata <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\alpha=pr_{1}\cdots r_{l}q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=pr_{1}\cdots r_{l}q</annotation></semantics></math>. Suppose we have constructed a smooth structure near the boundary of <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{\alpha}\widehat{V}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{\alpha}\widehat{V}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> and smooth bundle structures on <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{O}_{pq}^{(d)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{O}_{pq}^{(d)}</annotation></semantics></math> over this neighborhood. Now start with <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p15.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=d_{0}=d_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=d_{0}=d_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> and we would like to construct the smooth structure of <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p15.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{\alpha}\widehat{V}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{\alpha}\widehat{V}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> and the smooth bundle structure on <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p15.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{O}_{pq}^{(d_{0})}|_{\partial^{\alpha}\widehat{V}_{pq}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{O}_{pq}^{(d_{0})}|_{\partial^{\alpha}\widehat{V}_{pq}}</annotation></semantics></math>. First, the induction hypothesis granted a smooth structure on the product <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p15.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>. This is compatible with all the smooth structures near the boundary of <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p15.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{\alpha}\widehat{V}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{\alpha}\widehat{V}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then similar to above, one can have a smooth structure on the sum (the right hand side of (<a href="#S6.E10" title="In 6.4.2. Smoothing charts with boundary and corners ‣ 6.4. Proof of Theorem ‣ 6. Smoothing ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.10</span></a>)). Then extend to a smooth structure on <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p15.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{O}_{pq}|_{\partial^{\alpha}\widehat{V}_{pq}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{O}_{pq}|_{\partial^{\alpha}\widehat{V}_{pq}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The stabilization map then grants a smooth structure on <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p15.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{\alpha}\widehat{V}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{\alpha}\widehat{V}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> which extends the existing one near the boundary. The bundle isomorphism provides a smooth bundle structure of <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p15.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{O}_{pq}|_{\partial^{\alpha}\widehat{V}_{pq}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{O}_{pq}|_{\partial^{\alpha}\widehat{V}_{pq}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Inductively, one extends the smooth bundle structure to <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p15.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{O}_{pq}^{(d)}|_{\partial^{\alpha}\widehat{V}_{pq}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{O}_{pq}^{(d)}|_{\partial^{\alpha}\widehat{V}_{pq}}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p15.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq d_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq d_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then use the collar structure we extend the structures slightly into the interior of <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p15.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p16" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Inductive Construction III. We construct a <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant vector bundle reduction of <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\mu}\widehat{V}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\mu}\widehat{V}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> which is smooth near the boundary and is in the the isotopy class of the vector bundle reduction induced from the existing smoothings.</span> The previous construction induces a <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p16.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>-smoothing on a neighborhood <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p16.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\epsilon}(\partial\widehat{V}_{pq})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\epsilon}(\partial\widehat{V}_{pq})</annotation></semantics></math> of the boundary, using the smooth structures on bundles of the form (<a href="#S6.E11" title="In 6.4.2. Smoothing charts with boundary and corners ‣ 6.4. Proof of Theorem ‣ 6. Smoothing ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.11</span></a>) and equivariantization. Hence there is a corresponding (isotopy class) of vector bundle lift of the tangent microbundle <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p16.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\mu}\widehat{V}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\mu}\widehat{V}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> restricted to this region. From the construction we can see that</p>
<table id="S6.Ex135" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex135.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\left(N_{\epsilon}(\partial\widehat{V}_{pq})\right)\cong\left(T^{\rm vt}\widehat{V}_{pq}\oplus\widehat{\pi}_{pq}^{*}TB_{d_{pq}}\right)|_{N_{\epsilon}(\partial\widehat{V}_{pq})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≅</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>vt</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\left(N_{\epsilon}(\partial\widehat{V}_{pq})\right)\cong\left(T^{\rm vt}\widehat{V}_{pq}\oplus\widehat{\pi}_{pq}^{*}TB_{d_{pq}}\right)|_{N_{\epsilon}(\partial\widehat{V}_{pq})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p16.2" class="ltx_p">On the other hand, we know that via a fiberwise submersion on <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p16.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> one can obtain another vector bundle lift of <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p16.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\mu}\widehat{V}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\mu}\widehat{V}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> by the same vector bundle.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p17.1" class="ltx_p">We claim that these two vector bundle lifts, when restricted to their common domains, are in the same stable <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>-isotopy class of vector bundle lifts. We show why this is the case if <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> is a codimension 1 stratum. In this case, we know that</p>
<table id="S6.Ex136" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex136.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{\alpha}V_{pq}={\rm Stab}_{F_{pq,\alpha}}(V_{\alpha})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Stab</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{\alpha}V_{pq}={\rm Stab}_{F_{pq,\alpha}}(V_{\alpha})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p17.2" class="ltx_p">i.e., the boundary <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p17.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{\alpha}V_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{\alpha}V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> is a disk bundle over <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p17.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>. We can choose an (invariant) connection on <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p17.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{pq,\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{pq,\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> to induce a smooth splitting</p>
<table id="S6.Ex137" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex137.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="TF_{pq,\alpha}\cong T^{\rm vt}F_{pq,\alpha}\oplus\pi_{F_{pq,\alpha}}^{*}TV_{\alpha}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>vt</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">TF_{pq,\alpha}\cong T^{\rm vt}F_{pq,\alpha}\oplus\pi_{F_{pq,\alpha}}^{*}TV_{\alpha}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p17.3" class="ltx_p">It also induces a corresponding splitting on the microbundle level. Although the fibers of the projection onto <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p17.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\delta(\alpha)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\delta(\alpha)}</annotation></semantics></math> are no longer smooth, the microbundle version of the above splitting can still be restricted to each fiber. Then combining with the microbundle splitting of <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p17.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\mu}V_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\mu}V_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> one obtains</p>
<table id="S6.Ex138" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex138.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\mu}(\partial^{\alpha}V_{pq})\cong\pi_{F_{pq,\alpha}}^{*}(F_{pq,\alpha})_{\mu}\oplus\pi_{F_{pq,\alpha}}^{*}T_{\mu}V_{\alpha}\cong T^{\rm vt}_{\mu}(\partial^{\alpha}V_{pq})\oplus\pi^{*}T_{\mu}B_{\delta(\alpha)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi>μ</mi><mi>vt</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\mu}(\partial^{\alpha}V_{pq})\cong\pi_{F_{pq,\alpha}}^{*}(F_{pq,\alpha})_{\mu}\oplus\pi_{F_{pq,\alpha}}^{*}T_{\mu}V_{\alpha}\cong T^{\rm vt}_{\mu}(\partial^{\alpha}V_{pq})\oplus\pi^{*}T_{\mu}B_{\delta(\alpha)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p17.4" class="ltx_p">Notice that this is an equivariant fiberwise submersion of <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p17.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{\alpha}V_{pq}\to\partial^{\delta(\alpha)}B_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{\alpha}V_{pq}\to\partial^{\delta(\alpha)}B_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> (see Definition <a href="#S6.Thmthm18" title="Definition 6.18. ‣ 6.1.4. Fiberwise submersions ‣ 6.1. Preliminaries ‣ 6. Smoothing ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.18</span></a>). The collar structure can be used to extend this fiberwise submersion trivially into the collar region. Using Lemma <a href="#S6.Thmthm21" title="Lemma 6.21. ‣ 6.1.4. Fiberwise submersions ‣ 6.1. Preliminaries ‣ 6. Smoothing ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.21</span></a> one can extend it globally to <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p17.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then using the fiberwise smooth structure we obtained a vector bundle lift of <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p17.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\mu}V_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\mu}V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p18" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p18.1" class="ltx_p">On the other hand, the vector bundle lift on <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> induced from smoothing is in the same stable isotopy class of vector bundle lifts as the one from fiberwise smooth structure and microbundle splitting. Therefore, one can find another orthogonal <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>-space <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p18.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{pq}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{pq}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> such that the <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p18.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{pq}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{pq}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>-stabilization of the interior vector bundle lift of <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p18.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\mu}\widehat{V}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\mu}\widehat{V}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> is isotopic to the one from the boundary smooth structure. Also notice that one can choose a <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p18.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>-invariant continuous cut-off function on the overlap of the two domains of the vector bundle lifts to interpolate this two vector bundle lifts using the isotopy. Note that this is one salient feature of the existence of collar structures: we are free to interpolate between different data over the collar regions. Therefore, we have obtained a vector bundle lift of <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p18.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\mu}\widehat{V}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\mu}\widehat{V}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> which is smooth near the boundary.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p19" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p19.1" class="ltx_p">In general, when <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> is not a codimension 1 stratum, there are many intermediate stratum. However, one can choose connections on all the intermediate difference bundles <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\beta\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\beta\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> compatibly, utilizing Lemma <a href="#S5.Thmthm54" title="Lemma 5.54. ‣ 5.4.4. More on obstruction bundles ‣ 5.4. Global chart construction III ‣ 5. Global Kuranishi charts on Floer moduli spaces ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.54</span></a>. This still allows us to build the interior microbundle splitting which extends the boundary ones. We omit the details.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p20" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p20.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p20.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Inductive Construction IV. Smoothing for <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="pq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">pq</annotation></semantics></math>.</span> In the previous steps, we have obtained a smooth structure on a neighborhood of <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial\widehat{V}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial\widehat{V}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>, a smooth <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p20.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(n)</annotation></semantics></math>-bundle structure of <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p20.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{O}_{pq}^{(d)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{O}_{pq}^{(d)}</annotation></semantics></math> over this neighborhood, and a <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p20.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant vector bundle reduction</p>
<table id="S6.Ex139" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex139.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{pq}:(T^{\rm vt}\widehat{V}_{pq}\oplus\widehat{\pi}_{pq}^{*}B_{pq})_{\mu}\to T_{\mu}\widehat{V}_{pq}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>vt</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{pq}:(T^{\rm vt}\widehat{V}_{pq}\oplus\widehat{\pi}_{pq}^{*}B_{pq})_{\mu}\to T_{\mu}\widehat{V}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p20.2" class="ltx_p">which is smooth near <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p20.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial\widehat{V}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial\widehat{V}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then one can apply the relative version of Lashof’s <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p20.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-smoothing theorem (see Appendix <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B Relative stable equivariant smoothing ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a> and Theorem <a href="#A2.Thmthm3" title="Theorem B.3. ‣ Appendix B Relative stable equivariant smoothing ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a>) to obtain another <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p20.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>-orthogonal space <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p20.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{pq,0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{pq,0}</annotation></semantics></math> and a <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p20.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>-smoothing on <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p20.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm Int}\widehat{V_{pq}}\times{\bm{R}}_{pq,0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Int</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm Int}\widehat{V_{pq}}\times{\bm{R}}_{pq,0}</annotation></semantics></math> which coincides with the stabilization of the existing smoothing. Redefine <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p20.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> by taking direct sum with <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p20.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{R}}_{pq,0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑹</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{R}}_{pq,0}</annotation></semantics></math> and redefine <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p20.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p20.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{O}_{pq}^{(d)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{O}_{pq}^{(d)}</annotation></semantics></math> etc. Moreover, one can extend the smooth structures on <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p20.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{O}_{pq}^{(d)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{O}_{pq}^{(d)}</annotation></semantics></math> inductively to the interior of <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p20.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>. Furthermore, we extend the existing inner product on the trivial bundle <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p20.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> to the whole <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p20.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> smoothly.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p21" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p21.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, we see that we have constructed a smoothing for any K-chart <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> with energy <math id="S6.SS4.SSS2.p21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>. Furthermore, they satisfy the induction hypotheses listed at the beginning. Therefore, Theorem <a href="#S6.Thmthm31" title="Theorem 6.31. ‣ 6.3. The main theorem about smoothing ‣ 6. Smoothing ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.31</span></a> holds. ∎</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S7" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">7. </span>Constructions for PSS, SSP, and the homotopy</h2>

<div id="S7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this subsection, we discuss K-charts for PSS, SSP, and continuation type moduli spaces. The constructions here are carried out almost verbatim as the case of moduli spaces of Floer trajectories. Therefore, our main purpose here is to fix the notations, and only the key modifications are presented in detail.</p>
</div>
<section id="S7.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">7.1. </span>PSS bimodule and SSP bimodule</h3>

<section id="S7.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">7.1.1. </span>Thimbles and auxiliary moduli spaces</h4>

<div id="S7.Thmthm1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S7.Thmthm1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 7.1</span></span><span id="S7.Thmthm1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S7.Thmthm1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S7.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S7.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S7.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A <span id="S7.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">prestable PSS thimble</span> is a triple <math id="S7.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Sigma,\Sigma_{\text{PSS}},{\bf L})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mtext>PSS</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐋</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Sigma,\Sigma_{\text{PSS}},{\bf L})</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S7.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> is a genus <math id="S7.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> prestable curve with two marked points <math id="S7.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{-},z_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{-},z_{+}</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="S7.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\text{PSS}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mtext>PSS</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\text{PSS}}</annotation></semantics></math> being a distinguished horizontal irreducible component of <math id="S7.I1.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S7.I1.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf L}=({\rm L}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐋</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf L}=({\rm L}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S7.I1.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm L}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm L}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is a lateral line on each horizontal component lying between <math id="S7.I1.i1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\text{PSS}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mtext>PSS</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\text{PSS}}</annotation></semantics></math> (included!) and the marked point <math id="S7.I1.i1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{+}</annotation></semantics></math> (see Figure <a href="#S7.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ item 1 ‣ Definition 7.1. ‣ 7.1.1. Thimbles and auxiliary moduli spaces ‣ 7.1. PSS bimodule and SSP bimodule ‣ 7. Constructions for PSS, SSP, and the homotopy ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<figure id="S7.F2" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2209.08599v1/PSS.svg" id="S7.F2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="width:25.584em; height:12.877em;aspect-ratio:340/171;" width="340" height="171"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 2. </span>An example of prestable PSS thimble. The red curves are the lateral lines and the gray sphere is <math id="S7.F2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\rm PSS}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>PSS</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\rm PSS}</annotation></semantics></math> on which we interpolate between the Hamiltonian <math id="S7.F2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> and a constant function.</figcaption>
</figure></li>
<li id="S7.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S7.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A <span id="S7.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">prestable SSP thimble</span> is a triple <math id="S7.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Sigma,\Sigma_{\text{SSP}},{\bf L})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mtext>SSP</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐋</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Sigma,\Sigma_{\text{SSP}},{\bf L})</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S7.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> is a genus <math id="S7.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> prestable curve with two marked points <math id="S7.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{-},z_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{-},z_{+}</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="S7.I1.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\text{SSP}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mtext>SSP</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\text{SSP}}</annotation></semantics></math> being a distinguished horizontal irreducible component of <math id="S7.I1.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S7.I1.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf L}=({\rm L}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐋</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf L}=({\rm L}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S7.I1.i2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm L}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm L}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is a lateral line on each horizontal component lying between the marked point <math id="S7.I1.i2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{-}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.I1.i2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\text{SSP}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mtext>SSP</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\text{SSP}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS1.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS1.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">By imposing extra marked points and stability conditions, one can define the notion of stable marked PSS/SSP thimble as in Definition <a href="#S5.Thmthm12" title="Definition 5.12. ‣ 5.2.1. Moduli spaces of stable cylinders ‣ 5.2. Global chart construction I ‣ 5. Global Kuranishi charts on Floer moduli spaces ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.12</span></a>. Given an integer <math id="S7.SS1.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, the moduli space of stable PSS resp. SSP thimbles in <math id="S7.SS1.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{CP}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℂ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{CP}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is the set of equivalence classes of objects</p>
<table id="S7.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Sigma,\Sigma_{\rm PSS},{\bf L},u),\ \ \ \ \ {\rm resp.}\ \ \ \ \ (\Sigma,\Sigma_{\rm SSP},{\bf L},u)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>PSS</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐋</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.667em">,</mo><mi>resp</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo><mspace style="width:2.667em;" width="2.667em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>SSP</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐋</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Sigma,\Sigma_{\rm PSS},{\bf L},u),\ \ \ \ \ {\rm resp.}\ \ \ \ \ (\Sigma,\Sigma_{\rm SSP},{\bf L},u)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS1.SSS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S7.SS1.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Sigma,\Sigma_{\text{PSS}}/\Sigma_{\text{SSP}},{\bf L})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mtext>PSS</mtext></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mtext>SSP</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐋</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Sigma,\Sigma_{\text{PSS}}/\Sigma_{\text{SSP}},{\bf L})</annotation></semantics></math> is a prestable PSS/SSP thimble and <math id="S7.SS1.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u:\Sigma\to\mathbb{CP}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>ℂ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u:\Sigma\to\mathbb{CP}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is a stable map. We define <math id="S7.SS1.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}^{\text{PSS}}_{0,2}(d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mtext>PSS</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}^{\text{PSS}}_{0,2}(d)</annotation></semantics></math> to be the subset of moduli spaces of stable PSS thimbles such that the underlying map <math id="S7.SS1.SSS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u:\Sigma\to\mathbb{CP}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>ℂ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u:\Sigma\to\mathbb{CP}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is not contained in any hyperplane, and <math id="S7.SS1.SSS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}^{\text{SSP}}_{0,2}(d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mtext>SSP</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}^{\text{SSP}}_{0,2}(d)</annotation></semantics></math> can be defined similarly. These two moduli spaces are smooth manifolds with corners. Just as Lemma <a href="#S5.Thmthm15" title="Lemma 5.15. ‣ 5.2.3. Stable cylinders in projective spaces ‣ 5.2. Global chart construction I ‣ 5. Global Kuranishi charts on Floer moduli spaces ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.15</span></a>, the following statements hold.</p>
<ol id="S7.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S7.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S7.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The natural forgetful map <math id="S7.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}^{\text{PSS}}_{0,2}(d),{\mathcal{F}}^{\text{SSP}}_{0,2}(d)\to{\mathcal{F}}_{0,2}(d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mtext>PSS</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mtext>SSP</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}^{\text{PSS}}_{0,2}(d),{\mathcal{F}}^{\text{SSP}}_{0,2}(d)\to{\mathcal{F}}_{0,2}(d)</annotation></semantics></math> is smooth.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S7.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S7.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The evaluation maps <math id="S7.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{ev}_{\pm}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>ev</mtext><mo>±</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{ev}_{\pm}</annotation></semantics></math> at the marked points <math id="S7.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{\pm}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mo>±</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{\pm}</annotation></semantics></math> are smooth and stratified submersive onto <math id="S7.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{CP}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℂ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{CP}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S7.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S7.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">By intersecting with <math id="S7.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(d+2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(d+2)</annotation></semantics></math> generic hyperplanes in <math id="S7.I2.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{CP}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℂ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{CP}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, the moduli spaces <math id="S7.I2.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}^{\text{PSS}}_{0,2}(d),{\mathcal{F}}^{\text{SSP}}_{0,2}(d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mtext>PSS</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mtext>SSP</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}^{\text{PSS}}_{0,2}(d),{\mathcal{F}}^{\text{SSP}}_{0,2}(d)</annotation></semantics></math> are locally diffeomorphic to a real blowup of the Deligne–Mumford space <math id="S7.I2.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{0,d(d+2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{0,d(d+2)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S7.SS1.SSS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Note that we do not necessarily equip all the horizontal components of <math id="S7.SS1.SSS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Sigma,{\bf L})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐋</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Sigma,{\bf L})</annotation></semantics></math> with a lateral line, so the real blowup in (3) is different from the one in Lemma <a href="#S5.Thmthm15" title="Lemma 5.15. ‣ 5.2.3. Stable cylinders in projective spaces ‣ 5.2. Global chart construction I ‣ 5. Global Kuranishi charts on Floer moduli spaces ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.15</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS1.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS1.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The spaces <math id="S7.SS1.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}_{0,2}^{\rm PSS}(d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>PSS</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}_{0,2}^{\rm PSS}(d)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.SS1.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}_{0,2}^{\rm SSP}(d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>SSP</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}_{0,2}^{\rm SSP}(d)</annotation></semantics></math> are stratified by the same poset <math id="S7.SS1.SSS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{A}}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔸</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{A}}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> of ordered partitions of <math id="S7.SS1.SSS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> (with the same depth function, see Notation <a href="#S5.Thmthm7" title="Notation 5.7. ‣ 5.1.4. Notations ‣ 5.1. Basic notions and the main theorem about global charts ‣ 5. Global Kuranishi charts on Floer moduli spaces ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.7</span></a>). However, the geometric meaning of an element <math id="S7.SS1.SSS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=(d_{0},\ldots,d_{l})\in{\mathbb{A}}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝔸</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=(d_{0},\ldots,d_{l})\in{\mathbb{A}}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is different. For example, in the PSS case, the integer <math id="S7.SS1.SSS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the total degree of the components between <math id="S7.SS1.SSS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{-}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.SS1.SSS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\rm PSS}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>PSS</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\rm PSS}</annotation></semantics></math> (included).</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.Thmthm2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_notation">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S7.Thmthm2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Notation 7.2</span></span><span id="S7.Thmthm2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="S7.Thmthm2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S7.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S7.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S7.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S7.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p,q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p,q</annotation></semantics></math> be capped 1-periodic capped Hamiltonian orbits. Introduce the integers</p>
<table id="S7.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S7.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S7.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ d_{\bullet q}:={\mathcal{A}}_{H}(q)-C^{\rm PSS},\ " display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∙</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mi>PSS</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ d_{\bullet q}:={\mathcal{A}}_{H}(q)-C^{\rm PSS},\ </annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S7.Ex2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\ d_{p\bullet}:=C^{\rm SSP}-{\mathcal{A}}_{H}(p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∙</mo></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mi>SSP</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ d_{p\bullet}:=C^{\rm SSP}-{\mathcal{A}}_{H}(p)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.I3.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S7.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\rm PSS}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mi>PSS</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\rm PSS}</annotation></semantics></math> resp. <math id="S7.I3.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\rm SSP}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mi>SSP</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\rm SSP}</annotation></semantics></math> is the constant chosen to define the <math id="S7.I3.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm PSS}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>PSS</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm PSS}</annotation></semantics></math> resp. <math id="S7.I3.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm SSP}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>SSP</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm SSP}</annotation></semantics></math> moduli spaces (see Subsection <a href="#S4.SS3" title="4.3. PSS and SSP bimodules ‣ 4. Proof of the integral Arnold conjecture ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S7.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S7.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Extra symmetry groups</p>
<table id="S7.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{\rm PSS}_{\bullet q}:=\{g\in PU(d_{\bullet q}+1)\ |\ g([1,0,\ldots,0])=[1,0,\ldots,0]\in\mathbb{CP}^{d_{\bullet p}}\}\cong U(d_{\bullet p})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∙</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>PSS</mi></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∙</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℂ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∙</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∙</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{\rm PSS}_{\bullet q}:=\{g\in PU(d_{\bullet q}+1)\ |\ g([1,0,\ldots,0])=[1,0,\ldots,0]\in\mathbb{CP}^{d_{\bullet p}}\}\cong U(d_{\bullet p})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S7.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="G_{p\bullet}^{\rm SSP}:=\{g\in PU(d_{p\bullet}+1)\ |\ g([1,0,\ldots,0])=[1,0,\ldots,0]\in\mathbb{CP}^{d_{p\bullet}}\}\cong U(d_{p\bullet})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∙</mo></mrow><mi>SSP</mi></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∙</mo></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.667em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℂ</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∙</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∙</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{p\bullet}^{\rm SSP}:=\{g\in PU(d_{p\bullet}+1)\ |\ g([1,0,\ldots,0])=[1,0,\ldots,0]\in\mathbb{CP}^{d_{p\bullet}}\}\cong U(d_{p\bullet})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.I3.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where the isomorphisms are induced from (<a href="#S5.E3" title="In item 3 ‣ Notation 5.7. ‣ 5.1.4. Notations ‣ 5.1. Basic notions and the main theorem about global charts ‣ 5. Global Kuranishi charts on Floer moduli spaces ‣ Arnold Conjecture over Integers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3</span></a>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S7.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S7.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Homogeneous posets with partial order induced from refinement of words</p>
<table id="S7.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbb{A}}_{\bullet q}^{\rm PSS}:=\{\bullet r_{1}\cdots r_{l}q|r_{1}&lt;\cdots&lt;r_{l}&lt;p\text{ as objects in }T^{\rm Floer}\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔸</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∙</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>PSS</mi></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">∙</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mi>q</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">&lt;</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">&lt;</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>p</mi><mtext> as objects in </mtext><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>Floer</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{A}}_{\bullet q}^{\rm PSS}:=\{\bullet r_{1}\cdots r_{l}q|r_{1}&lt;\cdots&lt;r_{l}&lt;p\text{ as objects in }T^{\rm Floer}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S7.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbb{A}}_{p\bullet}^{\rm SSP}:=\{pr_{1}\cdots r_{l}\bullet|p&lt;r_{1}&lt;\cdots&lt;r_{l}\text{ as objects in }T^{\rm Floer}\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔸</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∙</mo></mrow><mi>SSP</mi></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">∙</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">&lt;</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">&lt;</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mtext> as objects in </mtext><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>Floer</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{A}}_{p\bullet}^{\rm SSP}:=\{pr_{1}\cdots r_{l}\bullet|p&lt;r_{1}&lt;\cdots&lt;r_{l}\text{ as objects in }T^{\rm Floer}\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.I3.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">with depth functions</p>
<table id="S7.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\rm depth}(\bullet r_{1}\cdots r_{l}q)=l,\ {\rm depth}(pr_{1}\cdots r_{l}\bullet)=l." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>depth</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">∙</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>l</mi><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mi>depth</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">∙</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm depth}(\bullet r_{1}\cdots r_{l}q)=l,\ {\rm depth}(pr_{1}\cdots r_{l}\bullet)=l.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.I3.i3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">The concatenation of words induces maps between homogeneous posets</p>
<table id="S7.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{A}}_{\bullet p}^{\rm PSS}\times{\mathbb{A}}^{\rm Floer}_{pq}\to{\mathbb{A}}_{\bullet q}^{\rm PSS}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔸</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∙</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mi>PSS</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>𝔸</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>Floer</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi>𝔸</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∙</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>PSS</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{A}}_{\bullet p}^{\rm PSS}\times{\mathbb{A}}^{\rm Floer}_{pq}\to{\mathbb{A}}_{\bullet q}^{\rm PSS}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S7.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbb{A}}^{\rm Floer}_{pq}\times{\mathbb{A}}_{q\bullet}^{\rm SSP}\times\to{\mathbb{A}}_{p\bullet}^{\rm SSP}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔸</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>Floer</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>𝔸</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∙</mo></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>SSP</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">×</mo><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>𝔸</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∙</mo></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>SSP</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{A}}^{\rm Floer}_{pq}\times{\mathbb{A}}_{q\bullet}^{\rm SSP}\times\to{\mathbb{A}}_{p\bullet}^{\rm SSP}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.I3.i3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">There are natural maps of posets</p>
<table id="S7.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
